{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals","id":1035738,"title":"Mages are nothing but prey to other Supernaturals?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-01-21T10:13:36-08:00","id":1035738,"title":"Mages are nothing but prey to other Supernaturals?","content":"So this came up in a thread on another forum and I figured I'd post this here to get some input from people more familiar with Mage than I am (I have most of the books, but have never actually gotten to play a Mage game). So I'm looking for thoughts on the following quote:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages should never take it for granted that they can take on other supernatural creatures. They are human and, while they can temporarily modify themselves to become superhuman, do not have any innate supernatural capabilities. They are prey, not predators, and should never assume that they are anything but prey when they deal with other supernatural creatures. They should never get into fights with other supernatural creatures without proper preparation, should always avoid unnecessary fights with other supernatural creatures whenever possible, and should never fight fair against other supernatural creatures when they have to fight. </div> </div> </div>This sounds incredibly incorrect to me, but being less familiar with the system I can't necessarily point out why. I do agree Mages are far, far better with preparation (sometimes unbeatable). But to say they &quot;should never assume that they are anything but prey when they deal with other supernatural creatures&quot;?<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm curious to get the Mage forum's perspective.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T10:29:39-08:00","id":1035749,"title":"","content":"For the most part a Mage will assume that they are the top of the food chain though this is largely due to hubris. And with the proper preparation they probably are. They should not seek out combat with other supernaturals, or really anything else for that matter unprepared since they are human and therefore are frail compared to the other creatures who can soak lethal damage. This is also because most Mage are not violent predators. There are a few factions such as Akashics that are more equipped for violence but still they are not the equal to a werewolf on the spur of the moment. Again, if prepared its a whole nother story.<br /> <br /> Also, why should a Mage expose himself to dangerous combat when they can, with the right spheres sit in safety and dispatch their enemies. The Vampire elder does the same thing but through minions of lesser vampires and ghouls instead or magick. Does this make the vampire a lesser form of combatant?<br /> <br /> I seriously doubt that a werewolf would consider that an unseen Mage using Correspondence and Spirit to blast him with fire and lightning wherever he trys to hide (even through the Umbra) as &quot;prey&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:06:23-08:00","id":1035761,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals#post1035738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this came up in a thread on another forum and I figured I'd post this here to get some input from people more familiar with Mage than I am (I have most of the books, but have never actually gotten to play a Mage game). So I'm looking for thoughts on the following quote:<br /> <br /> <br /> This sounds incredibly incorrect to me, but being less familiar with the system I can't necessarily point out why. I do agree Mages are far, far better with preparation (sometimes unbeatable). But to say they &amp;quot;should never assume that they are anything but prey when they deal with other supernatural creatures&amp;quot;?<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm curious to get the Mage forum's perspective.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>If my Etherite archmage with Arete 5 and, say, Spirit 5, Matter 5, Prime 5, Entropy 5, Forces 5, Life 4, Mind 4, Time 4 and Correspondence 3 goes to the supermarket, but forgot all his weird toys that he uses as foci and forgot his Prime enchanted Exo-Squeleton that allows him to walk in the fires of hell and squash armies of demons, he better not bump on his way on that neonate vampire that made him laugh when vowed to kill him and he let live because those threaths amuzed the mighty Mage.<br /> <br /> Our good archmage so full of Hubris will die at the hands of the neonate in the first round.<br /> <br /> Now, when said archmage is controlling his mighty Ethership, a Starship Class Omega that rivals the Qui La Machine of the Void Engeneers (and that has so many permanent Effects on the ship that the thing makes reality warp around it), he can vaporize entirely packs of Gurahls or Mokole simply by pressing one buttom... Or his &quot;Iron Man&quot; battlesuit (and Talisman full of bullshit permanent effects) makes him a good match for many metuselahs...<br /> <br /> But a naked Mage, is a lot less likely to win.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:18:12-08:00","id":1035764,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035761#post1035761\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If my Etherite archmage with Arete 5 and, say, Spirit 5, Matter 5, Prime 5, Entropy 5, Forces 5, Life 4, Mind 4, Time 4 and Correspondence 3 goes to the supermarket, but forgot all his weird toys that he uses as foci and forgot his Prime enchanted Exo-Squeleton that allows him to walk in the fires of hell and squash armies of demons, he better not bump on his way on that neonate vampire that made him laugh when vowed to kill him and he let live because those threaths amuzed the mighty Mage.<br /> <br /> Our good archmage so full of Hubris will die at the hands of the neonate in the first round..</div> </div> </div> </div>On the other hand with a non-technomancer with those stats who can yell Enochian to turn the vampire into a vam-pyre (get it? Get it?), or even has dropped their first two instruments at that point and one of them happens to be the one they used to create fire..things look quite different.<br /> <br /> As usual with Mage, it hightly depends on the specific mage, the specific situation, the running effects, paradigm, how much time the Mage needs to achieve their results, who the enemies are, if the Mage can handle the kind of enemies well or actually has absolutely no method to...it depends, really, on a lot of subjective things, with the specific mage as the subject.<br /> <br /> Both, Karlgust and Tuch are quite correct, as is my example, but that <i>exactly shows why that post from the other forum is way, way too generalizing and a crude blanket statement</i>. There are Mages that are anything but prey.<br /> <br /> One thing is always true though: A Mage without any running effects, prepared wonders, permenant changes or magic at hand is just that - a human. When you strip everything away, they are just a human, most had a human upbringing and life before their awakening, and when they are young they all mostly still also think like normal humans, broadened view of reality or not.<br /> <br /> And it highly depends on a lot of variables if a Mage is stripped of everything or, as a matter of fact, is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-21-2017, 02:20 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:27:59-08:00","id":1035768,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> Your etherite archmage with Arete 5 has already abandoned two of his foci and can just will miracles into existence.<br /> <br /> But really, that's why being a hermetic and using enochian spells as a focus is so good. You are never going to leave your tongue in your other trousers.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a> Mages are tough. Very, very tough, especially if rules for ritual magic are being used. A chargen Life mage can easily run around with 5 in all physical and mental attributes and ability to soak Aggravate damage, all at a cost of spending a few days each month doing rituals. If said mage is an akashic, then the average ancilla Gangrel and his droogs who decide to bully said akashic will leave the fight as an artistic interpretation of a vampire centipede.<br /> <br /> But of course, that doesn't mean Mages are unbeatable. You still need to maintain those rituals so there are times when you are a vanilla mortal. Mind control works perfectly fine against most mages (though the older the mage the more likely he's to have Mind 1), and vampires have a shitton of mind control. Overwhelming alpha strike also works perfectly fine on mages. Buy ten AKs, unload full auto bursts in a drive-by.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:44:34-08:00","id":1035772,"title":"","content":"You'll hardly find a Mage in such situations thou... And the more powerful, the less likely. That m\u00e1ster Etherite, for example, even naked would have A LOT of permanent effects... His own body would be a relic (a living being with permanent magikal effects), since he knows every Sphere AND Time above 4 and Entropy above 3, his eyes would have nano cibernetical modifications, that allows him to see in infra red, ultra violet, sound waves sonar (like Batman in the Dark Knight), to detect any life pattern with hostile intencions and to detect any magick around, or any hostile spirit, and to know how far away that &quot;hostile presence is&quot;... Plus, that would auto activate at any moment that he could be endangered (every level 1 allows him to see... Well, basically, anything. If he asks, the ST describes to him - at details). That &quot;spider sense&quot; can detect ANY danger to him. Since he also has Entropy, that means this effect will always get on whenever he could be endangered in the near future.<br /> This Etherite don't need to do nothing to have that; it's a permanent boon he his from his ciborg eyes (or quantum brain chip, or whatever)... That effect is always on BY DEFAULT because it is a &quot;talisman&quot;, a &quot;magikal&quot; item with a permanent always on effect.<br /> That means he can never be surprised.<br /> Never.<br /> Not only that, he will always know what's comming for him... Vampire, Werebeast, Mage... Hell, it's possible that by the time his ambushers get to him, he would know them better than themselves<br /> <br /> But hold on, because thats only what he would have with only the level 1 of Spheres.<br /> <br /> One of the things that make Mages ridiculously power, is the fact that they can make items with permanent effects. It doesn't matter that I only have 3 Arete dices, if Control gave me one of their highly experimental anti-matter portable blaster cannons that have a permanent 10 successes Forces 5 nuclear Ray, it will ALWAYS cause 21 aggravated damage on enemies.<br /> <br /> I may need a full day to make my luck ritual do give me more dices in one skill; but if I put that effect on my rabbit tail, I'll have that effect always on on me (and I don't take penalties for multiple effects). Besides, my Arete pool of 3 may grante only 2 successes at most of the best situations, buy I can accumulate 10 successes on my luck charm (and, once again, it will be always on).<br /> <br /> That's one of the reason that technocrats are so ridiculously overpowered... They simply use A LOT of magikal items... First of all, they have ridiculous amounts of Primium ON EVERYTHING. Secondly, a typical Hit Mark will have dozens of perm effects.<br /> <br /> Besides, if you piss the Etherite Archmage, he won't be the one knocking on your door. He will be sending his killer assassin automatons that can chew bubble gun while ripping Nexus Crawlers appart and that have 100 perm effects on them and a huge Prime battery with 50 quintessence points each (or even more, when I were ST on a Order of Reason/Technocracy game where my PC where part of Control, one of my PCs, a gabrielite, made a giant turtle with 5.000 thousands of periapts on it - quintessence batteries, so that thing could storage 250.000 quintessence points... He made the turtle into a Dimensional Traveler, and the creature had to feed on entire spiritual realms to fully recharge after spending some like half of it - that wasn't a problem thou. <br /> Another creation where a satelite with a might Ion cannon. Every 10 meters (roughly 10 yards) of lenght of the cannon, he placed a special eletromagnetic propelent ring. The Cannon, with 1 km (half a mile I guess), had 100 of those magnetic rings.<br /> Each one of them were enchanted with 10 aggravated damage. Each pulse of that thing consumed 100 quintessence (it needed A LOT of periapts - Tass bateries), but caused ONE THOUSAND AGGRAVETED damage by use<br /> <br /> EDIT: I forgot to say it were 1.000 damage per round in an 50 yards area at a high cost of 100 quintessence/round... Which wasn't really a problem, given their vast resources","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-21-2017, 03:39 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T11:49:32-08:00","id":1035773,"title":"","content":"At 3ed, you just start being able to abandon foci from Arete 6 and above... I don't know in M20 if that still stands, correct me if it isn't.<br /> <br /> Even so, at least for teachies, the ability to abandon foci were left at ST decision.<br /> <br /> Oh well, better toys, worse abilities... That's life...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:02:54-08:00","id":1035777,"title":"","content":"Maintaining permanent effects is not without its downsides, as you get permanent paradox for each effect you have.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:15:55-08:00","id":1035782,"title":"","content":"Without any spells up, mages are effectively just mortal. Mages can certainly cast spells to do things, but this can often take time and requires some level of preparedness. Further, spell casting can often carry the risk of Paradox with it and not every mage can &quot;hang&quot; spells to let them come into effect later, and many don't want to suffer the Paradox from getting permanent spells.<br /> <br /> Vampires, werewolves and such don't really have to worry about that quite as much, are often far more free to use their supernatural abilities without blowback, and their physical bodies are often a heck of a lot stronger than a mage's. Every Vampire (thanks to their ability to spend blood to increase their natural Attributes) and Werewolf (thanks to their shapeshifting) are going to be pretty damn powerful in a fight, straight out of the box.<br /> <br /> In contrast Mages are often &quot;Theoretical Schrodinger Boxes&quot; - in <i>theory</i> a Mage can do anything and everything. In reality though, most mages don't have every Sphere at 5 and are going to be rather limited in how they can react and respond to a given opponent. One mage might be able to instantly destroy any Vampire, but most mages will probably find themselves in a bit of trouble if a Vampire suddenly decided to jump them in a dark alleyway. <br /> <br /> As a result, in general, most mages probably are going to be &quot;prey&quot; to Vampires and Werewolves, with the understand that most Vampires and Werewolves are going to be prey to Archmages.<br /> <br /> I think the <i>real</i> prey splat in the WoD wasn't Mages but rather Changelings, who had a lot of issues in tangling with other splats.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:26:57-08:00","id":1035788,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035782#post1035782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In reality though, most mages don't have every Sphere at 5 and are going to be rather limited in how they can react and respond to a given opponent. One mage might be able to instantly destroy any Vampire, but most mages will probably find themselves in a bit of trouble if a Vampire suddenly decided to jump them in a dark alleyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>I have to disagree with this. A mage with one of the real spheres (i.e. Forces, Life or Matter) or Entropy has a virtually limitless toolbox even at level 3. Forces and Matter (and Life) cover literally everything that actually exists. The possibilities are endless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:36:54-08:00","id":1035793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035777#post1035777\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maintaining permanent effects is not without its downsides, as you get permanent paradox for each effect you have.</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that just for VULGAR effects? Like having attributes bellow 5 or making your harder to soak aggravated damage... I think that keeping a mind shield or &quot;luck aura&quot; doesn't generate that<br /> <br /> Besides, you can circumvent that by placing those effects on wondrous creations... Artifacts, amulets, talismans, periapts, relics... All created using Prime. Those items can even &quot;soak&quot; or mitigate the paradox, and some rules at Forged at Dragon's Fire are very powerful options<br /> <br /> Oh yes, you can also have familiars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:43:05-08:00","id":1035796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035788#post1035788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree with this. A mage with one of the real spheres (i.e. Forces, Life or Matter) or Entropy has a virtually limitless toolbox even at level 3. Forces and Matter (and Life) cover literally everything that actually exists. The possibilities are endless.</div> </div> </div> </div>You have a lot of options, but at the same time you're still going to have a hard time battling something like a werewolf or a vampire. In general, dealing with a supernatural threat is not easy even for many mages. For example, to directly affect a werewolf with magic you generally need to both Life and Spirit (and possibly Prime too). A Matter mage or Life Mage or Forces mage could inflict some damage on a werewolf (possibly aggravated if the mage is a Matter mage who conjures something silver) but werewolves are pretty damn good at healing damage.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a very powerful mage would simply rip the werewolf's soul of his body and call it a day. When you're looking at the capabilities of high end Mages and low end Mages you're dealing with two very, very different power levels.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/741-anubisxy","name":"AnubisXy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar741_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:45:33-08:00","id":1035799,"title":"","content":"I think permanent effects, vulgar or not, give paradox. But I could be wrong and can't be bothered to check.<br /> <br /> Crafting wonders requires Prime 4 + sphere from which you want to draw the effect, so very few mages are capable of that. It's entirely possible that in the town of adventure <i>no one</i> is capable of that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:51:39-08:00","id":1035800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035768#post1035768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> But really, that's why being a hermetic and using enochian spells as a focus is so good. You are never going to leave your tongue in your other trousers.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not actually a certainty, given the WoD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T12:57:28-08:00","id":1035802,"title":"","content":"Well, in WtA, Possessed have access to a Power called Homogeneity that cancels all effects in five yards on a Manipulation plus Occult roll (only opposable by the target's Willpower if the target understands what the Possessed is trying to do). You can recast the effect, but you are stripped until you can recast the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:03:59-08:00","id":1035804,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AnubisXy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035796#post1035796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You have a lot of options, but at the same time you're still going to have a hard time battling something like a werewolf or a vampire. In general, dealing with a supernatural threat is not easy even for many mages. For example, to directly affect a werewolf with magic you generally need to both Life and Spirit (and possibly Prime too). A Matter mage or Life Mage or Forces mage could inflict some damage on a werewolf (possibly aggravated if the mage is a Matter mage who conjures something silver) but werewolves are pretty damn good at healing damage.<br /> <br /> Meanwhile a very powerful mage would simply rip the werewolf's soul of his body and call it a day. When you're looking at the capabilities of high end Mages and low end Mages you're dealing with two very, very different power levels.</div> </div> </div> </div>A Matter mage can burry the werewolf neck deep into asphalt and walk away, or turn air into white phosphorus, or walk away through the nearest wall. A Forces mage can fly away and there's fuck all a werewolf can do about it. Unless of course you define victory exclusively as murderizing the opponent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:14:43-08:00","id":1035805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035788#post1035788\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have to disagree with this. A mage with one of the real spheres (i.e. Forces, Life or Matter) or Entropy has a virtually limitless toolbox even at level 3. Forces and Matter (and Life) cover literally everything that actually exists. The possibilities are endless.</div> </div> </div> </div>The &quot;problem&quot; about mages isn't really that the mechanics restricts them too much. Actually, it's the other way around... And sometimes the ST will just have to say &quot;that's too much dude&quot;. A Mage's power is only limited by the player creativity and/or ST desired level of his campagn.<br /> <br /> So, if you wanna make Mages as enemies against your Vampires or Garou PC, just keep a Basic understand of what Mages can do, and use that as guidelines for narrativa purposes - unless you really want the players to face a guy that can conjure an Ion Cannon pulse from his satelity-talisman on space that can do 1.000 aggr damage in an area of a house.<br /> <br /> So, some ideas for balancing things up:<br /> <br /> Max ritual success: I never saw that rule before except here in the f\u00f3rum (is that some new feature o M20?), but I like it (it doesn't work when making magikal items thou, just ignore it when making them and use Forged on Dragon's Fire instead for the CREATION of the item only, but keep it for the level of successes the item can have) Your maximum success equals Arete + Willpower.<br /> That's good, no &quot;200 successes to open the Abyss and release all demons) stuff.<br /> Still, that means that initial chars will have a Max of 8... Which is A LOT, but not borderline insane.<br /> <br /> Narrativa: don't just say &quot;ok, how much tass do you have? 50? Ressonance? Entropic? Ok, roll the dice... Fail, too bad, try again... Do you have another 50 Tass.. Oh, you do have? Ok, one more go... Fine, 7 rounds to make the item... Ok, your spectral scythe that steal corpus from wraiths and store as quintessence with entropic ressonance is done&quot;... No. Go away from mechanics a little... The more unusual the thing, the harder to come buy... Make the PC having to find an Eutanathoi to teach him how to go to the Underworld, make him having to gather corpus from Specters (now, that's a challenge), make him have to WASTE a good deal of that just so he can study the substance enough to be able to deal with it...<br /> There is a reason after all that some effects are know only by a few... Spirit 3 allows a Mage to enter the Umbra... That also includes crossing the Shroud to the lands of the dead. So, why only the Eutanathoi know how to get there amongst the Traditions? Why only the Technocracy and the Sons of Ether know how to make Primium? Why only the Akashics know the Dim Mak?<br /> <br /> Now, even with all that, I'll just give two simple effects that make it a lot harder to make mages &quot;easy prey&quot;, even if they are initial chars. Both simple level 1 effects, and anyone could make them 2 &quot;always on&quot; at a rather easy cost<br /> <br /> Danger Sense (Entropy 1) - Exactly as the name says; if there is immediate Danger, you'll get that &quot;spider sense&quot;. You may not know what it is, but you know that IT IS.<br /> With a HUGE pool of 8 (!!!) successes on this staying &quot; always on&quot;, that's a great thing for a begginer. Spend some 3 successes for duration and you're fine with a always on 5 hints of danger... Note that that sense, althouth not allowing you to see past ilusions or invisibilities like obfuscation, will still bell anyway<br /> <br /> Mind Shield (Mind 1) - 8 successes, minus 3 for duration, gives you an always on mental defense of 5 dots against ilusions, obfuscation, mind readings, domination, mental attacks, etc. Any mental intrusion will need at least 6 successes to bypass that, at which point the Mage can resist with his Willpower (that is never less than 5) if the power allows it. Also note that, as soon as anyone tries to get into the Mages head, he will notice the intrusion<br /> <br /> Now, those are two MIGTHY defenses for initial chars","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:16:15-08:00","id":1035807,"title":"","content":"I think that Prey may be pushing it too far. Sure, even Archmages are squishy without prep compared to a neonate vampire.<br /> But compared to the Joe Average that vampires are acustomed to call prey?<br /> <br /> A &quot;really&quot; powerful Mage it's no more &quot;prey&quot; than an Imbued Hunter is.<br /> Sure, he can't soak aggravated, but he can most likely deliver it, and also may be able to resist some minor powers that target the mind, the soul, or are magical in nature, like the Delirium, Dominate or Thaumaturgy (Arete 5+ isn't so pathetic as a Countermagick soak as to be called &quot;no defense&quot;, albeit it's not too hard to overcome. Heck, I would argue that most neonates are less resistent to Dominate than that) . Hunters are better resisting mental/spiritual stuff, but can't always resist magic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:22:07-08:00","id":1035810,"title":"","content":"Some mages are easy prey for some supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> Some mages are never unprepared. Some are invulnerable to physical attacks. Some mages can load from a savegame/ respawn in their sanctum.<br /> Some stay safely in a pocket universe and co-locate from there, risking only one HL if the copy gets killed.<br /> <br /> Permanent Paradox (Permadox) is warranted if:<br /> <br /> 1. You go over human ratings in traits. (Wether temporally or permanent)<br /> <br /> 2. You fused a Wonder with yourself.<br /> <br /> 3. From a very strong Backlash.<br /> <br /> 4. You magickally develop unnatural qualities (scales, wings, gills, etc.)<br /> <br /> Permanent is a misnomer here. If you drop the effect granting you wings then the Permadox dissapears. Likewise with inhuman traits and fused wonders. Permadox from a Backlash is another story, but you can get rid of that, too(it is not so easy however).<br /> <br /> Another thing is the low possibility to interact with a mage in a meaningful way.<br /> They are rare, they can manipulate chance to be less in danger of random encounters, they are Arcane, they are only human (which is a benefit because you can blend in easily).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:23:32-08:00","id":1035811,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035799#post1035799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think permanent effects, vulgar or not, give paradox. But I could be wrong and can't be bothered to check.<br /> <br /> Crafting wonders requires Prime 4 + sphere from which you want to draw the effect, so very few mages are capable of that. It's entirely possible that in the town of adventure <i>no one</i> is capable of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yes, thats why I side with the Union. We NEVER run out of the cool toys.<br /> <br /> That's the good thing about working with organized, united people that share a same goal and help each other and that have places like Autochtonia and Mecha I and II to keep putting all sorts of hypertech stuff in your lap.<br /> <br /> Not to mention the fat pay checks that are always religiously payed without delay, courtesy of the Syndicate.<br /> <br /> Sucks being you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:32:31-08:00","id":1035814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035810#post1035810\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some mages are easy prey for some supernatural creatures.<br /> <br /> Some mages are never unprepared. Some are invulnerable to physical attacks. Some mages can load from a savegame/ respawn in their sanctum.<br /> Some stay safely in a pocket universe and co-locate from there, risking only one HL if the copy gets killed.<br /> <br /> Permanent Paradox (Permadox) is warranted if:<br /> <br /> 1. You go over human ratings in traits. (Wether temporally or permanent)<br /> <br /> 2. You fused a Wonder with yourself.<br /> <br /> 3. From a very strong Backlash.<br /> <br /> 4. You magickally develop unnatural qualities (scales, wings, gills, etc.)<br /> <br /> Permanent is a misnomer here. If you drop the effect granting you wings then the Permadox dissapears. Likewise with inhuman traits and fused wonders. Permadox from a Backlash is another story, but you can get rid of that, too(it is not so easy however).<br /> <br /> Another thing is the low possibility to interact with a mage in a meaningful way.<br /> They are rare, they can manipulate chance to be less in danger of random encounters, they are Arcane, they are only human (which is a benefit because you can blend in easily).</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks nonsense... So, the only real downside for most permanent effects will be the increase in difficult for several effects on at the same time.<br /> <br /> Still, I don't think it would be a bad idea to have a ton of permanent effects at the cost of not being able to cast any effect outside your sanctum... Depending on the effects, even a lot of Permadox is acceptable, if you can accept to trade your ability of &quot;casting on the go&quot; for a series of static superpowers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:38:58-08:00","id":1035817,"title":"","content":"I'm not backing up the &quot;prey&quot; bit, but there are some things to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035804#post1035804\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A Matter mage can burry the werewolf neck deep into asphalt and walk away</div> </div> </div> </div>Burrow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , or turn air into white phosphorus </div> </div> </div>That would be vulgar as hell, so a mage can't take success as a given, even if they're insane enough to want to do it. Even if you do succeed, Willie Peter is a substance that invites a lot of official attention, what with it being a less direct health hazard as well as a fire hazard and all; if you activate it too close to yourself, you'll need Life to heal your burns and avoid developing phossy jaw, and another Matter effect to dispose of the WP so that it doesn't contaminate the scene, or anyone at it. Assuming that you're able to get away, of course, and not in the custody of authorities who really want to know where you got all of that undocumented WP, which, if used for any purpose other than simply making smoke, is considered a chemical weapon.<br /> <br /> Garou, meanwhile, can use Master of Fire, a starting Gift native to the most populous splats of the monster type, to turn the damage bashing, and being half spirit presumably means that they don't have to worry about developing phossy jaw after the fact. Solomonds and Chu-jung kamuii in wani form could probably outright bathe in it with no ill effects, and go so far as to take control of it and set it back on the mage It would definitely take care of vampires, but then, again, you'd have to either be ignorant of the full ramifications of using WP or else crazy to do it. Unlike a nexus crawler, a mage generally has to face the music for their wanton disruptions of reality.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> , or walk away through the nearest wall. </div> </div> </div>OH YEAH!<br /> <br /> Wait, you said quietly. Never mind.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Forces mage can fly away and there's fuck all a werewolf can do about it. Unless of course you define victory exclusively as murderizing the opponent. </div> </div> </div>Spirit of the Bird. The werewolf can then play chicken with the mage, testing who's willing to fly into an open area to avoid an obstacle first. Changelings, Hungry Dead, and Shinma can also take to the skies after a flying mage, to say nothing of Fera who are either of flight-capable animals or otherwise have some way to gain said capability, which is broad enough to include most of them. Yes, even the Rokea, and they'll swim through the air after you as a giant shark as a result of how the Gift works.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T13:57:18-08:00","id":1035823,"title":"","content":"Or a Possessed can just turn off all of a Mage's magical effects for a few turns when they get to 100'. Oh, what can a Mage do when their Spheres are turned off for the three turns it takes for them to fall to their deaths? Nothing except flap their arms and hope that they remembered to pay their life insurance...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:19:09-08:00","id":1035830,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035817#post1035817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would be vulgar as hell, so a mage can't take success as a given, even if they're insane enough to want to do it. Even if you do succeed, Willie Peter is a substance that invites a lot of official attention, what with it being a less direct health hazard as well as a fire hazard and all; if you activate it too close to yourself, you'll need Life to heal your burns and avoid developing phossy jaw, and another Matter effect to dispose of the WP so that it doesn't contaminate the scene, or anyone at it. Assuming that you're able to get away, of course, and not in the custody of authorities who really want to know where you got all of that undocumented WP, which, if used for any purpose other than simply making smoke, is considered a chemical weapon.<br /> <br /> Garou, meanwhile, can use Master of Fire, a starting Gift native to the most populous splats of the monster type, to turn the damage bashing, and being half spirit presumably means that they don't have to worry about developing phossy jaw after the fact. Solomonds and Chu-jung kamuii in wani form could probably outright bathe in it with no ill effects, and go so far as to take control of it and set it back on the mage It would definitely take care of vampires, but then, again, you'd have to either be ignorant of the full ramifications of using WP or else crazy to do it. Unlike a nexus crawler, a mage generally has to face the music for their wanton disruptions of reality.</div> </div> </div> </div>White Phosphorous in its gaseous form ignites at 34 celcius. If it's too cold outside for that then you can turn air into any other gas that ignites at a lower temperature of which wikipedia has a handy list. As for the rest of the stuff - I have no idea what you are talking about. You don't &quot;possess&quot; white phosporus in any meaningful capacity. I'm literally talking about transforming the air around a werewolf and letting him burn. Or turn the air into one of the many, many poisonous gases like sarin, VX, or just a very annoying cloud of bear mace. And then leave because you are a mage and you have no pesky morality scale to deal with.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:22:51-08:00","id":1035835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035823#post1035823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a Possessed can just turn off all of a Mage's magical effects for a few turns when they get to 100'. Oh, what can a Mage do when their Spheres are turned off for the three turns it takes for them to fall to their deaths? Nothing except flap their arms and hope that they remembered to pay their life insurance...</div> </div> </div> </div>Obscure werewolf bullshit is obscure. Expecting to see non-Mage enemies played by non-Mage rules in a Mage game is unreasonable.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:27:49-08:00","id":1035837,"title":"","content":"Well, if you are within fifty yards of the Werewolf (who may be immune to sarin gas with the Rank 1 Resist Toxin Gift), I would suggest making a new character because your old one is dying from trace exposure of enough sarin gas to kill a Werewolf in Crinos form.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:50:54-08:00","id":1035844,"title":"","content":"Yes, Homogeneity is so obscure it's in the most recent core book for Werewolf! Wait..<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035830#post1035830\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">White Phosphorous in its gaseous form ignites at 34 celcius. If it's too cold outside for that then you can turn air into any other gas that ignites at a lower temperature of which wikipedia has a handy list. As for the rest of the stuff - I have no idea what you are talking about. You don't &quot;possess&quot; white phosporus in any meaningful capacity. I'm literally talking about transforming the air around a werewolf and letting him burn. Or turn the air into one of the many, many poisonous gases like sarin, VX, or just a very annoying cloud of bear mace. And then leave because you are a mage and you have no pesky morality scale to deal with.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you not know what WP's other effects, aside from fire? It creates huge amounts of smoke and it's quite noticeable if you use it anywhere where anyone can see it. It also causes necrosis of bone tissue in the jaw due to toxic interactions with phosphate metabolism. Even if you just spontaneously make it with magick, it will still be very noticeable, and anyone fleeing the site (which the hypothetical mage won't be able to do coincidentally without having some kind of residue on them, given that Garou and other monsters will be on you very up close and very quickly and combustion will violently send the products of the reaction everywhere) will probably be wanted for questioning, if seen. Afterwards, the area that the mage doused in WP will be contaminated with it, just so that you could inflict a paltry amount of bashing damage on a werewolf (Master of Fire changes fire to bashing for the scene; it is also a first rank homid Gift, so at least 2/3 of all Garou on the planet will at least have the option of picking it up whenever they have a spare moment to talk to an appropriate spirit).<br /> <br /> Nerve gas is even worse of an idea because it's even more likely to catch attention after the fact, on account of how it will diffuse even faster through the air and is even more immediately lethal... but less so for werewolves, who can use Resist Toxin to knock it down and easily reduce the damage down to survivable levels even without it. If a mage is just blithely creating VX or sarin without a second thought, they'll probably end up apprehended by magickally-inclined authorities in no time flat, because there are few threats to the sort of safe and orderly existence that the Technocracy wants to produce than nerve gas anywhere near a populated, wealthy area. Bear mace would be far more sensible choice, but keep in mind that Resist Toxin can easily deal with capsaicins. As can being a non-mammalian shapeshifter (only mammals are affected by capsaicins, so Ananasi, Corax, Mokole, Nagah, and Rokea would shrug off the effects in non-human forms).<br /> <br /> Quite frankly, I'm shaking my head that the alleged boundless creativity of Mage is being sent straight for the spontaneous appearance of uncommon and highly controlled nerve agents and Willie Peter when they could just locate a grain silo and tweak it a bit within coincidental paramters so that it creates a thermobaric explosion, or even just buying some sacks of flour and spreading them around to the same effect. Of course, the fire would still be much less effective against werewolves than it would be against vampires. Post-Revised is a bitch for pyromaniacs who want to pursue Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:55:38-08:00","id":1035846,"title":"","content":"The mage may have a less dangerous form of killing a Werewolf. Like a rote to launch a silver stake to the werewolf with brutal Force (Prime 2, Matter 2, Forces 3, I think), which a strong mage can do, and would be much like fireballing a vampire (with similar chances to fail). Or a &quot;bullet to silver&quot; rote.<br /> <br /> But relative ways of sove a situation are relative.<br /> <br /> Now:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Mages should never take it for granted that they can take on other supernatural creatures. They are human and, while they can temporarily modify themselves to become superhuman, do not have any innate supernatural capabilities. They are prey, not predators, and should never assume that they are anything but prey when they deal with other supernatural creatures. They should never get into fights with other supernatural creatures without proper preparation, should always avoid unnecessary fights with other supernatural creatures whenever possible, and should never fight fair against other supernatural creatures when they have to fight. </div> </div> </div>I would suggest to define Prey in this context.<br /> Why would mages be Prey to other supernaturals?, because they can't likely survive agains't a Werewolf?<br /> What isn't Prey?.<br /> Why mages should never take it for granted that they can take on Hunters or Changelings?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-21-2017, 05:58 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T14:57:07-08:00","id":1035847,"title":"","content":"People are forgetting about pattern leakage (unless that's not a thing in M20). But might I suggest that this kind of discussion inevitably becomes dumb and embarrassing and pointless?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:02:17-08:00","id":1035852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035847#post1035847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">People are forgetting about pattern leakage (unless that's not a thing in M20). But might I suggest that this kind of discussion inevitably becomes dumb and embarrassing and pointless?</div> </div> </div> </div>It most certainly does. I presented a few examples of what a mage might do when confronted by an enemy in an alley, and everyone felt the need to build a white room scenario where a werewolf would win the white room fight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:04:58-08:00","id":1035854,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">It most certainly does. I presented a few examples of what a mage might do when confronted by an enemy in an alley, and everyone felt the need to build a white room scenario where a werewolf would win the white room fight.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep. That happens. Nevermind that most vampires would fall just as easily in those situations.<br /> That's why I say that we should define exactly what is and isn't <i>prey</i> here.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-21-2017, 06:07 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:05:49-08:00","id":1035855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035844#post1035844\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Quite frankly, I'm shaking my head that the alleged boundless creativity of Mage is being sent straight for the spontaneous appearance of uncommon and highly controlled nerve agents and Willie Peter when they could just locate a grain silo and tweak it a bit within coincidental paramters so that it creates a thermobaric explosion, or even just buying some sacks of flour and spreading them around to the same effect. Of course, the fire would still be much less effective against werewolves than it would be against vampires. Post-Revised is a bitch for pyromaniacs who want to pursue Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>A grain silo. That is conveniently located in the same dark alley where you get jumped by a werewolf. If that's the case then just pull out a light machine gun you've loaded with silver bullets and shoot the sunovabich.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T15:53:56-08:00","id":1035874,"title":"","content":"Well, there are problems with creating silver bullets from lead bullets in the barrel of a LMG (and does the character have the Heavy Weapons Ability?). Silver possesses a lower density than lead, so the same mass will be a larger bullet, which will burst the gun when fired because the gases from the propellant cannot escape (turning lead bullets into silver bullets is Matter 2/Correspondence 1, turning lead bullets into useful silver bullets is Matter 4/Correspondence 1 to turn the excess silver into air). Of course, I would not tell my players that unless they possessed the right Abilities (Firearms 3+, Science 1+, or Technology 3+ would be sufficient).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-21-2017, 06:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:03:22-08:00","id":1035880,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> You missed the joke.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:32:13-08:00","id":1035888,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035768#post1035768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> Your etherite archmage with Arete 5 has already abandoned two of his foci and can just will miracles into existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aaaactualy no <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Technomancers get to do that starting at Arete 6, alas, even in M20. The flipside of having a paradigm that makes coincidental magicks much easier, with way less suspicious tools.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035799#post1035799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think permanent effects, vulgar or not, give paradox. But I could be wrong and can't be bothered to check.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nah, they do not. The usual rule of vulgarity applies.<br /> <br /> <br /> ...<br /> EDIT:<br /> <br /> ...also I see the thread once more turned into a 'Splat vs Splat' back and forth. Sigh.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-21-2017, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:44:04-08:00","id":1035889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Silver possesses a lower density than lead, so the same mass will be a larger bullet, which will burst the gun when fired because the gases from the propellant cannot escape (turning lead bullets into silver bullets is Matter 2/Correspondence 1, turning lead bullets into useful silver bullets is Matter 4/Correspondence 1 to turn the excess silver into air)</div> </div> </div> </div>Since Matter 2-3 allows to alter the properties, like the durability, of a sustance (turning a jacket into an armor without altering the shape, elasitcity, and weight was Matter 2 the last time I chacked), it should also be able to alter the weight and mass. So, instead to turn the excess silver into air, just dump one extra success of Matter 2 to sligthly alter the mass.<br /> <br /> But it's necessary for most mages to be able to kill most werewolves in a fight unprepared to not be prey for them? Isn't enough with being potentialy more dangerous than a deer or a normal guy? .<br /> <br /> If your answer it's no, then sure, mages are prey. Not because a mage can't possibly slay a werewolf unprepared, but because it's hard, and there's a lot more chances that it will end bad for the mage than for the werewolf.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T16:55:36-08:00","id":1035894,"title":"","content":"I think it is more knowing the limitations of the character type. Mages are powerful with experience and preparation, much more so than equivalent supernatural characters, but they are not meant to be tanks. Mages survive through deception, evasion, and subterfuge. <br /> <br /> I have been playing Mage since 1996, and I still find it odd that there are Mage players who think their character's are Superman. Yes, Mages are adaptable and flexible, but they go squish as well as any other mortal when going toe-to-toe with other supernaturals without their Spheres. Even Changelings without their Arts are tougher than Mages without their Spheres. And you do not need exotic powers, just getting rid of foci is sufficient (and you can take a Mage's hands, feet, and tongue if they do not have more separable foci).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T17:33:23-08:00","id":1035905,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have been playing Mage since 1996, and I still find it odd that there are Mage players who think their character's are Superman.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a common misconception. They see all the powers of the Spheres and go crazy. I can turn werewolves to silver and vampires to chairs with a twich if my fingers !!!!!!.<br /> It's only when you meditate on the rules (and/or on your experience) how hard it's to pull all off that bulshit, how unlikely it's to be prepared for EVERYTHING (even with Time there are going to be things that you ain't going to expect)...and that while mages may be able to potentialy do everything, they rarely manage to do everything they want, in the practice.<br /> <br /> However, let's not get crazy. Mages aren't as weak as Norman, the normal guy. I will defend that the average mage can be as strong as the average Hunter when unprepared.<br /> <br /> My definition of unprepared it's not naked, but with the average amount of precaution that players have.<br /> <br /> I think it's rare for a mage to be without any means of defense, any sort of protection (I've yet to play with a troupe that disregards self defense entirely. Maybe your experience was different). I had an Euthanatos once who had Entropy 1 always on, to detect trouble, that way he wasn't easy to ambush. Most Hermetics never go out without one magick wand, same goes for most Agents (exept it's a gun). A mage isn't often without, at least, one Sphere. It can happen (especialy if the Foci it's too cumbersome or outlandish. It happened to one Etherite I had, he didn't carry his focy because they would attract too much attention) but it's not so common. Even then they would lose to a werewolf. But to a changeling?. Really?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-21-2017, 08:37 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T18:04:14-08:00","id":1035911,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035905#post1035905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think it's rare for a mage to be without any means of defense, any sort of protection (I've yet to play with a troupe that disregards self defense entirely. Maybe your experience was different). I had an Euthanatos once who had Entropy 1 always on, to detect trouble, that way he wasn't easy to ambush. Most Hermetics never go out without one magick wand, same goes for most Agents (exept it's a gun). A mage isn't often without, at least, one Sphere. It can happen (especialy if the Foci it's too cumbersome or outlandish. It happened to one Etherite I had, he didn't carry his focy because they would attract too much attention) but it's not so common. Even then they would lose to a werewolf. But to a changeling?. Really?.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly. Given that Mages tend to have multiple different kinds of Instruments (7 minimum, as of M20), it's harder to assume any given Mage is totally without magical options.<br /> <br /> A couple pages back, someone brought up the scenario of an Arete 5 Etherite with a ludicrious number of Sphere dots, but didn't happen to bring any of them when they went to a supermarket. Quite simply, if an Etherite with that level of experience doesn't have at least one sonic screwdriver (or similar) in his pocket wherever he goes, he deserves to die.<br /> <br /> And that's assuming he's not from the Adventurer faction of the Society of Ether. In that case, he may very well be literally Armed so long as he has his two fists. While this might not allow him to pull off all his more outrageous feats of Science(!), it does make him capable of defending himself. Possibly more trouble than he's worth, to any casual predator.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the scenario placed the attack in a supermarket. Any Inspired Scientist worth his salt could MacGuyver a way out of that situation with half the contents of a grocery store. Including, probably, with actual salt. Again, this isn't a perfect fix for the Mage; he's still in mortal danger and must be very quick to do said MacGuyvering. But it does mean he's not helpless. And what predators hate more is &quot;prey&quot; that can bite back. Why do you think most predator animals target the youngest, oldest, or sickest prey animals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-21T19:50:19-08:00","id":1035923,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035855#post1035855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A grain silo. That is conveniently located in the same dark alley where you get jumped by a werewolf.</div> </div> </div> </div>Most werewolves hang out closer to grain silos, though. The urban contingent is only about one quarter of them or so. Also, you could go with flour sacks and chunky salsa instead, though, as with the nerve gas and WP, that's not really the best idea if you're in close quarters with the intended target.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> If that's the case then just pull out a light machine gun you've loaded with silver bullets and shoot the sunovabich. </div> </div> </div>You don't pull out a machine gun of any type. You lug it around, an ungainly thing frequently weighed down by a bipod at the front to keep it from firing wildly in every direction. And in an alleyway, there's not much room to swing one around without banging the barrel and/or bipod on something, which adds up to an unpleasant time when a werewolf in wolf form (probably way more reasonable for maneuvering in a restricted alleyway than Crinos) runs under you and pulls out a hamstring or two.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T00:32:27-08:00","id":1035978,"title":"","content":"Going with an actual prey scenario it is not very difficult for a beginning mage to be prepared with one effect.<br /> Entropy 2 to lower the chance of being a target of a violent encounter.<br /> <br /> Mind 2 to give you an aura of \u201cnot the right target\u201c<br /> Which is a variation of the rote \u201cSomebody else's Problem\u201c A mind rote that diverts attention an has a lot of similarities to Arcane.<br /> <br /> Which is another point. Even low levels make a mage an unlikely target. (Because there a so much more available targets)<br /> <br /> And when you consider high level Arcane...<br /> You have prey with dicepool over 10 (3 dex+ 3 stealth+ Arcane 5), on top you lose 5 dice to notice them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:17:41-08:00","id":1036051,"title":"","content":"Let me give you all an example of mages (or my mage) becoming prey, note: spheres are spirit 3, prime 2, corr 1<br /> <br /> So, in an attempt to make allies my character goes to the local forest to communicate with the garou. He approaches them in the umbra while they're burning fire. One of them comes into the umbra and begins to blackmail him. He forces him out of the umbra<br /> <br /> I talk to the elders and they tell me to leave. I leave and meet a fera that I try to get as an ally. She takes it as me stalking her and has me tied up to a car and transported to the forest. <br /> <br /> 5-6 werewolves, including an elder stand over me and taunt me, tell me how spiritually weak I am, and the whole time I'm thinking &quot;my character is pathetic.&quot;<br /> <br /> So, the elder lights his sword on fire and makes my shaman grovel. Then, they eventually decide to kill him due to the power he may very well possess in the future to come against them. <br /> <br /> The fera shoots him with an arrow, the elder decapitates him and a sword ruptures his spline. <br /> <br /> Question is, what would you have done in this particular situation? (I tried escaping into the umbra but their initiatives were higher than mine)<br /> <br /> In all reality, I'm not even sure if having other spheres would have made a difference.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:19:37-08:00","id":1036052,"title":"","content":"Yes, Mages are better off avoiding drawing attention than looking for other supernatural creatures. Each level of Arcane should halve the chances of a random attack by supernatural creatures (which would probably be only 1:10,000 per day in a normal city). A Mage with Arcane 5 should be have less than a 10% chance of being randomly attacked by supernatural creatures during their life. The average human should probably survive one attack every quarter century, though the nature of the attacks may be financial (Mages), mental (Changelings), physical (Kindred or KJ), or spiritual (Demons, Spirits, Wraiths, etc). Attacks by Fera should be very rare, as Fera do not normally need the money, do not normally need to feed on humans, and do not normally need to possess humans.<br /> <br /> Your character suffered from an accidental territorial intrusion. You probably accidentally stumbled upon their Caern and, after they warned you away, you pursued one of their members. While the final taunting was a bit much, they were actually merciful and restrained for Garou the first time, as they would normally kill uninvited Mages who stumble upon their Caerns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-22-2017, 10:28 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:32:47-08:00","id":1036059,"title":"","content":"We must realize that these scenarios are asking different types of Supernatural powers to enguage one another in one of their's preferred form of combat (werewolf's - close quarters) and then saying said supernatural is the best all around combatant.<br /> <br /> It's like telling a physics professor he's stupid because he failed a exam on brain surgery. It just isn't so.<br /> <br /> We are kidding ourselves if we say Werewolves aren't the typical dominate force in close combat, they are made for it. This doesn't mean they are all automatically screwed in other forms of warfare but they excel in close quarters.<br /> <br /> The Vampire is made for subtlety, now some of them can fight up close, quite well in fact. Most werewolves don't want to tangle with Karsh for sure, but most vampires arent like him. They will use manipulation and guile to weaken thier enemy before finishing them off with subordinates.<br /> <br /> Likewise the Mage will use his command of the spheres to learn everything he can about his enemy before destroying him without the enemy even knowing what happened. Up close and personal? Not if he can help it as it woild require a great deal of preparation and luck on his part.<br /> <br /> They are each different, with their own specialties, quit trying to compare pitchers to linebackers and concluding the pitcher is a pansy athlete because the linbacker laid him out without trying.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/987-tuch","name":"Tuch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar987_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T07:45:12-08:00","id":1036063,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Your character suffered from an accidental territorial intrusion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't accidental!!. He entered in their territory knowingly:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJhon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>in an attempt to make allies</b> my character goes to the local forest to communicate with the garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well. That's why I say we should define what it's &quot;prey&quot;. ANY supernatural creature, even another fera, would likely be killed in that situation.<br /> You, literaly, walked into the fortress of your enemy, without any plan (you character may not have known that werewolves hated mages, but that's tangential to the issue). Caerns are very well protected, usualy by high rank Garou and spirits.<br /> <br /> BTW, a werewolf cub shouldn't take for granted that he can enter uninvited a Horizon Realm and escape with his skin, if he goes alone and without preparation. \u00bfDoes that make werewolves prey?. I would think not.<br /> <br /> So, pray tell me, <i>What's a Prey</i>? , What isn't a Prey?.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:09:39-08:00","id":1036075,"title":"","content":"Garou do not control every forest. While they are likely to be dominant in the wilderness area of the continental USA (2.7% of the land area or 170,500 square miles), the forested area of the continental USA (34% of the land area or 1,180,000 square miles) is far too large to be claimed by the twelve hundred or so Garou who call the USA home. Of course, if you are a Mage and go hunting for Caerns, you will have a much higher probability of running into Garou (and Garou may be the least unpleasant thing that you run into when you find a strange Caern).<br /> <br /> I think 'prey' in this context means innate abilities. Any human can go into the wilderness with a Land Rover, body armor, and a small arsenal to slaughter wolves, and he will be the top predator (at least if there are no local Garou around). The same human who runs out of gas on a stretch of lonely road in the middle of the forest with just his street clothes and the stuff in the trunk of his car is probably going to be prey if the local wolves take exception to his existence. Even Changelings, since they have innate lethal soak and have their innate Birthrights, are less vulnerable than Mages when stripped to just their innate abilities (Mages are just humans with strange backgrounds when they are stripped down to their innate abilities).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:15:39-08:00","id":1036078,"title":"","content":"If mages are prey because an unprepared starting character can't survive a fight with 6 experienced Garou in their territory then everyone it's prey in the WoD. Even a Mokole would likely die against:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJhon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">5-6 werewolves, including an elder</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:21:14-08:00","id":1036080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think 'prey' in this context means innate abilities. Any human can go into the wilderness with a Land Rover, body armor, and a small arsenal to slaughter wolves, and he will be the top predator (at least if there are no local Garou around). The same human who runs out of gas on a stretch of lonely road in the middle of the forest with just his street clothes and the stuff in the trunk of his car is probably going to be prey if the local wolves take exception to his existence. Even Changelings, since they have innate lethal soak and have their innate Birthrights, are less vulnerable than Mages when stripped to just their innate abilities (Mages are just humans with strange backgrounds when they are stripped down to their innate abilities).</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, if having innate habilities it's what differences prey from predator, then yes, mages (usualy) have no &quot;inate habilities&quot;. They have to learn to fight, and have one or two &quot;weapons&quot;, to be different for the normal mortal. Then again, same goes for Hunters. If a Hunter it's out of Conviction, he can't do shit.<br /> <br /> EDIT:<br /> Now that I think about that, this isn't necesarily true. Some mages can use magick with their fists or their speech (as has been stated previously). Even naked a mage may be better off than a human<br /> <br /> SO, no, mages are no prey. Not even naked, dependant on their foci. Just add some good old aggravated damage to your fists and that changeling it's going to have a run for his money.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 11:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:23:59-08:00","id":1036082,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036078#post1036078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If mages are prey because an unprepared starting character can't survive a fight with 6 experienced Garou in their territory then everyone it's prey in the WoD. Even a Mokole would likely die against:<br /> <br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>I think that there is this prevailing notion that high-level Shamans (spirit mages) are incredibly strong and wield more umbral authority than many of Gaia's breed in the Umbra. I just find that hard to believe. Yeah, you don't incur paradox in the umbra, but that's about it. Many of gaia's breed are completely composite beings when in the umbra, so it's no different than encountering them in the real world. If you run into one, you're pretty much prey (I've had multiple instances where Garou have attacked my mage because they felt as if he thought he &quot;owned&quot; the spirit world.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:42:18-08:00","id":1036087,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I think that there is this prevailing notion that high-level Shamans (spirit mages) are incredibly strong and wield more umbral authority than many of Gaia's breed in the Umbra. </div> </div> </div>High-level Shamans wield more umbral authority than any other Mage. This does not mean that they wield more authority than many of Gaia's breed, at least not in the Middle Umbra (that's the place where Gaia's breed has the most authority). The authority of Gaia's breed it's not due to their power, but because they did many powerful pacts with incredibly powerful spirits. Shamans did pacts with powerful spirits too, but not that many, just enough to not be kicked out of the Aetherial Realm, where they want to travel there.<br /> <br /> However:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, you don't incur paradox in the umbra, but that's about it. Many of gaia's breed are completely composite beings when in the umbra, so it's no different than encountering them in the real world. If you run into one, you're pretty much prey (I've had multiple instances where Garou have attacked my mage because they felt as if he thought he &quot;owned&quot; the spirit world.) </div> </div> </div>You're underestimating what &quot;not incuring in paradox&quot; means for a Mage.<br /> <br /> It makes ALL magick less difficult. It means that they can have any sort of bizarre shenaningan in place without much trouble. It means that you could encounter an Etherite with his Super-Starship that travels faster than light and does 25 aggravated damage to everything in a radious of ten miles, just because his forcefield it's active, and that's before he fires his super-weapons.<br /> <br /> A &quot;powerful&quot; Shaman might have similar shenanigans in place, he may be inmaterial (Life 4 Forces 4 to become pure energy), exist in several layers of the umbra at the same time (Spirit 4, Correspondence 4 + Life 4 to not die if one of &quot;you&quot; get's killed + Spheres specific to the layer), have Attributes above 10 (Life 3), Stop Time itself with just an Arete roll (Time 5, it's 3-5 successes, if I don't remember bad) . And that's on top of having some umbral alies (maybe not so many as the Garou, but it's better than nothing).<br /> This it's, however, all possible thanks to preparation (and to &quot;not incuring in paradox&quot; )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T08:46:04-08:00","id":1036090,"title":"","content":"In General shamen think quite the opposite way.<br /> They ask, they don't usually command.<br /> The Garou mistook you for an hermetic.<br /> They think they own the world as their birthright.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:23:30-08:00","id":1036151,"title":"","content":"Might seem like a dumb question, but why is our hypothetical Mage being attacked by a hypothetical Garou? What's the Garou's motivation here?<br /> <br /> Because the reason for why the fight is happening informs how it would play out. What each individual's &quot;victory&quot; condition is, whether the Garou will listen to reason, whether the Garou can just be driven off by a show of force (as I've said before, predators tend to eschew targets that are more trouble than they're worth).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:33:03-08:00","id":1036156,"title":"","content":"Being a Mage is a lot like being a human. Alone, unarmed, you're still potentially dangerous. But only slightly more dangerous than average Joe on the street. Other splats are like Bears. Bears are big, strong, and have claws. They will rip you limb from limb and eat you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last I checked, it was humans who hunt bears for fun and food.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T10:51:44-08:00","id":1036159,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036156#post1036156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Being a Mage is a lot like being a human. [...] Other splats are like Bears. Bears are big, strong, and have claws. They will rip you limb from limb and eat you.<br /> <br /> <br /> Last I checked, it was humans who hunt bears for fun and food.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exactly.<br /> The puny, thinskinned, fangless and senseless bipedals are only prey.<br /> Yet they have killed countless species.<br /> Rather strange, isn't it?<br /> Almost a PARADOX...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:08:17-08:00","id":1036171,"title":"","content":"Even when Mages are in the Umbra, they still suffer pattern bleeding when they maintain augmentations for more than a day (one health level of lethal damage or one point of Quintessence per point of improved attributes and major change). Pattern bleeding has nothing to do with the Consensus, it has everything to do with the Pattern (only by permanently changing the Pattern, by accepting permanent Paradox, can you avoid it). Archmages avoid pattern bleeding by consuming large amounts of Quintessence or by accepting large amounts of permanent Paradox.<br /> <br /> As for creating multiple copies of yourself, I think that only one copy can actually use True Magic because there is only one Avatar and each would count as a 'major' change to the other copies (meaning that each copy takes a number of health levels of lethal damage or requires a number of points of Quintessence per day equal to the other number of copies). Like most ubermunchkingamer tricks, it only works if STs are willing to ignore the rules of Pattern Bleeding, Paradox, etc. When STs are unwilling to let players break the rules, then the trick is only somewhat abusive (it would still require 20 successes per copy though, as copying yourself is a godlike feat).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:26:59-08:00","id":1036187,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036171#post1036171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even when Mages are in the Umbra, they still suffer pattern bleeding when they maintain augmentations for more than a day (one health level of lethal damage or one point of Quintessence per point of improved attributes and major change). Pattern bleeding has nothing to do with the Consensus, it has everything to do with the Pattern (only by permanently changing the Pattern, by accepting permanent Paradox, can you avoid it). Archmages avoid pattern bleeding by consuming large amounts of Quintessence or by accepting large amounts of permanent Paradox.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is even worse, pattern bleeding occurs even with permanent effects. Permadox and Pattern bleeding are not really linked. You can only avoid it if you pay for the improvements with XP (half the normal cost) after you made it permanent..<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036171#post1036171\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for creating multiple copies of yourself, I think that only one copy can actually use True Magic because there is only one Avatar and each would count as a 'major' change to the other copies (meaning that each copy takes a number of health levels of lethal damage or requires a number of points of Quintessence per day equal to the other number of copies). Like most ubermunchkingamer tricks, it only works if STs are willing to ignore the rules of Pattern Bleeding, Paradox, etc. When STs are unwilling to let players break the rules, then the trick is only somewhat abusive (it would still require 20 successes per copy though, as copying yourself is a godlike feat).</div> </div> </div> </div>HDYDT has this covered (for good and ill) with the Correspondence table(use the entry with the weakest connection) plus 1 for each location plus 1 for indepedent movement(and HL) and 1 for Multitasking. (Everywhere at once Correspondence 4, Life 3, Mind 1) altough you still take damage if one of the copies gets killed: 1 HL agg damage. One Avatar is not so much of an issue, you can do 1 effect per round with your original self. Because of your high capability in Correspondence it is not really a problem you can not overcome (in fact it costs only 1 additional success to send your effect to anyplace one of your copies perceives.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":12022,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","user":"Nonsense","date":".  Pattern Bleeding 01-22-2017, 02:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:38:50-08:00","id":1036196,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035799#post1035799\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think permanent effects, vulgar or not, give paradox. But I could be wrong and can't be bothered to check.<br /> <br /> Crafting wonders requires Prime 4 + sphere from which you want to draw the effect, so very few mages are capable of that. It's entirely possible that in the town of adventure <i>no one</i> is capable of that.</div> </div> </div> </div>No need for that much. You can still make temporary &quot;one use&quot; amulets with only <b><u>Prime 2</u></b> that will be VERY useful.<br /> <br /> So, just walk around with a little bit of &quot;Fireball Dust&quot;, enough for 5 shoots. If you keep your 8 successes from the maximum your inititial char can accumulate, that means that you need just a little bit of Tass to walk around with a 15 AGGRAVETED damage bomb enough for 5 uses before having to replenish in your Sanctum (1 success to hit one target, the remaining 7 gives 14 damage + 1 from Forces), and for all that you'll only need Forces 3 and Prime 2 (begginers chars can start with both spheres at 3). Is that enough for anyone would be &quot;Mage Hunters&quot;?<br /> <br /> In fact, in a Cabal of PC, isn't even necessary that all of them have Prime... One is all it takes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:54:32-08:00","id":1036206,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals#post1035738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this came up in a thread on another forum and I figured I'd post this here to get some input from people more familiar with Mage than I am (I have most of the books, but have never actually gotten to play a Mage game). So I'm looking for thoughts on the following quote:<br /> <br /> <br /> This sounds incredibly incorrect to me, but being less familiar with the system I can't necessarily point out why. I do agree Mages are far, far better with preparation (sometimes unbeatable). But to say they &quot;should never assume that they are anything but prey when they deal with other supernatural creatures&quot;?<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm curious to get the Mage forum's perspective.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Every group in the World of Darkness thinks they are the be-all-end-all. None of them are, and all of them are. Everybody is both profoundly deadly and desperately vulnerable. Mages attack best from deep cover and with preparation. Example: Make the Vampire's house <i>accidentally</i> burn down an hour after sunrise in June. Turn the hunter's bullets to silver, but only while they are inside of living werewolf flesh. Other ideas should be easy to churn out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-27-2019, 07:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T11:56:57-08:00","id":1036207,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035817#post1035817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not backing up the &quot;prey&quot;; bit, but there are some things to keep in mind.<br /> <br /> That would be vulgar as hell, so a mage can't take success as a given, even if they're insane enough to want to do it. Even if you do succeed, Willie Peter is a substance that invites a lot of official attention, what with it being a less direct health hazard as well as a fire hazard and all; if you activate it too close to yourself, you'll need Life to heal your burns and avoid developing phossy jaw, and another Matter effect to dispose of the WP so that it doesn't contaminate the scene, or anyone at it. Assuming that you're able to get away, of course, and not in the custody of authorities who really want to know where you got all of that undocumented WP, which, if used for any purpose other than simply making smoke, is considered a chemical weapon.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vampire and Werewolf players think they are safe from a Mage &quot;cuz Paradox&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let me tell you this: you're not.<br /> <br /> While a Mage will take care to be <u>subtle</u> <b>most of the time</b> in order to avoid <u><b>unnecessary</b></u> paradox...<br /> <br /> When a Hit Mark squadron, armed to the teeth, or a Garou pack, Vampire coterie or monstrous insanities summoned by a nephandus are chasing the Mage<br /> <br /> Them, all bets are off. To hell with Paradox! Go down with a BANG!!! YEAH BABY, LET PARADOX STACK UP 20 or more!!! Who cares? When you're fighting for your life, just unleash your full powers, and hope that when the Paradox kicks, it may also take a few of the bastards with you<br /> <br /> And if I'm running in fury mode, basically saying &quot;Consensus can be damned!&quot;, do you REALLY think I'll care about the consequences or legal implications! Dude, Mages fight or work for the Technocracy, who is the POLICE OF REALITY, and do that on a regular base.<br /> <br /> Which is why a cornered Mage will be the most dangerous OF ALL<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035817#post1035817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou, meanwhile, can use Master of Fire, a starting Gift native to the most populous splats of the monster type, to turn the damage bashing, and being half spirit presumably means that they don't have to worry about developing phossy jaw after the fact. Solomonds and Chu-jung kamuii in wani form could probably outright bathe in it with no ill effects, and go so far as to take control of it and set it back on the mage It would definitely take care of vampires, but then, again, you'd have to either be ignorant of the full ramifications of using WP or else crazy to do it. Unlike a nexus crawler, a mage generally has to face the music for their wanton disruptions of reality.<br /> <br /> Spirit of the Bird. The werewolf can then play chicken with the mage, testing who's willing to fly into an open area to avoid an obstacle first. Changelings, Hungry Dead, and Shinma can also take to the skies after a flying mage, to say nothing of Fera who are either of flight-capable animals or otherwise have some way to gain said capability, which is broad enough to include most of them. Yes, even the Rokea, and they'll swim through the air after you as a giant shark as a result of how the Gift works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Congratulations on creating a Mage-Hunter-Specific Garou. Now tell me, how many more Gifts will your character have to have to be able to do with every possible contingencies when hunting Mages?<br /> <br /> Do you also have a Gift to turn your Garou imune to Silver? Because the Mage can simply turn the floor above the Garou into Silver, or the air he breathes... And many, many more","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:06:47-08:00","id":1036211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035823#post1035823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a Possessed can just turn off all of a Mage's magical effects for a few turns when they get to 100'. Oh, what can a Mage do when their Spheres are turned off for the three turns it takes for them to fall to their deaths? Nothing except flap their arms and hope that they remembered to pay their life insurance...</div> </div> </div> </div>But not magikal items (talismans, periapts, relics, amulets), because those items have been PERMANENTLY changed... A magikal scythe that sucks wraiths corpus is not &quot;activating&quot; the effect, that effect is a permanent part of it's pattern.<br /> <br /> So, next time a Qui La Machine enters your Caern to sanitize it and you try that trick, don't get surprised when you find yourself &quot;disembodied&quot; on the after life...<br /> <br /> You also can't &quot;cancel&quot; any effect that were made permanent by the total alteration of the pattern. So, when I use Matter 5 to create ADAMANTIUM or VIBRANIUM... Your little &quot;dispel&quot; gift will be as useful as a picture of an oxigen atom to a drowning man. Same goes for any life permanent alterations (so, next time that some Victors and monstruosities from the Progenitors are hunting you... Please use that little power. It would be very funny to see).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:14:49-08:00","id":1036214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036207#post1036207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Do you also have a Gift to turn your Garou imune to Silver? Because the Mage can simply turn the floor above the Garou into Silver, or the air he breathes... And many, many more</div> </div> </div> </div>During a fight? That level of transformation is easily equal to blowing up a car, so it would be an Outlandish Feat (requiring a minimum of 10 successes), which would take a Mage with Arete 4 and Matter 4 an average of five turns to accomplish. Are you going to stand around chanting for five turns while Garou are chewing on you?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T12:21:16-08:00","id":1036216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035911#post1035911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exactly. Given that Mages tend to have multiple different kinds of Instruments (7 minimum, as of M20), it's harder to assume any given Mage is totally without magical options.<br /> <br /> A couple pages back, someone brought up the scenario of an Arete 5 Etherite with a ludicrious number of Sphere dots, but didn't happen to bring any of them when they went to a supermarket. Quite simply, if an Etherite with that level of experience doesn't have at least one sonic screwdriver (or similar) in his pocket wherever he goes, he deserves to die.<br /> <br /> And that's assuming he's not from the Adventurer faction of the Society of Ether. In that case, he may very well be literally Armed so long as he has his two fists. While this might not allow him to pull off all his more outrageous feats of Science(!), it does make him capable of defending himself. Possibly more trouble than he's worth, to any casual predator.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the scenario placed the attack in a supermarket. Any Inspired Scientist worth his salt could MacGuyver a way out of that situation with half the contents of a grocery store. Including, probably, with actual salt. Again, this isn't a perfect fix for the Mage; he's still in mortal danger and must be very quick to do said MacGuyvering. But it does mean he's not helpless. And what predators hate more is &amp;quot;prey&amp;quot; that can bite back. Why do you think most predator animals target the youngest, oldest, or sickest prey animals?</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason why a used such an ABSURD example of an archmage, that probably took 3 life times to reach his level of power, were to ilustrate exactly what kind of an absurd scenario to make such a claim of &quot;beeing prey&quot; true.<br /> <br /> So, unless you are in an absurd and total unrealistic situation, Mages are Dangerous. Very, very dangerous","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:07:02-08:00","id":1036235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals#post1035738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So this came up in a thread on another forum and I figured I'd post this here to get some input from people more familiar with Mage than I am (I have most of the books, but have never actually gotten to play a Mage game). So I'm looking for thoughts on the following quote:<br /> <br /> <br /> This sounds incredibly incorrect to me, but being less familiar with the system I can't necessarily point out why. I do agree Mages are far, far better with preparation (sometimes unbeatable). But to say they &quot;should never assume that they are anything but prey when they deal with other supernatural creatures&quot;?<br /> <br /> In any case, I'm curious to get the Mage forum's perspective.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Many deserve to be... they hunt Vampires for Tass.<br /> <br /> defile Garou caerns.<br /> <br /> And some have assaulted fae glens.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:10:21-08:00","id":1036236,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036051#post1036051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me give you all an example of mages (or my mage) becoming prey, note: spheres are spirit 3, prime 2, corr 1<br /> <br /> So, in an attempt to make allies my character goes to the local forest to communicate with the garou. He approaches them in the umbra while they're burning fire. One of them comes into the umbra and begins to blackmail him. He forces him out of the umbra<br /> <br /> I talk to the elders and they tell me to leave. I leave and meet a fera that I try to get as an ally. She takes it as me stalking her and has me tied up to a car and transported to the forest. <br /> <br /> 5-6 werewolves, including an elder stand over me and taunt me, tell me how spiritually weak I am, and the whole time I'm thinking &amp;quot;my character is pathetic.&amp;quot;<br /> <br /> So, the elder lights his sword on fire and makes my shaman grovel. Then, they eventually decide to kill him due to the power he may very well possess in the future to come against them. <br /> <br /> The fera shoots him with an arrow, the elder decapitates him and a sword ruptures his spline. <br /> <br /> Question is, what would you have done in this particular situation? (I tried escaping into the umbra but their initiatives were higher than mine)<br /> <br /> In all reality, I'm not even sure if having other spheres would have made a difference.</div> </div> </div> </div>Once I defeated a Garou with Dimensional Sciences (Spirit) 2 and my always on &quot;Danger Sense&quot; Entropy 1 and some minor coincidental effects of Entropy 2. Oh, and I was a Void Engeneer, and had none of my toys with me. And I was a mental/social character.<br /> <br /> Wanna know how?<br /> <br /> Ok, here's how: my Danger Sense (which is always on), explained as a form of &quot;meditation&quot;, but none of the supersticious mambo jambo your traditionalists misconceptions might think, rather, it's a product of intensive mental concentration to sharpen your senses to the level of a machine (from time to time you need to get back to the &quot;training room&quot; to spend some time reviewing combat tactics and situational conditions of the field and repass most cases of unforseen contingencies in order to keep your mind always sharpen). With that, I had a permanent 5 successes to sense any dangerous situation, that's a HUGE edge to any agent.<br /> <br /> As soon as why would be aggressor tryed to sprang the trap on me, I sensed a &quot;disturbance in the Force&quot;. Something wasn't quite right. Too quiet.<br /> <br /> Luckly, I had been trained by the best of the best of the Union. I would turn the trap against the one trying to get me.<br /> <br /> Finding myself on a dire situation... Required dire actions. Thing is, I know for a fact that brain waves can have a quantum effect on the quintessential flutuations on parallel dimensions... That Dimensional Science 1, a first semester discipline, and I was paying attention to the class. All I had to do was to be able to set the correct brain waves to have the correct effect. <br /> <br /> Traditionalists, of course, have no idea of what they're doing most of the time, but when they use what they call &quot;blood Magic&quot;, they are in fact making use of the pain as a way to attune their brain waves to the correct patterns of oscilations to send quantum waves to parallel dimensions, and their blood as a strong source of ressonance to serve as a source of a &quot;quantum anchor&quot; for the effect.<br /> <br /> And so, that's what I did. &quot;Blood Magic&quot;.<br /> <br /> But not just that. I had a plan. A dangerous one, but still... I looked at the trash can, and found a dead coachroach. Good, that would be perfect.<br /> <br /> I used a mail in the trash can to cut myself. I poured my blood on the dead insect. As the pain took hold of my mind, I know why brain waves needed to change from Gama-B to Delta-Y. The pain would help that, if I could manage to remain focused (not hard to set the right thought patterns for a trained agent). The blood mixing with the body of the dead insect would change my psychic emanations EXACTLY to the primordial waves I wanted to create...<br /> <br /> I took my time. My enemy were still waiting, confident that he would have the hold on me. The thing I was doing was uncommon for an agent, so I took my time to make things RIGHT.<br /> <br /> And my efforts brought fruits... Many Entropic Extra Dimensional Entities showed up... As I was expecting.<br /> <br /> Well... The Nexus Crawler and many other banes made a quick job with the werewolf. I had to make a few &quot;pacts&quot; with the spirits of Wyrm, pacts that, of course, I wouldn't follow later, like promisses of quintessence, services, whatever... Well, I promisses them heaven and Earth.<br /> <br /> After that, I got grounded for a while in the Amalgam, and we had a few troubles with banes since that (which is very good, because that way we wouldn't need to keep hunting the damn things around all corners of the Tellurian, besides, after that I made sure to make alliances with many pattern Extra Dimensional Manifeststions - alliances with Weaver spirits).<br /> <br /> But I won.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:28:43-08:00","id":1036244,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036051#post1036051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me give you all an example of mages (or my mage) becoming prey, note: spheres are spirit 3, prime 2, corr 1</div> </div> </div> </div>Since you placed yourself on that ridiculous situation, here is what I could have done:<br /> <br /> Manipulation + Fast Talk: &quot;Could you please just let me make an last pray, so that my soul may find find the halls of my ancestors?&quot;<br /> <br /> Or, if they just tell you to shut up while acting like the typical villain who love &quot;I'm so superior&quot; speeches while giving time to the heroes to defeat him, you should use the time of their yadda yadda to use your effects.<br /> <br /> First, use Prime 2 to attune the ressonance of the ropes to yours. After that, those ropes would be as if it were your own flesh.<br /> <br /> Secondly, AWAKE the spirit of the rope.<br /> <br /> Third, keep praying for the spirits of destruction... But only unleash the call a little before the Garou were done with their lecturing and deciding on the execution method.<br /> <br /> When the banes show up, ask for the ropes to release you and to trap your enemies. Since the spirit of the ropes loves you (thanks to the atunement), they'll do that.<br /> <br /> While ravoc runs wild, throw quintessence bolts in anyone that crosses your path.<br /> <br /> You may wanna have scanned to area previosly with Corr 1 to set the best escape rote.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:35:55-08:00","id":1036246,"title":"","content":"Spirit 2 is not sufficient to summon anything and Nexus Crawlers eat Mages as well as Garou.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:48:12-08:00","id":1036252,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036207#post1036207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampire and Werewolf players think they are safe from a Mage &quot;cuz Paradox&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let me tell you this: you're not.<br /> <br /> While a Mage will take care to be <u>subtle</u> <b>most of the time</b> in order to avoid <u><b>unnecessary</b></u> paradox...<br /> <br /> When a Hit Mark squadron, armed to the teeth, or a Garou pack, Vampire coterie or monstrous insanities summoned by a nephandus are chasing the Mage<br /> <br /> Them, all bets are off. To hell with Paradox! Go down with a BANG!!! YEAH BABY, LET PARADOX STACK UP 20 or more!!! Who cares? When you're fighting for your life, just unleash your full powers, and hope that when the Paradox kicks, it may also take a few of the bastards with you<br /> <br /> And if I'm running in fury mode, basically saying &quot;Consensus can be damned!&quot;, do you REALLY think I'll care about the consequences or legal implications! Dude, Mages fight or work for the Technocracy, who is the POLICE OF REALITY, and do that on a regular base.<br /> <br /> Which is why a cornered Mage will be the most dangerous OF ALL</div> </div> </div> </div>So what does that have to do with being jumped in an alleyway again? Was that even the agreed upon scenario? Because you suggested it, and it's a pretty bad time to be a mage, what with it being a quick, unforeseen attack and all. And it also doesn't change that a mage might end up killing themselves before they die of Paradox (if there is an unrestrained release of nerve gas or white phosphorous).<br /> <br /> Maybe we should just change the thread into how one game deals with another's antagonists. That seems more productive.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Congratulations on creating a Mage-Hunter-Specific Garou. Now tell me, how many more Gifts will your character have to have to be able to do with every possible contingencies when hunting Mages? </div> </div> </div>Gifts are super easy to learn and actually have lots of uses, so it's nowhere near &quot;specific hyperoptimized build&quot; level. Those first rank Gifts, if in-list, only cost 3 xp per. The cost doesn't even really go up all that much, especially if you learned a high Rank Gift through a totem.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, a specific build because of a Gift that allows you to fly? There aren't an infinite number of Gifts to learn under most assumptions of progression. You take whatever you can get<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Do you also have a Gift to turn your Garou imune to Silver? </div> </div> </div>Two, actually (Luna's Blessing and Luna's Avenger), and one that makes them resistant to it (Luna's Armor); Luna's Blessing even acts over a long term and might cause an attack using silver to botch when it otherwise wouldn't have. Those, however, are all higher Rank stuff (unless you follow a particular totem or have some very impressive marks for trickery and no regard for the pact, anyway).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Because the Mage can simply turn the floor above the Garou into Silver, or the air he breathes... And many, many more </div> </div> </div>So can nexus crawlers. Unlike nexus crawlers, however, most mages are fragile. If they tried to take on said crawler, they might succeed in keeping said bane from warping reality too much, but the bane would still get a normal action to tear into them, and even spectacular amounts of aggravated damage can get tanked by the amount of Essence a crawler usually carries around (meaning they they have at least thirty health levels, but probably more like fifty to eighty).<br /> <br /> That isn't even the strongest form of bane that warps reality, incidentally. Those are Dream Makers, and they effectively have <i>several hundred health levels</i>. Think the antagonist of the Wishmaster series, with a history that's suspiciously reminiscent of the background for the focus monsters of D:tF. You can't really go in for instant kills against that kind of being; even a shitload of successes in a direct magickal attack could just get no-sold by the stock of Essence that the bane is carrying around.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T13:55:24-08:00","id":1036259,"title":"","content":"And they are not even the most powerful of standard spirits. Nameless, spirits of the Wyld, can kill itself to erase anything less powerful than an Incarna from existence (permanently and forever removing it from all time). It also goes off like a nuke when it does.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:00:11-08:00","id":1036266,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036259#post1036259\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And they are not even the most powerful of standard spirits. Nameless, spirits of the Wyld, can kill itself to erase anything less powerful than an Incarna from existence (permanently and forever removing it from all time). It also goes off like a nuke when it does.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then again, it is a suicide attack, so it's probably not going to happen... maybe.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:00:29-08:00","id":1036267,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036235#post1036235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Many deserve to be... they hunt Vampires for Tass.<br /> <br /> defile Garou caerns.<br /> <br /> And some have assaulted fae glens.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Not our fault. When we look at you guys, all that we see are delicious living Tass bateries. Not to mention that some of you have tasteful Nodes as well... Hmmm... That just set my appettite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:02:19-08:00","id":1036268,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036246#post1036246\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 2 is not sufficient to summon anything and Nexus Crawlers eat Mages as well as Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit 2 can summon ANYTHING and I made a deal with the banes while the crawler were chewing<br /> <br /> And double crossed them after","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:14:19-08:00","id":1036273,"title":"","content":"Let me put this in perspective. A stupid mage doesn't live long enough to YOLO into, say, a pack of werewolves and survive the fight.<br /> <br /> A <i>powerful</i> mage can YOLO into a pack of werewolves and not just survive the fight, but come out of it completely unscathed. But why would they, when they can lay low until the Leonids and literally drop a meteor on their Caern, entirely coincidentally and something just about any Adept with the right paradigm and spheres can do?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:27:06-08:00","id":1036277,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036252#post1036252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So what does that have to do with being jumped in an alleyway again? Was that even the agreed upon scenario? Because you suggested it, and it's a pretty bad time to be a mage, what with it being a quick, unforeseen attack and all. And it also doesn't change that a mage might end up killing themselves before they die of Paradox (if there is an unrestrained release of nerve gas or white phosphorous).<br /> <br /> Maybe we should just change the thread into how one game deals with another's antagonists. That seems more productive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I just told you. Entropy 1. The Mage WON'T bump into the Garou on alley, no matter if by accident or on a trap.<br /> Unless you have a metuselah, the Mage is safe. But in that case, it wouldn't much matter what you do, if you pissed a 5th generation Vampire with thousands of years, you deserve to die.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036252#post1036252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Gifts are super easy to learn and actually have lots of uses, so it's nowhere near &amp;quot;specific hyperoptimized build&amp;quot; level. Those first rank Gifts, if in-list, only cost 3 xp per. The cost doesn't even really go up all that much, especially if you learned a high Rank Gift through a totem.<br /> <br /> I mean, seriously, a specific build because of a Gift that allows you to fly? There aren't an infinite number of Gifts to learn under most assumptions of progression. You take whatever you can get</div> </div> </div> </div>That's the thing, you are taking ONE single hypotetical situation and think things are all granted. That was just ONE EXAMPLE. Unless you think that EVERY Mage will try to fly away when confronted by by a Garou, your argument is pointless.<br /> <br /> Wanna see? Ok, Corr 3, and sayonara. Now that I'm in my Sanctum, I can use Corr 2 Prime 2 to send aggr damage at you without you even knowing were that's coming from.<br /> <br /> Do you think that would be to hard? Not at all. If my Sanctum is attuned to me, it's like casting effects on myself, so I would need only ONE success in Arete to port away.<br /> <br /> After, I just open 1 window to keep a track on you, and take my time to build up 25 successes on a pure quintess\u00eancia energy attack to give you 48 aggr in a single blow (and 2 Paradox of the effect plus 3 of the Jump is something I can live with).<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036252#post1036252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two, actually (Luna's Blessing and Luna's Avenger), and one that makes them resistant to it (Luna's Armor); Luna's Blessing even acts over a long term and might cause an attack using silver to botch when it otherwise wouldn't have. Those, however, are all higher Rank stuff (unless you follow a particular totem or have some very impressive marks for trickery and no regard for the pact, anyway).</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, Mage-Hunter customized. Lers try to make a Garou-Hunter customized Mage equiped with every possible contingencies after your initial Garou char and see how do you do.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036252#post1036252\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So can nexus crawlers. Unlike nexus crawlers, however, most mages are fragile. If they tried to take on said crawler, they might succeed in keeping said bane from warping reality too much, but the bane would still get a normal action to tear into them, and even spectacular amounts of aggravated damage can get tanked by the amount of Essence a crawler usually carries around (meaning they they have at least thirty health levels, but probably more like fifty to eighty).<br /> <br /> That isn't even the strongest form of bane that warps reality, incidentally. Those are Dream Makers, and they effectively have <i>several hundred health levels</i>. Think the antagonist of the Wishmaster series, with a history that's suspiciously reminiscent of the background for the focus monsters of D:tF. You can't really go in for instant kills against that kind of being; even a shitload of successes in a direct magickal attack could just get no-sold by the stock of Essence that the bane is carrying around.</div> </div> </div> </div>And?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:33:24-08:00","id":1036280,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036273#post1036273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Let me put this in perspective. A stupid mage doesn't live long enough to YOLO into, say, a pack of werewolves and survive the fight.<br /> <br /> A <i>powerful</i> mage can YOLO into a pack of werewolves and not just survive the fight, but come out of it completely unscathed. But why would they, when they can lay low until the Leonids and literally drop a meteor on their Caern, entirely coincidentally and something just about any Adept with the right paradigm and spheres can do?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=z5Otla5157c\" data-code=\"z5Otla5157c\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/z5Otla5157c/maxresdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:35:16-08:00","id":1036282,"title":"","content":"Spirit 2 can CALL anything short of very mighty Umbrood residing in their own faraway realm(e.g. Demon Lord from Hell) thats what Spirit 4 i nedded for.<br /> If a called Spirit decides to appear you have to strike a deal with it. It could be, that a calling produces not the desired mighty spirit but only a messenger for the busy spirit.<br /> <br /> The thing to go if you want a really powerful borderline munchkin mage, is to invest in wonders, familiars, (semi)permanent effects and hanged spells. Because they:<br /> 1. Are a reliable source of quickly getting effects requiring a bunch of successes.<br /> 2. You can actuallly &quot;cast&quot; more than one effect per round(because you only trigger the effect.)<br /> 3. Talismans and Fetisches can act out of their own volition. completely negating the nedd of an action on your part.<br /> 4. Talismans and Familiars can store Paradox(5 per Point in its rating), some can even negate it.<br /> 5. If you enchant your Clothes then you don't have to fear pattern bleeding<br /> 6. If an effect lasts only a day pattern bleeding isn't an issue<br /> <br /> Since Adept level is at least 45XP in the future, you have to work with charms and long lasting effects. Familiar is nice to have or absolutely high power (I am lucking at you Bad Luck Charm).<br /> <br /> Possibilities with the above mentioned spheres:<br /> - Smokebomb to step sideways (Spirit 3, Prime 2, Tass)<br /> - Medicine bag of slipstream (increased difficulty to hit you) (Correspondence 1, Prime2, Tass)<br /> - Candle to harden the Gauntlet (for use after you stepped sideways) (Spirit 3, Prime 2, Tass)<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:41:52-08:00","id":1036283,"title":"","content":"True, I couldn't have put that better.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Many deserve to be... they hunt Vampires for Tass.<br /> <br /> defile Garou caerns.<br /> <br /> And some have assaulted fae glens.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do Prey animals often do these things? I tought that exploiting the natural resources was the kind of things that hunters do <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anycase, the fact this debate even exists should be enough to demonstrate that Garou would do best not playing arround when they have the luck of facing a seemingly unprepared mage. Especialy if they don't know how powerful it's the mage, or how unprepared he is. Just attack the mage fast, no gloating, no abusing, no &quot;playing with your prey&quot;, because while a garou can finish a mage easily, you don't know what the mage might have under the sleeve.<br /> That alone it's reason enough to not parley with mages <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> EDIT: This has derailed into what we know it would <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 05:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T14:58:24-08:00","id":1036290,"title":"","content":"Wow. I put the question up and then got busy for a day or 2. I come back and there are 6 pages to catch up on.<br /> <br /> Just wanted to make sure to say thank you to everyone that's participated thus far. This has been an interesting enough read. Opinions on the status of Mages in the WoD seems to be quite varied. They seem to run the gamut of Mages being pushovers who run or die in every encounter to quasi-gods that can never lose.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:02:18-08:00","id":1036295,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036268#post1036268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirit 2 can summon ANYTHING and I made a deal with the banes while the crawler were chewing<br /> <br /> And double crossed them after</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit 2 calls, it does not summon, and major spirits like Nexus Crawlers do not respond to Spirit 2 calls. And the type of banes that respond to a Spirit 2 call cannot control Nexus Crawlers, that requires Incarna levels of power. Your ST was just being kind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:07:13-08:00","id":1036296,"title":"","content":"Major spirits respond to Spirit 2 calls like any other spirit. That it's, they respond if they feel like it.<br /> Do they feel like it?. Well, nobody knows what a Nexus Crawler feels, they're too unpredictable...so it's kind of a risky bet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 06:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:29:30-08:00","id":1036303,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036290#post1036290\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. I put the question up and then got busy for a day or 2. I come back and there are 6 pages to catch up on.<br /> <br /> Just wanted to make sure to say thank you to everyone that's participated thus far. This has been an interesting enough read. Opinions on the status of Mages in the WoD seems to be quite varied. They seem to run the gamut of Mages being pushovers who run or die in every encounter to quasi-gods that can never lose.</div> </div> </div> </div>Joined lately to the crowd, reading through the pages too.<br /> <br /> I suspect it boils down to the average favoritism of players. A Werewolf player WANTS her splat to be the apex predator, a Mage player WANTS mages to be unbeatable gods. The truth is, as frequently is somewhere in the middle, and I think the majority knows that.<br /> <br /> A mage could be very good at bashing things with proper build and foci, like an Akashayana, but ultimately they're humans and have more limitations, resource-wise and in other things. Werewolves are good at bashing per definition. That's their thing, that even their non-combat focused characters are better at combat than the other splats' similar ones with their forms and rage, while ALSO being good on their specific build. Mages would be better at other things, like sheer flexibility, insane ritual effects and information gathering,b ut they have to work really hard to be able to go toe-to-toe with a combat-focused garou, especially without preparation. <br /> <br /> It's a little bit like the ranger/fighter debate in D&amp;D. People are complaining since 3e that rangers are not as good as fighters, that instead of the ranger being the iconic two-weapon fighter, thanks to Drizzt, you could build a better two-weapon fighter with the fighter class. Well, duh, the fighter's purpose is to be the best at fighting, the ranger's purpose is to be flexible and being competent in more areas, including fighting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:43:14-08:00","id":1036311,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036268#post1036268\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirit 2 can summon ANYTHING and I made a deal with the banes while the crawler were chewing<br /> <br /> And double crossed them after</div> </div> </div> </div>What kind of deal did you make?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:46:31-08:00","id":1036313,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036282#post1036282\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Spirit 2 can CALL anything short of very mighty Umbrood residing in their own faraway realm(e.g. Demon Lord from Hell) thats what Spirit 4 i nedded for.<br /> If a called Spirit decides to appear you have to strike a deal with it. It could be, that a calling produces not the desired mighty spirit but only a messenger for the busy spirit.<br /> <br /> <b>The thing to go if you want a really powerful borderline munchkin mage, is to invest in wonders, familiars, (semi)permanent effects and hanged spells. Because they:<br /> 1. Are a reliable source of quickly getting effects requiring a bunch of successes.<br /> 2. You can actuallly &quot;cast&quot; more than one effect per round(because you only trigger the effect.)<br /> 3. Talismans and Fetisches can act out of their own volition. completely negating the nedd of an action on your part.<br /> 4. Talismans and Familiars can store Paradox(5 per Point in its rating), some can even negate it.<br /> 5. If you enchant your Clothes then you don't have to fear pattern bleeding<br /> 6. If an effect lasts only a day pattern bleeding isn't an issue</b><br /> <br /> Since Adept level is at least 45XP in the future, you have to work with charms and long lasting effects. Familiar is nice to have or absolutely high power (I am lucking at you Bad Luck Charm).<br /></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Mind giving some examples? As far as I'm aware, you still need to activate fetishes and talisman, although I could be wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:56:24-08:00","id":1036317,"title":"","content":"Yes, I agree with the idea that every supernatural creature has their specialty. Changelings are meant to be artists, Garou are meant to be combat monsters, Kindred are meant to be social manipulators, Mages are meant to be jack-of-all-trades but master-of-none, etc. Mages are capable of amazing feats, they can turn lead into gold and teleport from LA to London for tea, but they really should avoid combat with other supernatural creatures (and use diplomacy and bargaining to convince other supernatural creatures to fight on their behalf).<br /> <br /> Most supernatural creatures do not care about Mages, they have other problems and Mages can get very capable allies by helping other supernatural deal with the problems that they are not good at. If Bone Gnawers are going to lose their favorite park, Mages can manipulate the system to stop them from losing the park. If Malkavians are worried about an asylum being closed due to lack of funding, Mages can literally make gold to donate to save the asylum. Mages can be the fixers of the supernatural world if they want to and can be the difference between a peaceful city and a city with constant warfare between supernatural factions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T15:56:43-08:00","id":1036318,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036296#post1036296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Major spirits respond to Spirit 2 calls like any other spirit. That it's, they respond if they feel like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I have a question. Does Spirit 2 summon (as in make appear) spirits? Or does it call to them, to come if they want to. There is a very big difference here. I am genuinely curious how this works.<br /> <br /> With the Nexus Crawler example, I'd find it hard to believe that you could put out a call, and have one show up terribly fast, since they generally exist far removed from the Penumbra. I would imagine that if if were possible to have one appear, it would take a lot of successes to do so and thus (logically, to me) require a ritual casting. Or is my understanding of this off (it very well may be)?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:05:54-08:00","id":1036320,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals#post1035738\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><i>They should never get into fights with other supernatural creatures without proper preparation, should always avoid unnecessary fights with other supernatural creatures whenever possible, and should never fight fair against other supernatural creatures when they have to fight.</i></div> </div> </div> </div>Name a splat that's not true for. WoD practically runs on <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AlwaysABiggerFish\" target=\"_blank\">Always a Bigger Fish</a>. Any given splat has its associated boogeymen, from the Methuselahs to the Earthbound to HIT Marks to accountants who <i>really</i> want to talk about their stamp collection. <br /> <br /> The advice you gave is good no matter what sort of character facing whatever sort of opponent. Strike first, strike hard, strike again, and there is no such thing as overkill.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:06:32-08:00","id":1036321,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036318#post1036318\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a question. Does Spirit 2 summon (as in make appear) spirits? Or does it call to them, to come if they want to. There is a very big difference here. I am genuinely curious how this works.</div> </div> </div> </div>Neither. Conjuring spirits is Spirit 4.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> [ 4 ] Rend Gauntlet / Seal Breach / Bind Spirit [ Mage: The Ascension (20th Anniversary) -- Page 522 ]<br /> <br /> As the mage approaches Mastery, he can tear Gateways in the Gauntlet, allowing groups or large objects to pass through, or close such breaches, too. Both applications, of course, are deeply vulgar.<br /> <br /> <b>At this Rank, the mage may also compel spirits to appear</b>, bind them into Fetish objects, or tie them to certain spots or prisons. For obvious reasons, such bondage is risky, especially if the spirit is powerful. A brave or foolish Spirit mage can even turn himself into a temporary Fetish, channeling a spirit entity into his mortal body; in such cases, he loses his ability to use true magic, but he may employ the capabilities of the spirit inside him. On the flipside, he can also exorcise a spirit that has possessed a mortal host. In all cases, the mage enters a series of resisted rolls against the spirit, pitting his Willpower against that spirit's own. </div> </div> </div>Summoning spirits from afar would be Spirit 2 (what you need to talk to spirits) plus Correspondence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:14:20-08:00","id":1036325,"title":"","content":"And you would likely have a royally pissed off spirit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:36:56-08:00","id":1036332,"title":"","content":"&quot;For each Mage player who thinks a mage is a omnipotent god there is crappy game-master who forgot half of the rules of the game&quot; (cit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:37:19-08:00","id":1036333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036277#post1036277\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Like I said, Mage-Hunter customized.</div> </div> </div> </div> <div class=\"videocontainer with-aspect-ratio videocontainer-horizontal\" style=\"aspect-ratio: 16/9;\"> <a class=\"video-frame\" href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-code=\"pEZgJyTzqPg\" data-provider=\"youtube\" data-height=\"0\" data-width=\"0\" itemprop=\"video\"> <div class=\"videothumbnail\" style=\"\"> <img src=\"https://img.youtube.com/vi/pEZgJyTzqPg/hqdefault.jpg\" alt=\"\" /> <div class=\"videothumbnailoverlay\"></div> </div> </a> </div><br /> <br /> Burrow and Spirit of the Bird easily fit into functioning as an escape and general ambush capacity for anyone who doesn't count on werewolves being able to travel under or over (which is anyone unfamiliar with the Garou). Resist Toxin and Master of Fire are both starting Gifts for a broad swath of Garou, which cubs would likely snap up for various reasons.<br /> <br /> If I were going to make a W:tA character specifically to fuck with mages, I'd make a Viskr Ananasi with the rite for instantly summoning paradox-spirits and max out their social Traits so that they could plausibly pretend to be the mage's &quot;friend&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:37:21-08:00","id":1036334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036325#post1036325\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And you would likely have a royally pissed off spirit.</div> </div> </div> </div>That really depends on the spirit. Most would probably see this as an employment opportunity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer","name":"Kammerer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12892_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1191"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:46:09-08:00","id":1036336,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kammerer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036334#post1036334\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That really depends on the spirit. Most would probably see this as an employment opportunity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, nexus crawlers. They're not stable or reasonable, and are explicitly stated to act like self-aware disasters. They roll in, warp shit in strange and horrifying ways, and then leave. Also, a mage who calls one would have to roll Willpower to avoid fleeing, on account of their horrifying appearance, so the reception will probably go south in every kind of way.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:53:55-08:00","id":1036338,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So I have a question. Does Spirit 2 summon (as in make appear) spirits? Or does it call to them, to come if they want to. There is a very big difference here. I am genuinely curious how this works.<br /> <br /> With the Nexus Crawler example, I'd find it hard to believe that you could put out a call, and have one show up terribly fast, since they generally exist far removed from the Penumbra. I would imagine that if if were possible to have one appear, it would take a lot of successes to do so and thus (logically, to me) require a ritual casting. Or is my understanding of this off (it very well may be)?</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit 2 makes a &quot;call&quot; for nearby spirits. It's like yelling a &quot;Hey, you!. Yes, you, the tree spirit&quot; in the Umbra. I'm not sure of how big it's the area of effect, but I guess the more successes, the &quot;stronger&quot; it's your yelling.<br /> <br /> You need Correspondence 2 to call spirits that are very far. This works like Correspondence, so the number of successes needed depend on your connection with the spirit rather than the distance. Calling your Familiar from the other side of the universe may be easier than calling an unknown spirit in another city. You can call a given spirit only if you know something about the spirit, but you could also call a &quot;generic&quot; spirit.<br /> <br /> Spirit 4 compells the spirit to come and obey you (powerfull spirits are harder to compel, obviously, and may consider it rude)<br /> <br /> Neither of these effects make the spirit appear in front of you, they just call the spirit and inform it where you are.<br /> <br /> Correspondence 4 makes the spirit appear in front of you.<br /> <br /> So, yes, the Nexus Crawler example would have likely failed","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T16:58:36-08:00","id":1036342,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036332#post1036332\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;For each Mage player who thinks a mage is a omnipotent god there is crappy game-master who forgot half of the rules of the game&quot; (cit)</div> </div> </div> </div>Ha! So true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm a big Mage fan, but when one of my might-be-players-in-the-future, another big mage fan said that with corresp 1/forces/1 you could alter a flashlight's light into sunlight and sear vampires... I started to understand why people say mages are overpowered all the time...<br /> <br /> Alternately, there are the <i>other</i> game masters, who are convinced that mages are bonkers and start the chronicle with taking away all the hermetics' implements, just because. Happened with another friend and I worked hard since to convince him that no, not the game is shitty and mages are useless, it was his ST.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":6363,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","user":"PM\u00e1rk","date":". 01-22-2017, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:02:21-08:00","id":1036344,"title":"","content":"That happens because players don't read the damn rules!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <i>They should never get into fights with other supernatural creatures without proper preparation, should always avoid unnecessary fights with other supernatural creatures whenever possible, and should never fight fair against other supernatural creatures when they have to fight.</i><br /> <br /> <br /> Name a splat that's not true for. WoD practically runs on <a href=\"http://tvtropes.org/pmwiki/pmwiki.php/Main/AlwaysABiggerFish\" target=\"_blank\">Always a Bigger Fish</a>. Any given splat has its associated boogeymen, from the Methuselahs to the Earthbound to HIT Marks to accountants who <i>really</i> want to talk about their stamp collection.<br /> <br /> <b>The advice you gave is good no matter what sort of character facing whatever sort of opponent. Strike first, strike hard, strike again, and there is no such thing as overkill</b>.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. All supernaturals in WoD have dangerous skills. None should be taken for granted. <hr />It's fun how this turned from &quot;mages cannot win when they fight against <b>another supernatural</b> unprepared&quot; to &quot;mages cannot win when they fight <b>a werewolf</b> unprepared&quot;. The latter it's mostly true for almost any normal scenario. The former, less so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:15:35-08:00","id":1036346,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a> :<br /> <br /> To add to my previous post about calling and summoning:<br /> <br /> To summon a spirit to fight for you like a D&amp;D mage summons a fire elemental, you would need Spirit 4/Correspondence 4. This it's very hard because you need to control the spirit, and this demands a huge number of successes (not sure how many, but this it's usually a ritual), and then you would need more successes to teleport it where you are<br /> <br /> However, if you already had a pact with the fire elemental, it would be Spirit 2/ Correspondence 4, and much less successes because summoning someone you have a connection it's easier than summoning a random guy, and you wouldn't need to compell the elemental.<br /> <br /> Also, Spirit 4 can make the spirit appear in the material world if he can't Materialize (outlandish and vulgar, but quite awesome)<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 08:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:17:21-08:00","id":1036347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1035823#post1035823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or a Possessed can just turn off all of a Mage's magical effects for a few turns when they get to 100'. Oh, what can a Mage do when their Spheres are turned off for the three turns it takes for them to fall to their deaths? Nothing except flap their arms and hope that they remembered to pay their life insurance...</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit/DimSci 2 and Correspondence 2 device. Spirit magic no longer works on you. Laugh at the Possessed and Garou who try it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036187#post1036187\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">HDYDT has this covered (for good and ill) with the Correspondence table(use the entry with the weakest connection) plus 1 for each location plus 1 for indepedent movement(and HL) and 1 for Multitasking. (Everywhere at once Correspondence 4, Life 3, Mind 1) altough you still take damage if one of the copies gets killed: 1 HL agg damage. One Avatar is not so much of an issue, you can do 1 effect per round with your original self. Because of your high capability in Correspondence it is not really a problem you can not overcome (in fact it costs only 1 additional success to send your effect to anyplace one of your copies perceives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alternatively, use a cloning vat to clone yourself, creating new individuals who are exact clones of you. High level Mind to erase their mind, and then permanently possess them. And conjunctional Time/Mind to increase your mental actions per round by 1 for every clone so you can actually control them all. Add in Prime to consecrate them, and you are essentially a hivemind creature any one of which can use true magic. Sure, you need 1 extra success for one of the secondary units. To make the correspondence connection. But...<br /> <br /> Is this a pain in the ass? Yes. Totally.<br /> <br /> But it's also terrifyingly effective.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:19:07-08:00","id":1036348,"title":"","content":"<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036342#post1036342\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ha! So true. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I'm a big Mage fan, but when one of my might-be-players-in-the-future, another big mage fan said that with corresp 1/forces/1 you could alter a flashlight's light into sunlight and sear vampires... I started to understand why people say mages are overpowered all the time...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Oh but that is the least, mistaking the spheres you need is almost acceptable.<br /> <br /> For example: lot of people talks about prepping their mage with a lot of effects before the fight, and they forget the +1 difficult for every 2 effect on.<br /> If your mage is very well prepared trust me, in the middle of the fight he will not be able to cast even a boquet of flowers.<br /> <br /> Even more, they forget that if you cast a spell in the mid of a fight and you do not have weapons or fighting techniques as a focus that's fast casting (and saddly,not every mage is an Euthanatos or an Akashic), +1 to difficult, and if there are a lot of enemies and you lack a sensory effect running your mage is distracted, +1 to +3 difficult, if you want to turn air in willey pete, that's an outlandish feat, +1 to 3 again.<br /> <br /> And again, vital question: does your mage believes that he can do what he is doing? An Akashic mage does believe that air can be turned in willey pete just like that? Because if your mage is a Solificati maybe yes, but if you are a Virtual Adept, well, probably no.<br /> <br /> Or does your Virtual Adept believe that he can summon concrete out of nowhere to entrap a werewolf? Are you sure? Does your Syndicate mage believes that he can summon a Nexus Crawler? Even if Dimensional Science is almost a monopoly in the hands of the Void Engineers?<br /> <br /> Does people remember that long rituals requires stamina rolls? and that a botching a ritual is the harbinger of a mega-ton of raining shit?<br /> <br /> <br /> No, and too often this is caused by poor game masters who allow their players to just munchkin their way out without regards for rules and the lore of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-22-2017, 08:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:24:28-08:00","id":1036350,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036344#post1036344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That happens because players don't read the damn rules!</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, came to the same conclusion. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> This. All supernaturals in WoD have dangerous skills. None should be taken for granted. </div> </div> </div>Absolutely.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It's fun how this turned from &quot;mages cannot win when they fight against <b>another supernatural</b> unprepared&quot; to &quot;mages cannot win when they fight <b>a werewolf</b> unprepared&quot;. The latter it's mostly true for almost any normal scenario. The former, less so. </div> </div> </div>I suspect it's because it implied physical confrontation and werewolves are arguably the best at that as starting and &quot;mid-level&quot; characters. I might add that I think the same is true for Vampires, namely that an average mage unprepared have a distinct disadvantage against the average vampire physically. No-paradox, boosting stats, soaking lethal, half-bashing, aggravated bite damage and healing are no jokes. And that's before taking into account the physical disciplines, although most of the vampires would probably have some of them.<br /> <br /> Point in fact, I believe that werewolves are the best and vampires are second best in combat as starting characters and without preparation <i>in general</i>. Mages are behind both, without preparation and/or specific build. Changelings, I don't know, I'll wait C20. Mummies, Wraiths, no idea.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:28:34-08:00","id":1036353,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036347#post1036347\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Alternatively, use a cloning vat to clone yourself, creating new individuals who are exact clones of you. High level Mind to erase their mind, and then permanently possess them. And conjunctional Time/Mind to increase your mental actions per round by 1 for every clone so you can actually control them all. Add in Prime to consecrate them, and you are essentially a hivemind creature any one of which can use true magic. Sure, you need 1 extra success for one of the secondary units. To make the correspondence connection. But...<br /> <br /> Is this a pain in the ass? Yes. Totally.<br /> <br /> But it's also terrifyingly effective.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Sure, an easy task that would just require Life 5,Correspondence 5,Time 3,Prime 2,Mind 5, vulgar as hell.<br /> <br /> It involves so many high level spheres that neither Porthos or the Matriarch could pull that.<br /> <br /> <br /> And here's another thing, people forget how mages are built.<br /> <br /> Aside from the most powerful masters pre-storm, high spheres are not really common.<br /> <br /> The Matriarch, one of the most powerfull technocrat ever statted had Corr 5,Force 5, Life 3,Mind 4,Matter 4,Prime 4.<br /> <br /> Just two spheres at 5, no Entropy, no Spirit,no Time.<br /> <br /> <br /> Laughing Eagle, who was the Primus of the Dreamspeaker had Entropy 3, Force 2, Life 4,Mind 2,Matter 1, Prime 3, Spirit 5, Time 4.<br /> <br /> Mustai, one of the most powerfull masters of the Order of Hermes had Cor 3,Entropy 3,Force 5,Life 4,Matter 2,Mind 2,Prime 4,Spirit 3<br /> <br /> <br /> And we are speaking of pre-storm masters, and not the first masters of the bunch,but some of the strongest masters in the world.<br /> <br /> <br /> Amanda Peel, one of the highest ranking technocrats on earth after the storm had Arete 6, Corr 3,Force 5,Matter 4,Mind 5,Prime 4.<br /> Just 5 Spheres; no Life,no Entropy,no Dimensional Science, no Time<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> For some strange reasons people assume that mages will all be like Porthos and Voormas, that they will have all the nine spheres, and that they will be all at the same level and each one of them will be sky-high.<br /> <br /> Like if a Werewolf player or a Vampire player would assume that the average Werewolf or Vampire is the Night-Lord or Baba Yaga, more or less.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-22-2017, 08:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:36:14-08:00","id":1036357,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even more, they forget that if you cast a spell in the mid of a fight and you do not have weapons or fighting techniques as a focus that's fast casting (and saddly,not every mage is an Euthanatos or an Akashic), +1 to difficult, and if there are a lot of enemies and you lack a sensory effect running your mage is distracted, +1 to +3 difficult, if you want to turn air in willey pete, that's an outlandish feat, +1 to 3 again.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can also sidestep this if you have an Instrument prepared to cast the Rote. Like a fireball wand, or a raygun. As long as you use it to cast that rote, it's without penalty. But true, being a fighting mage who blends combat with magick (which isn't the same as being an Euthanatos or an Akashic), does give you a small edge if you get surprised.<br /> Another it's the &quot;Violence as a Focus&quot;, that allows you to cast magick at the same time you attack (effectively giving you an extra action), so, your &quot;doctor adventure&quot; can change the substance off his ether gloves to silver at the same time he gives his desperate blow, the last and only chance he has against the fearsome werewolf that he wasn't expecting! . Being in the Umbra also gives a small boost, as Coincident stuff it's less difficult to cast. But all in all, you want to be prepared (and this isn't only having two or three effects on you!) if you're going to fight against anything that can be dangerous.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-22-2017, 08:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:37:23-08:00","id":1036358,"title":"","content":"The only problem with that is the 'unprepared' thing. Every one of these threads just ASSUMES the Garou or Vamp get's the drop on the mage. In which case, yes. He dies.<br /> <br /> the chances of this are so low as to be highly improbable. The most common and easily used mage powers are sensory in effect and can do everything from giving you precognition, predator vision, distant viewing, mind reading, and so on.<br /> <br /> A mage with life 1 will be able to pick Garou and Vampire out of a crowd with trivial ease. And what reason do they have NOT to have it on all the time? Or at least most of the time. It's trivial to do. And from there, once they've identified them. Why not follow them a bit with correspondence 1.<br /> <br /> And when it comes time to kill them? A high powered silenced rifle enchanted with Prime 2 is going to dish out more damage in that particular fight than a werewolves claws and teeth will, because the werewolf will never see the shot coming. One minute all is fine and dandy and the next, they're bleeding out on the pavement, pattern shredded.<br /> <br /> THAT is a mages advantage. They don't have to get anywhere near you for you to be dead. They don't have to stand out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:43:48-08:00","id":1036362,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12892-kammerer\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar12892_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12892\" data-vbnamecard=\"12892\">Kammerer</a> and <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar1683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"1683\" data-vbnamecard=\"1683\">Aleph</a> thanks for the responses. Calling to Banes made enough sense. It was the idea of a Nexus Crawler being there that bothered me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:47:55-08:00","id":1036363,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036346#post1036346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar805_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"805\" data-vbnamecard=\"805\">idpersona</a> :<br /> <br /> To add to my previous post about calling and summoning:<br /> <br /> To summon a spirit to fight for you like a D&amp;D mage summons a fire elemental, you would need Spirit 4/Correspondence 4. This it's very hard because you need to control the spirit, and this demands a huge number of successes (not sure how many, but this it's usually a ritual), and then you would need more successes to teleport it where you are<br /> <br /> However, if you already had a pact with the fire elemental, it would be Spirit 2/ Correspondence 4, and much less successes because summoning someone you have a connection it's easier than summoning a random guy, and you wouldn't need to compell the elemental.<br /> <br /> Also, Spirit 4 can make the spirit appear in the material world if he can't Materialize (outlandish and vulgar, but quite awesome)</div> </div> </div> </div>How do you do that states clearly that spirit sphere with 5 + successes is enough to bring forth entities. If you've made a pact with a spirit, I assume you'd have it on speed dial, so you would probably have an easier time calling it.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:52:57-08:00","id":1036367,"title":"","content":"Sure, but you have to compell it too.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I suspect it's because it implied physical confrontation and werewolves are arguably the best at that as starting and &quot;mid-level&quot; characters. I might add that I think the same is true for Vampires, namely that an average mage unprepared have a distinct disadvantage against the average vampire physically. No-paradox, boosting stats, soaking lethal, half-bashing, aggravated bite damage and healing are no jokes. And that's before taking into account the physical disciplines, although most of the vampires would probably have some of them.<br /> <br /> Point in fact, I believe that werewolves are the best and vampires are second best in combat as starting characters and without preparation <i>in general</i>. Mages are behind both, without preparation and/or specific build. Changelings, I don't know, I'll wait C20. Mummies, Wraiths, no idea.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, but this thread wasn't about who is the strongest in a fair fight, it was about Mages being prey, because they're helpless against any supernatural when unprepared. Well, unprepared mages aren't more helpless than Imbued Hunters, and I see no one calling them Prey!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:56:21-08:00","id":1036371,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036358#post1036358\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The only problem with that is the 'unprepared' thing. Every one of these threads just ASSUMES the Garou or Vamp get's the drop on the mage. In which case, yes. He dies.<br /> <br /> the chances of this are so low as to be highly improbable. The most common and easily used mage powers are sensory in effect and can do everything from giving you precognition, predator vision, distant viewing, mind reading, and so on.<br /> <br /> A mage with life 1 will be able to pick Garou and Vampire out of a crowd with trivial ease. And what reason do they have NOT to have it on all the time? Or at least most of the time. It's trivial to do. And from there, once they've identified them. Why not follow them a bit with correspondence 1.<br /> <br /> And when it comes time to kill them? A high powered silenced rifle enchanted with Prime 2 is going to dish out more damage in that particular fight than a werewolves claws and teeth will, because the werewolf will never see the shot coming. One minute all is fine and dandy and the next, they're bleeding out on the pavement, pattern shredded.<br /> <br /> THAT is a mages advantage. They don't have to get anywhere near you for you to be dead. They don't have to stand out.</div> </div> </div> </div>The bullet has to be enchanted, not the rifle.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T17:56:31-08:00","id":1036372,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036367#post1036367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but you have to compell it too.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> I agree, but this thread wasn't about who is the strongest in a fair fight, it was about Mages being prey, because they're helpless against any supernatural when unprepared. Well, unprepared mages aren't more helpless than Imbued Hunters, and I see no one calling them Prey!</div> </div> </div> </div>Not sure why you'd need to compel a spirit you've made a pact with. The chiminage you offered for a specific duration of time (that's how I do my pacts) should be compelling enough.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:00:21-08:00","id":1036375,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036371#post1036371\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The bullet has to be enchanted, not the rifle.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the WEAPON has to be enchanted. Now, dependent on paradigm yes, maybe you would have to enchant the bullets individually.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:19:28-08:00","id":1036382,"title":"","content":"Nope, bullets have to be enchanted separately because otherwise you get a rifle that can do aggravated damage with the rifle butt and aggravated damage with the bullets (same thing with bows and arrows or slings and stones). It is the etheric form of the weapon that changes and deals aggravated damage. Since the damage is done by the bullet, and the etheric form of the bullets are unchanged, so the bullets do normal damage unless they are changed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-22-2017, 09:21 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:24:51-08:00","id":1036386,"title":"","content":"The damage bars go with the rifle, not the bullets. The bullets are PART of the rifle. An interchangeable part. But still.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:30:08-08:00","id":1036388,"title":"","content":"No, bullets are not part of a rifle because the bullets could be created after the rifle was enchanted. While the bullets in the rifle may be enchanted with the rifle during the first ritual, reloads would not be enchanted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T18:38:35-08:00","id":1036391,"title":"","content":"Mage 20<br /> <br /> Targeted Damage Effect<br /> Bruce Foster sights, aims, and shoots. A .44 Magnum slug<br /> tears into the raging man-beast that\u2019s been rampaging through<br /> the office complex. The monster sneers \u2013 Bullets? How pathetic<br /> \u2013 and then howls in realization that the special Technocratic<br /> ammo in Bruce\u2019s gun, combined with Bruce\u2019s Enlightened<br /> marksmanship, has unexpected, deadly consequences.<br /> \u201cThanks to our special ammo,\u201d says Bruce\u2019s player, Bill,<b> \u201cI\u2019m<br /> using the gun to throw a coincidental Forces/ Prime Effect into<br /> that lycanthropic bastard: Forces 2 for velocity and damage, and<br /> Prime 2 to energize my bullets so they do aggravated damage.\u201d</b><br /> Because this is a coincidental Effect, the difficulty is 5. (2 + 3 =<br /> 5) Bill rolls Bruce\u2019s Enlightenment of 4 to trigger the desired<br /> Effect. Four dice hit the table, scoring two successes.<br /> To see whether or not the gunshot hits, Bill rolls with<br /> Bruce\u2019s Dexterity + Firearms dice pool. Three successes. Bruce\u2019s<br /> gun can fire up to three shots per turn; because a player can<br /> make only one Arete/ Enlightenment roll per turn, however,<br /> the Effect roll applies the damage as the result of all three shots.<br /> Checking the Base Damage or Duration chart, Bill<br /> discovers that his two successes, plus one additional success<br /> for the Forces Sphere, equal six health levels\u2019 worth of damage.<br /> Because the Prime 2 addition enhanced that damage, the<br /> arrogant lupine who figured he could shake off that pistol shot<br /> suddenly takes a six health-level aggravated damage attack. Sure,<br /> the werewolf can try to soak that damage, but still \u2013 six agg in<br /> a single turn? That shit\u2019s gonna hurt. Suddenly, Wolfie\u2019s not<br /> quite as spry as he was a moment ago\u2026","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T19:08:38-08:00","id":1036397,"title":"","content":"Yes, the gun is the foci, and Bruce is energizing the bullets with the effect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T19:35:43-08:00","id":1036404,"title":"","content":"Ok, A.) M20's rules for how magic work are literally the dumbest thing I have ever in my life read. Aside from My Immortal. Don't use them. Ever.<br /> <br /> B.) Enchanting is an explicitly temporary effect there is no 'permanent enchanting'. How many bullets do you expect you ACTUALLY NEED. to kill a Garou? Given you're dishing out 8+ agg damage per shot?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-22T23:54:57-08:00","id":1036471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036367#post1036367\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I agree, but this thread wasn't about who is the strongest in a fair fight, it was about Mages being prey, because they're helpless against any supernatural when unprepared. Well, unprepared mages aren't more helpless than Imbued Hunters, and I see no one calling them Prey!</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, aside from the old Predator and Prey novel line, but it had a metis Garou knocking up an Imbued, so it can stay out in the cold with the sign around its neck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T01:04:49-08:00","id":1036489,"title":"","content":"When you're a supernatural creature, the difference between a normal thug with a normal gun and amunition, and a mage thug with a normal gun and amunition, it's that the mage thug might be able to deliver enough levels of Aggravated damage with it as to turn a vampire into ash in a single shot, while the normal thug it's going to be delivering Lethal dice (Contundent, and halved, if you're a vampire. Quite a difference for the leeches).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T03:06:44-08:00","id":1036513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036295#post1036295\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Spirit 2 calls, it does not summon, and major spirits like Nexus Crawlers do not respond to Spirit 2 calls. And the type of banes that respond to a Spirit 2 call cannot control Nexus Crawlers, that requires Incarna levels of power. Your ST was just being kind.</div> </div> </div> </div>I didn't called for a Nexus Crawler or anything like it. I just called for &quot;Entropic Entities&quot; and took my time to pool many successes.<br /> <br /> I didn't control the Nexus Crawler either; I simply summoned the banes closer to were the Garou were rather than where I was... Or do you think I'm stupid enough to summon a group of banes at my feet?<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 can call ANY KIND OF SPIRITS, even <b>Incarna</b> level; the truth is, that's up to the ST, who will determine the number of successes needed and if the spirits will answer.<br /> <br /> The description of Spirit 2 makes it clear that most of the time, SOMETHING answers. And yes, it is a SUMMONING, in the sense that makes spirits show up, even if only out of curiosity. So, I just called entropic spirits and did it with too much strenght; the fact is, the other banes were more than enough to kill the Garou, but the ST simply said that a Nexus showed too (it were a &quot;random encounter&quot; with the Nexus, I didn't called one), and if he saw me, I'm sure I would die, but he didn't, he saw the Garou (which is why I didn't summon the banes at my feet).<br /> <br /> The ST could have said in the ocasion &quot;sorry, nothing happens. No answe&quot;, and I wouldn't complain if I were in a green glade close to the Garou Caern, were there are almost no Wyrm spirits... But in a dark corner of a rough neighborhood of a big city, that would be ridiculous. So, he made it to be that about a dozen wyrm things showed, which is not beyond plausible in such a scenario, and randonmly between all those there was a Nexus.<br /> <br /> Some banes saw me in the trash hidding while the Nexus were busy and came to me, so I made them many empt promisses and that was the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> Now, can you stop trying to make &quot;holes&quot; on all of that scene just to show how tough invincible modafuqs Garou are?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:02:42-08:00","id":1036543,"title":"","content":"Anything would die against a Nexus Crawler, and they are challenging enemies for the defenders of Garou Caerns. It is a bit like saving that Garou are not so tough because nuclear weapons can take them out.<br /> <br /> As for Mages turning vampires to ash, let us examine that for a moment. We will use Revised because Revised is more available to the members of the forum. In Revised, using Prime 2 to make bullets do aggravated damage is usually a vulgar effect, meaning that it is difficulty 6. The effect is the equivalent to setting someone on fire in impressiveness (they both deal aggravated damage), so it requires a minimum of four successes. Each bullet (and it is the bullet that deals the damage, not the gun, so the bullets need to be charged) affected is a different Pattern, so you need one additional success per bullet charged, so a six round revolver would need 9 successes, plus one for the charge to last for the scene. So you are talking about a 10 success effect to have a revolver doing aggravated damage to vampires for one scene (generous STs will let you charge the revolver instead, but charging with revolver would only allow you to pistol whip someone for aggravated damage by RAW).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-23-2017, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T05:33:02-08:00","id":1036556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036513#post1036513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't called for a Nexus Crawler or anything like it. I just called for &amp;quot;Entropic Entities&amp;quot; and took my time to pool many successes.<br /> <br /> I didn't control the Nexus Crawler either; I simply summoned the banes closer to were the Garou were rather than where I was... Or do you think I'm stupid enough to summon a group of banes at my feet?<br /> <br /> Spirit 2 can call ANY KIND OF SPIRITS, even <b>Incarna</b> level; the truth is, that's up to the ST, who will determine the number of successes needed and if the spirits will answer.<br /> <br /> The description of Spirit 2 makes it clear that most of the time, SOMETHING answers. And yes, it is a SUMMONING, in the sense that makes spirits show up, even if only out of curiosity. So, I just called entropic spirits and did it with too much strenght; the fact is, the other banes were more than enough to kill the Garou, but the ST simply said that a Nexus showed too (it were a &amp;quot;random encounter&amp;quot; with the Nexus, I didn't called one), and if he saw me, I'm sure I would die, but he didn't, he saw the Garou (which is why I didn't summon the banes at my feet).<br /> <br /> The ST could have said in the ocasion &amp;quot;sorry, nothing happens. No answe&amp;quot;, and I wouldn't complain if I were in a green glade close to the Garou Caern, were there are almost no Wyrm spirits... But in a dark corner of a rough neighborhood of a big city, that would be ridiculous. So, he made it to be that about a dozen wyrm things showed, which is not beyond plausible in such a scenario, and randonmly between all those there was a Nexus.<br /> <br /> Some banes saw me in the trash hidding while the Nexus were busy and came to me, so I made them many empt promisses and that was the end of the scene.<br /> <br /> Now, can you stop trying to make &amp;quot;holes&amp;quot; on all of that scene just to show how tough invincible modafuqs Garou are?</div> </div> </div> </div>What charms did the banes have?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:34:13-08:00","id":1036577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mages turning vampires to ash, let us examine that for a moment.</div> </div> </div> </div>Let's do this thing.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> We will use Revised because Revised is more available to the members of the forum. </div> </div> </div>A false argument. Since the rules of M20 were clearly exemplified, you have no reason to argue that we're &quot;unfamiliar&quot; with them. They're up there, quoted of the book by Undead rabbit!<br /> <br /> But let's use revised. Not because it's more &quot;familiar&quot;, but because the example speaks for itself about how dangerous are M20 mages.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In Revised, using Prime 2 to make bullets do aggravated damage is usually a vulgar effect, meaning that it is difficulty 6. </div> </div> </div>Why? Bullets are supposed to kill people, nothing suggests that making a bullet do Aggravated it's vulgar. Healing and resisting aggravated it's vulgar, but causing it? Nah.<br /> Meaning that it's difficulty 5. 4 if you'r weapon it's a specialized Focus.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The effect is the equivalent to setting someone on fire in impressiveness (they both deal aggravated damage), so it requires a minimum of four successes. </div> </div> </div>Debatable, bullets are supposed to kill people, fire isn't supposed to appear from nowhere. 3 Successes should be enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Each bullet (and it is the bullet that deals the damage, not the gun, so the bullets need to be charged) affected is a different Pattern, so you need one additional success per bullet charged, so a six round revolver would need 9 successes, plus one for the charge to last for the scene. </div> </div> </div>Unless you're surronded by vampires, you probably don't want more than one or two bullets. Vampires don't hunt in packs.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> So you are talking about a 10 success effect to have a revolver doing aggravated damage to vampires for one scene (generous STs will let you charge the revolver instead, but charging with revolver would only allow you to pistol whip someone for aggravated damage by RAW). </div> </div> </div>In my previous example I was clearly referring to the example up there by Undead rabbit that it's copied as it is from M20...you're taking what I said out of context.<br /> <br /> But let's change the example to a different mage, this thug that isn't very well prepared uses the rules of Revised. Instead of using an enchanted bullet (which exploits various rules of M20), he can launch an energy ball (Prime 2). It's difficulty 6, unless the vampire it's attacking in public, which it's unlikely, and each success it's 2 Aggravated. You just need to accrue 3 successes at dif. 6 (maybe less, maybe more, dependant on foci and stuff) to Incapacitate the vampire if he hasn't Fortitude. If we spend a Willpower pont and all the Quintessence we can, this it's well whitin the realm of possibility for a mage.<br /> Even 2 successes, while not enough to win the fight, should be enough for the vampire to reconsider hunting Mages. 4 aggravated need 20 blood points to heal, more than what you bargained for.<br /> <br /> A normal mage can be dangerous to a normal vampire, even unprepared. Dangerous, not &quot;stronger&quot;. It's not the same. You're just denying the obvious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:40 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:44:07-08:00","id":1036583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036543#post1036543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything would die against a Nexus Crawler, and they are challenging enemies for the defenders of Garou Caerns. It is a bit like saving that Garou are not so tough because nuclear weapons can take them out.<br /> <br /> As for Mages turning vampires to ash, let us examine that for a moment. We will use Revised because Revised is more available to the members of the forum. In Revised, using Prime 2 to make bullets do aggravated damage is usually a vulgar effect, meaning that it is difficulty 6. The effect is the equivalent to setting someone on fire in impressiveness (they both deal aggravated damage), so it requires a minimum of four successes. Each bullet (and it is the bullet that deals the damage, not the gun, so the bullets need to be charged) affected is a different Pattern, so you need one additional success per bullet charged, so a six round revolver would need 9 successes, plus one for the charge to last for the scene. So you are talking about a 10 success effect to have a revolver doing aggravated damage to vampires for one scene (generous STs will let you charge the revolver instead, but charging with revolver would only allow you to pistol whip someone for aggravated damage by RAW).</div> </div> </div> </div>Careful there, buddy. If you're going to arbitrarily reference previous editions to make Mages weaker than they are in M20, you open yourself up to lawnchairs if a person feels like doing the same thing and arbitrarily referencing 1E. Or if you don't want to go that far back, if we're talking Sorcerer's Crusade or 2E mages slinging Forces+Prime fireballs, let's remember that additional successes multiply the damage done. Oh, and plus one for forces.<br /> <br /> Direct Pattern Damage isn't the only way to ash a vampire, lest we forget. Flamethrowers deal 8 damage (World of Darkness: Combat page 109) and can be brought in to the equation with a little bit of Correspondence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":1515,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","user":"BenjCano","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:47 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T06:44:11-08:00","id":1036584,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036556#post1036556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What charms did the banes have?</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't matter. He/she doesn't seem to want to discuss it, because asking any questions about the scene seems (to them) to be trying to make holes in their scene to prove how awesome Garou are. Even is nobody has taken that stance.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, the simplest way out would have been for the Garou to just leave the Umbra and disappear into the city. I don't know why a Garou would stand around while a dozen Banes (including a Nexus Crawler for precisely no reason) wandered up to see what called them.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:10:37-08:00","id":1036633,"title":"","content":"Or just turned into a wolf and run off. At 70 yards per turn, it would be traveling faster than most banes, and the banes would likely target the next thing around (the Mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T08:52:25-08:00","id":1036664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> They should never get into fights with other supernatural creatures without proper preparation, should always avoid unnecessary fights with other supernatural creatures whenever possible, and should never fight fair against other supernatural creatures when they have to fight. </div> </div> </div> As someone else said (in all these pages), I feel like this statement generally holds true of most splats. Any amount of combat between different supernaturals vary so much that any hypothetical presented will typically be flawed due to some advantage given to one side or the other. At least when it comes to Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage (I'm a lot less sure of the other lines), they all typically possess some powers that can waste someone who isn't prepared. Arguably mages can benefit the most from preparation and what they can do with their powers. There really isn't much even footing in fights because the element of surprise is so utterly massive in the game. And being aware of who/what your enemy is also matters so much. But the generalization of 'mages are prey' is entirely too situational to make. I typically dislike any situation where one side just knows someone else is a Mage, Werewolf, Vampire beforehand anyway.<br /> <br /> Even Karl's situation takes a lot for granted. Numerous things could have gone differently that results in him being dead. But noting all those things isn't necessarily productive because the permutations are countless. The scenario is neither here nor there in the discussion.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:48:49-08:00","id":1036746,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036556#post1036556\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What charms did the banes have?</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't important for the scene. Since you all need to know, I'll explain bellow.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036543#post1036543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anything would die against a Nexus Crawler, and they are challenging enemies for the defenders of Garou Caerns. It is a bit like saving that Garou are not so tough because nuclear weapons can take them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>If one looks upon all that has been said here, we basically have many WtA players that are basically stating they could waste any Mage if they sprang a trap on them, because, you know, puny Mages. I never said the Garou waiting for me were a pathetic thing; on the contrary, exactly why I considered him a major threath is the reason why I took such desperate measures. My point was to show, in a real gameplay case, that Mages are not defenseless weaklings as WtA think they are, and in fact, are extremely dangerous. I bet that Garou NPC thought exactly that way, that I would be easy prey. I just proved him how dangerous it is to make such an assumption.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036543#post1036543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for Mages turning vampires to ash, let us examine that for a moment. We will use Revised because Revised is more available to the members of the forum. In Revised, using Prime 2 to make bullets do aggravated damage is usually a vulgar effect, meaning that it is difficulty 6. The effect is the equivalent to setting someone on fire in impressiveness (they both deal aggravated damage), so it requires a minimum of four successes. Each bullet (and it is the bullet that deals the damage, not the gun, so the bullets need to be charged) affected is a different Pattern, so you need one additional success per bullet charged, so a six round revolver would need 9 successes, plus one for the charge to last for the scene. So you are talking about a 10 success effect to have a revolver doing aggravated damage to vampires for one scene (generous STs will let you charge the revolver instead, but charging with revolver would only allow you to pistol whip someone for aggravated damage by RAW).</div> </div> </div> </div>Wrong. You only need one success per bullet, and you don't need no successes for extended duration (at least I think you'll be using them to shoot your target... So... No need for more than one round duration). So, each success will enchant one bullet. Period. That's enough to kill most vampires or werewolves (unless you're very unluck).<br /> <br /> Plus... Why would enchanting the bullets be Vulgar? You're not enchanting your gloves to make your punches explode the enemy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T11:59:50-08:00","id":1036756,"title":"","content":"<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> :<br /> Aya Tari it's using Revised rules. They're different to what you seem to use, and more or less adjust to what Aya Tari stated in terms of successes, to my knowledge, altrough I think some points are debatable.<br /> Revised has, arguably, the weakest mages (in terms of instant power) of all the editions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-23-2017, 03:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:39:11-08:00","id":1036771,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036584#post1036584\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It doesn't matter. He/she doesn't seem to want to discuss it, because asking any questions about the scene seems (to them) to be trying to make holes in their scene to prove how awesome Garou are. Even is nobody has taken that stance.<br /> <br /> In all honesty, the simplest way out would have been for the Garou to just leave the Umbra and disappear into the city. I don't know why a Garou would stand around while a dozen Banes (including a Nexus Crawler for precisely no reason) wandered up to see what called them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ok, since it is THAT important, I'll give all the backstage's info<br /> <br /> First of all, my char have a always on &quot;Lucky Aura&quot; on him, with Entropy 2. Did I told you he were a Void Engeneer? Ok, so some explanation is in order here, since an effect with that name would seem impossible...<br /> <br /> So, that's how it works: first of all, the VE char has the flaw &quot;Pink Glasses&quot;, I don't know the exactly name in english, but he believes the Union to be the most perfect, autruistic and ethical organization in the world; anything other than that is just &quot;a few bad apples&quot; (damn traitors that should be lobotomized and sent to make to serve as mindless slaves and primal batteries), and he is the kind that would deliver his own mother to Control for conditioning if she went of trails... For her own good.<br /> <br /> Other than that, he has a high self-confidence, born from the fact that he believes himself to be part of the elite (an Enlightened person) amongst the elite (the Union, the best of the best).<br /> <br /> With all that, he believes himself... Destined for great deads. He doesn't have any of those mystic views of Fortune or Fate, mind you, those bygone ideas from cavemen are just silly supersticions from those damn pesks of the traditions that have no place in the bright Utopia of the Union. No, it's ratter a HUGE sense of self importance (Hubris some traditionalists would call... But who cares what they think right?).<br /> <br /> In his dreams, he is always the brave hero, saving the day with all his awesome skills and wits, having the divine might of the Union behind him backing him up. While he is having those dreams, destiny really seems to answer - that's basically a ritual of Entropy 2 to give him &quot;good luck&quot; for the day. That effect works as the &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; disadvantage for him, so, he doesn't know what he is doing actually, only that he is a luck person... His luck strenghten his convictions, which is the &quot;fuel&quot; for his &quot;luck&quot;.<br /> <br /> He does have an idea that his dreams may have something to do with the odds he have; he is a student of parapsychology, and study the effects of brainwaves on quantum fluctuations, so he knows how effective is to have an attuned mind, so he is always registering his brain waves for study purposes... Now, he is on the verge of a breakthrow on the study of the influence of psychic emanations on entropic events, and thus would be able to replace the need for random events caused by his dreams, to be able to manipulate randomness by inducing the right psychic brainwaves with eletromagnetic inductors.<br /> <br /> However, for know, he needs a good night sleeping. For the entire day, he will have a &quot;luck pool&quot;, automatic successes, or random luck events. The ST however, is the one that keep track of those and how to spend them, since my char &quot;cast&quot; that effect subconscious (like the Sleepwalker flaw, but only for that effect). The ST also makes all the roles of Arete (1 roll for every hour of sleep), and keep a track of the successes but didn't inform me of how big were my pool; the ST only gave hints, based on how &quot;epic&quot; my actions were on my dreams.<br /> <br /> So, the better the dreams I had on the previous night, the more confident on my success I would feel.<br /> <br /> I also knew that, when I had dreams filled with nightmares, the best thing to do would be calling in sick for the day... And if Paradox kicked, I would do go to use my NOM friend's drugs to \u00ednduce a dreamless sleep for a few days, until I can recover my self confidence back.<br /> <br /> That's also one of the worse weaknesses of my char... Do you wanna make him suffer? Use Mind 3 to see his dreams of the night, and make him see those dreams again while awake, but this time, twist things a bit... Since it's not a concious effect, it would probably turn my luck aura into unluckness for him... And would also crush his confidence.<br /> <br /> So... Why did a Nexus Crawler showed up?<br /> <br /> Because Im a luck bastard.<br /> <br /> Why didn't he come for me?<br /> <br /> Because Im a luck bastard.<br /> <br /> Two of the banes noticed me, and came to talk. Why didn't they attack me? I don't know... Luck perhaps? So, I promossed<br /> <br /> I don't know what happened to the Garou and the Nexus, I didn't stick around to check, all that I know is that my importance in the big scheme of things were reassured, as always. If the Garou escaped or not, I don't know, I didn't know him, and I believe he didn't know me (it was kind of a &quot;jump on the first that gets out of the compound&quot; situation). <br /> <br /> Some days later, some entropic beings came looking for me, to &quot;collect my debts&quot;. This time I was well prepared (what a luck to have gained a blaster pistol that same day!), so, I gave them the quintessence I had promissed, just not in the way they were expecting.<br /> <br /> Of course I had to report all that to my superiors (a good agent have nothing to fear, and must accept any correction that is due for misbehavior, after all), and I knew that would be a problem in my otherwise prestine curriculum, but that's life, it would only serve as a stimuli for me to be even better.<br /> <br /> But, since I'm such a luck bastard... My files would never have that bad notes... Just a few days after those events, and after I finished my absolutely precise report, some big shot sindic from the Special Projects Division with huge assets on some Pentex conglomerate, took great interest in my works with psychism, and decided to offer me his patronage...<br /> <br /> So, I'm truly a VERY luck bastard indeed, and some big shot of the Union have finally seem my potential, as I knew it would...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:43:06-08:00","id":1036775,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036664#post1036664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Even Karl's situation takes a lot for granted. Numerous things could have gone differently that results in him being dead. But noting all those things isn't necessarily productive because the permutations are countless. The scenario is neither here nor there in the discussion.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was Luck (with capital &quot;L&quot;)<br /> <br /> Which is why I love Entropy","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T12:47:16-08:00","id":1036778,"title":"","content":"You know, if someone's lucky, you;d think that just about any other spirit but a nexus crawler would show up. War spiders, astral manifestations of square-jawed heroes... a nexus crawler is like being so lucky that you the place you're in gets ripped through by an F5 tornado. And then we all read the statement sideways, but low and behold, we didn't miss anything, it's still there, and it still makes no sense.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:35:27-08:00","id":1036799,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036746#post1036746\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If one looks upon all that has been said here, we basically have many WtA players that are basically stating they could waste any Mage if they sprang a trap on them, because, you know, puny Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div> No, we just have you playing the victim again. Who are these MANY WtA in this thread saying this? All Saurs was saying is that the situation isn't so cut and dry as present. Aya is making odd claims, but that's normal (no offense). But that's not MANY people.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> It was Luck (with capital &quot;L&quot;)<br /> <br /> Which is why I love Entropy </div> </div> </div> Not really. Your ST was being extremely generous on various points. I'm not necessarily saying you should have failed. Just that we have a highly, highly situational example that doesn't really matter here. The more you explain, the more it just reads as ST fiat to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T13:47:53-08:00","id":1036812,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036771#post1036771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Ok, since it is THAT important, I'll give all the backstage's info</div> </div> </div> </div>It wasn't (to me at least). The only thing I questioned was the presence of a Nexus Crawler. But now that you've elaborated, I do have another question. Again, I'm less familiar with Mage than Vampire or Werewolf, so maybe I'm misunderstanding how the system works.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036771#post1036771\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> In his dreams, he is always the brave hero, saving the day with all his awesome skills and wits, having the divine might of the Union behind him backing him up. While he is having those dreams, destiny really seems to answer - that's basically a ritual of Entropy 2 to give him &quot;good luck&quot; for the day. That effect works as the &quot;Sleepwalker&quot; disadvantage for him, so, he doesn't know what he is doing actually, only that he is a luck person... His luck strenghten his convictions, which is the &quot;fuel&quot; for his &quot;luck&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>So while asleep, he gets a free 8 hour of Ritual casting of a luck aura (Entropy 2) because? I don't understand why this is being compared to a flaw, when it seems entirely broken system-wise.<br /> <br /> <br /> Back on the Nexus Crawler thing. Best explanation I can understand is that your ST didn't understand what they actually are and wanted to throw one in there for &quot;cool factor&quot;. Doesn't have it make any more sense, but at least that's a reason. And questioning a Nexus Crawler being there has nothing to do with the power level of Garou. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a>, I don't necessarily understand why you have such a problem with Werewolf players. In my experience there is a ton of overlap between people who play the various games. And again, in my experience (and this is solely speaking for myself) it usually isn't Garou being proclaimed the most powerful/unbeatable beings in the WoD. They tend to get undersold on these forums more often than not.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036664#post1036664\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> As someone else said (in all these pages), I feel like this statement generally holds true of most splats. Any amount of combat between different supernaturals vary so much that any hypothetical presented will typically be flawed due to some advantage given to one side or the other. At least when it comes to Vampire, Werewolf, and Mage (I'm a lot less sure of the other lines), they all typically possess some powers that can waste someone who isn't prepared. Arguably mages can benefit the most from preparation and what they can do with their powers. There really isn't much even footing in fights because the element of surprise is so utterly massive in the game. And being aware of who/what your enemy is also matters so much. But the generalization of 'mages are prey' is entirely too situational to make. I typically dislike any situation where one side just knows someone else is a Mage, Werewolf, Vampire beforehand anyway.</div> </div> </div> </div>If only I could like this post more than once.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:21:34-08:00","id":1036831,"title":"","content":"Wouldn't dream casting a ritual violate the basic paradigm of the VE? There is no technology to use for foci and, quite frankly, I am really skeptical about allowing characters to cast effects that affect the real world in their dreams. It is not only the potential game balance violations, but the potential scenario of anyone with Forces 3+ casting effects that affect the real world while experiencing a nightmare.<br /> <br /> I think Garou tend to be used a default in these scenarios because they are the most powerful beginning characters. Experienced vampires can usually take on individual Garou without that much danger (especially if they are combat build, an experienced vampire with Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Celerity 5, Potence 5, Athletics 5, Melee 5, and a couple of silver knives will likely have a Garou pelt before the end of the second turn), the danger for them comes from the fact that Garou travel in packs. Prepared beginning mages can usually do the same.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:25:13-08:00","id":1036835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036831#post1036831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't dream casting a ritual violate the basic paradigm of the VE? There is no technology to use for foci and, quite frankly, I am really skeptical about allowing characters to cast effects that affect the real world in their dreams. It is not only the potential game balance violations, but the potential scenario of anyone with Forces 3+ casting effects that affect the real world while experiencing a nightmare.<br /> <br /> I think Garou tend to be used a default in these scenarios because they are the most powerful beginning characters. Experienced vampires can usually take on individual Garou without that much danger (especially if they are combat build, an experienced vampire with Strength 5, Dexterity 5, Celerity 5, Potence 5, Athletics 5, Melee 5, and a couple of silver knives will likely have a Garou pelt before the end of the second turn.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you discount every Gift, sure. Spirit of the Fray and Sense Silver go a long way toward improving longevity.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:30:12-08:00","id":1036840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036812#post1036812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It wasn't (to me at least). The only thing I questioned was the presence of a Nexus Crawler. But now that you've elaborated, I do have another question. Again, I'm less familiar with Mage than Vampire or Werewolf, so maybe I'm misunderstanding how the system works.<br /> <br /> Back on the Nexus Crawler thing. Best explanation I can understand is that your ST didn't understand what they actually are and wanted to throw one in there for <b>&quot;cool factor&quot; </b>;. Doesn't have it make any more sense, but at least that's a reason. And questioning a Nexus Crawler being there has nothing to do with the power level of Garou.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I see why everybody got so fixated in that, ok, now I get it... Yes, it were just random cinematics, nothing to do with anything of importance really... It were more like &quot;something big shows up&quot;, that's all. The final outcome wasn't really important at all, just what would come next.<br /> <br /> Just consider that I am, most of the times, in the right place, at the right moment. Why didn't the Nexus (or some other similar bad thing) showed looking at me? Well, because I have an Entropy 2 effect always on that gives me good fortune... That good fortune makes the signal turn red just after I cross a street in high speed, making my persecutors crash, is the reason why that group of Eutanathoi assassin take the wrong turn when persecuting me (thou, I have to admit that I hate those demented bastards, because they can truly interfere with my higher status with their unnatural abilities) or why I can make that luck shot once in a while.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036812#post1036812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So while asleep, he gets a free 8 hour of Ritual casting of a luck aura (Entropy 2) because? I don't understand why this is being compared to a flaw, when it seems entirely broken system-wise.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's not a flaw, because the flaw <i>Sleepwalker </i> means that you can't use effects AT ALL; you don't believe you are &quot;Awake&quot;, and don't think you are the reason of those &quot;weird coincidences&quot;; you pray for God to help you... It was just a miracle that some explosion killed the Bad guys, but that had nothing to do with you.<br /> <br /> My guy had this as a sort of a quirk, not exactly a flaw that would give freebie points, and only for Entropy 2, and that is so as part of his paradigm.<br /> <br /> And if you think the system is broken... When, as a matter of fact, all that were a sort of &quot;self inflicted&quot; restriction, to make the char concept cooler. I could just say that I had a quantum computer that make &quot;subatomic adjustments&quot; based on a series of chaos maths, that would let me do exactly the same thing and just a few rounds of a ritual... Besides, I would be able to CONTROL the outcome of the result (I let that to the ST). Or a Hermetic could give luck/misfortune with just a small gesture, and directing that towards any event he wanted. So, if we consider RAW, I was in fact DEBBUFFING my char on purpose, for the sake of role playing (and if the Mage players can't learn how to do that, the ST will have to)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-23-2017, 08:28 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T14:44:56-08:00","id":1036852,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036756#post1036756\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> :<br /> Revised has, arguably, the weakest mages (in terms of instant power) of all the editions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I love a lot of the revised material, but as far as the magic rules go, I'm happy we got M20. It's good to have, in a game about magic and mages to have characters, who can actually do magic, even the fireworks sometimes.<br /> <br /> And despite the more harsh casting rules, revised books have some ridiculous spells in them.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:08:59-08:00","id":1036860,"title":"","content":"So, as it came up in the other thread, what could you do against the jam technology ww gift? I'm not speaking about making it useless or invalid by saying it somehow doesn't apply to technomagic implements and HIT Marks and the usual stuff. Let's assume it does. Let's assume the Technocracy sent in the first row of HIT marks and black suits and the resident garous laughed at that, jammed them and tear them into shreds. What now? How the technos could prevent it in the second row? Some sort of active anti-magic field generator? Aside from ridiculous amounts of primium, how could you make your agents' life a little bit safer if a region have constant garou problems? After a few encounters you'd likely have reports about that gift, because it's fairly low-level and common, so it's plausible that the R&amp;D guys and girls would work hard to counter it. <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not speaking about invalidating the gift. The goal is, if we're assuming it works really that well against technomagic stuff, to make said stuff a bit more resilient to the gift, with a system that needs resources, or could work only for a limited time, or need someone to maintain, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:18:36-08:00","id":1036863,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036831#post1036831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wouldn't dream casting a ritual violate the basic paradigm of the VE? There is no technology to use for foci and, quite frankly, I am really skeptical about allowing characters to cast effects that affect the real world in their dreams. It is not only the potential game balance violations, but the potential scenario of anyone with Forces 3+ casting effects that affect the real world while experiencing a nightmare.</div> </div> </div> </div>It doesn't violete the paradigm of the VE... Look, he doesn't believe he is casting ANYTHING AT ALL. He just have an absolutely conviction that he is special... And reality seems to agree on that (except on those nasty situations that it doesn't. Better stay in the lab on those bad days).<br /> In his paradigm, <b><i>he is special</i></b>... In fact, paradox for him is having unluckness! Being just ordinary is what would REALLY contradict his paradigm. That's why it works <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> As for dream-casting, that's a lot more common than you think. Many Ecstatics DO THAT ALL THE TIME. That's in fact, a <b>very common foci</b> for many effects. The Akashas learn to use Mind to control their dreams, and they can cast effects with no trouble while at it. Ecstatics use dream casting for Time divinations and Correspondence far scry, and the <b>Dream</b>speakers also use dream-casting on many spiritual effects, just to name the most common ones<br /> <br /> Now, the question here is: does your paradigm allows you to use dreams and sleep as foci? Your hermetic may dream he is sending thousands of fireballs on angry hordes of zumbies, but if he doesn't believe he can use dreams to make fireballs, you don't have to worry about being carbonizing by sleeping in the same room as him.<br /> <br /> Effects don't just come &quot;by accident&quot;... The only exceptions would be wild effects during the awakening, maybe on rare ocasions during epiphamies, or if the Mage is a suffering a Silence or is a Marauder. You won't risk turning someone into a stone because you had an espasm caused by a heart attack or something similar (again, unless you're a Marauder). So, when an Ecstatic go to sleep to try to see the future, he is focusing his mind into the desired effect, not just randomly letting his wild dreams starting shooting time distortions all around. I mean, he COULD send a lot of wild time distortions at random <i>in theory</i>. But, if he's paradigm only accounts for Time 2 effects while sleeping, than that's what he gets... And why doesn't the effect just go random? (since dreams are just weird). <b>Because he doesn't believe that </b>. He believes that, chanting the right chanties before sleep will let you see the future, so THAT'S IT. A botche would be seeing as bad concentration before going to bed (which could in turn give the Mage nightmares - or bad omens, again, that's paradigm based)<br /> <br /> By the same principle, my VE thinks he is special, and that his sleep reinforce his convictions and make his mind and sense's sharpen. He doesn't see the resultados as &quot;magik&quot;, but ratter as the result of intensive training, wits, and a self esteem that borderline supersticious believe in &quot;Divine Fate&quot; that gives him an undermining resolution. The fact that reality seems to bend over to adjust to his needs, just reassure his special position on the universe... <br /> <br /> Note that, while that effect can have a potential for be a game breaker (and I admit it, which is why a let it totally in the hands of the ST), it is ABSOLUTELY COINCIDENTAL... My VE simply doesn't see anything that could be breaking his paradigm<br /> <br /> So... He is luck, because he believes he MUST be luck, and he believes he MUST be luck because he IS, in the pratical sense, a luck bastard. Chiken and egg...<br /> <br /> That guy is, of course, just one bad backlash away from plumbing in a very interesting Quiet...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:27:47-08:00","id":1036866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036860#post1036860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as it came up in the other thread, what could you do against the jam technology ww gift? I'm not speaking about making it useless or invalid by saying it somehow doesn't apply to technomagic implements and HIT Marks and the usual stuff. Let's assume it does. Let's assume the Technocracy sent in the first row of HIT marks and black suits and the resident garous laughed at that, jammed them and tear them into shreds. What now? How the technos could prevent it in the second row? Some sort of active anti-magic field generator? Aside from ridiculous amounts of primium, how could you make your agents' life a little bit safer if a region have constant garou problems? After a few encounters you'd likely have reports about that gift, because it's fairly low-level and common, so it's plausible that the R&amp;D guys and girls would work hard to counter it. <br /> <br /> Again, I'm not speaking about invalidating the gift. The goal is, if we're assuming it works really that well against technomagic stuff, to make said stuff a bit more resilient to the gift, with a system that needs resources, or could work only for a limited time, or need someone to maintain, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ridiculous amounts of Primium<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> Send every Iterator home... Go rest a little guys...<br /> <br /> We need a Progenitor team here ASAP, we have a code-wolf situation and need specialized teams for extraction, over... Tell them to send all the Victors they have stored with the best gengenieered traits... Say what? No, no cyborgs, I told you before, it's a code WOLF situation... Yes yes, the Prime enhanced too... And the experentals, yes yes... <br /> <br /> Have you ever played StarCraft?<br /> <br /> Now, I want you to think on ZERGS<br /> <br /> If that fails, just call for an Ion Cannon burst from a satellitte in orbit (that should be the lest option if you are trying to take a Caern, because you'll want to let the Caern intact for future sanitization)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:36:32-08:00","id":1036868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036860#post1036860\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, as it came up in the other thread, what could you do against the jam technology ww gift? I'm not speaking about making it useless or invalid by saying it somehow doesn't apply to technomagic implements and HIT Marks and the usual stuff. Let's assume it does. Let's assume the Technocracy sent in the first row of HIT marks and black suits and the resident garous laughed at that, jammed them and tear them into shreds. What now? How the technos could prevent it in the second row? Some sort of active anti-magic field generator? Aside from ridiculous amounts of primium, how could you make your agents' life a little bit safer if a region have constant garou problems? After a few encounters you'd likely have reports about that gift, because it's fairly low-level and common, so it's plausible that the R&amp;D guys and girls would work hard to counter it.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not speaking about invalidating the gift. The goal is, if we're assuming it works really that well against technomagic stuff, to make said stuff a bit more resilient to the gift, with a system that needs resources, or could work only for a limited time, or need someone to maintain, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Jokes and overkill aside, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"12880\" data-vbnamecard=\"12880\">Karlgust</a> has a fairly solid approach. Don't send in cybernetically enhanced individuals and instead rely on genetically enhanced ones. Also, use Wonders (or whatever the Techocracy calls them). Jam Tech shouldn't work on enchanted items since it doesn't work on Fetishes. So while it may disable foci (since if the electronics in your ray gun don't work, you shouldn't be able to funnel magick through it, if you haven't surpassed that foci), you can still use other methods to channel your enlightenment.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:38:50-08:00","id":1036873,"title":"","content":"Oh, right, geneenginered stuff would do, as well as long-range weapons, like enhanced snipers and weapon wonders in general. BUT couldn't the technos come up with some sort of active disruptor device? Something that could grant a few more dice/successes to resist the gift's effect for a limited time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T15:53:13-08:00","id":1036880,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036866#post1036866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> We need a Progenitor team here ASAP, we have a code-wolf situation and need specialized teams for extraction, over... Tell them to send all the Victors they have stored with the best gengenieered traits... Say what? No, no cyborgs, I told you before, it's a code WOLF situation... Yes yes, the Prime enhanced too... And the experentals, yes yes...<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, and I liked that pretty much. I could imagine the desperation on the agent's face making the call behind the flipped car, while on the other side there are detonations and a HIT Mark's dented head flying away! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:03:47-08:00","id":1036885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036880#post1036880\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Oh, and I liked that pretty much. I could imagine the desperation on the agent's face making the call behind the flipped car, while on the other side there are detonations and a HIT Mark's dented head flying away! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Extra salt in the wound: the one who answers the call is actually Glass Walker taking hold of the signal just to mess with the agent's mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:07:27-08:00","id":1036889,"title":"","content":"Well, Mages aren`t made for combat like Garous, but a prepared Mage would make any Garou look like a puppy. A combat oriented Mage could even go close quarter with Werewolves or Vampires. <br /> <br /> Now, if a Mage is caught unprepared, and by unprepared I mean &quot;not completely ready to defeat his opponent&quot;, since no Mage is ever truly without some effects and/or magic items. Then, the Garou has some chance of killing the Mage, depending of the situation and the build of both characters.<br /> <br /> I'd say that the Mage has more chance of sensing the Garou first because of all the lvl 1 sphere being about sensing things. As an unpreped Mage, I would first try to avoid or paralyze the Garou by lifting him still with Forces, making him sleep with Life, or fucking with his head with Mind. A Time wonder to stop time or Correspondence to get the fuck outta there work as well.<br /> <br /> Then I would fry the motherfucker with something like Prime, Forces, Matter, preferably using silver. In M20 each success means 2 agg damage plus 1 success for Forces attacks. So an initial Mage with Arete 3 that spend 1 WP can deliver 10 agg damage with Forces. <br /> <br /> But the first thing the Mage must do is find a way to avoid the wolf attacks, like a Force field, paralyzing him, or even getting intangible...<br /> <br /> Mage's versatility make them just too overpower and even caught without a plan, they can just pull some fucking incredible effects that can change things to their favor.<br /> <br /> So, no, Mages aren't prey for anyone. It's easier to accept the other way around. I can see Mages going into Caerns kicking the wolves asses to get some Quintessence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3153-lord-revan","name":"Lord Revan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3153_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1419"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T16:45:08-08:00","id":1036907,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036873#post1036873\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, right, geneenginered stuff would do, as well as long-range weapons, like enhanced snipers and weapon wonders in general. BUT couldn't the technos come up with some sort of active disruptor device? Something that could grant a few more dice/successes to resist the gift's effect for a limited time.</div> </div> </div> </div>It is called <b>Primium</b>.<br /> <br /> And since the Technos put that stuff ON EVERYTHING, they could still put up on a fight<br /> <br /> If all else fails, make that call for that Syndic Supervisor that works on Special Projects Division for their expertise, since they are the ones that deals with the Fera the most... Just leave that option as a last resource, because the guys on SPD are very restrictive about their operations, so there is a high likelihood that they would demand full control of the operation in order to help, which means that you would seem as incompetent in the eyes of Control and the Ivory Tower, and those bastard Sindics would take all the war spoils away (meaning: the Node, whatever fetish they might get, and any &quot;test subjects&quot; that might be captured alive)... In that case, it is possible that the Caern would be stormed by an army of Fomori of the Pentex... Still, that's a card you can play if you are well connected within the bureoucracy of the Union<br /> <br /> <br /> Devices (tech word for artifacts) may not be affected, that's true, they are more resistant than ordinary items, I don't have the rules on me now of the Forged by Dragon's fire, but I do remember that is not as easy to screw them (otherwise, it would be too easy to use Matter or Life to frustrate their use, which would make them almost useless). As it goes about technocrats, they are always full of devices... Even un-enlightened (sleepers) agents can be find with some devices. Thats one of the things that make the Union such a tough enemy - they build those damn things on industrial scales. For example, the lowest MiB, with no souls (so they don't even have avatar to awaken), beings cloned on the Vat tanks of the Progenitors, that turn into a pool of mud upon death, will have at least their sunglasses as devices for a series of effects... Some may have the mind eraser Device (yep, like the movie). <br /> <br /> Traditionalists have a harder time getting those wonderful items; you need to be at least a Prime Initiate (Prime 4), or having some contact with someone who can give you one. Otherwise, you are limited to amulets with Prime 2+, but even amulets are quite useful, and can make you VERY powerful (Forces 3, Prime 2, stockpile &quot;thunder cristals&quot; that delivers 15 aggravated damage on a single target upon each activation). The real problem is <u>Tass</u>, the other thing the Technocracy excel (they not only have more and better defended Nodes, but they also can use their quintessence in a better way - Technocrats always SANITIZE the Nodes they capture - so, your nature Node that produced Tass in the form of leafs that fall of the big mystical tree your Verbena group worshiped and could be use for healing effects due to its ressonance, now will produce raw quintessence and quintessencial gel as Tass that has been purified of any &quot;residual ressonance&quot;, and now can be used to power up Hit Marks, Plasma Cannons, Qui La Machines, whatever... The same holds true for a Nephandi Node full of entropic resonance that had blood pouring from the walls, Tass used for cursing effects or summoning specters... Now, it will be cristal clean, and will power up ANY techie device)<br /> <br /> So, if you wanna make &quot;thunder cristals&quot; amulets (magical items with limited uses), you'll need access to a Node with Dinamic (Energetic) ressonance... It would do you no good to have a holy Church as a Node with Pattern (Calm) ressonance... Plus, the form of the Tass matters too: if your Node produce Tass in the form of growing fungus, you can use it to make magical potions, but you would need Life and Matter to turn that fungus into crystals...<br /> <br /> So... That's a lot easier for the techies...<br /> <br /> Traditionalists, as individuals, far exceed the Technocrats. After all, an agent cant just wave some bones and teleport a mile away, or simply singing something in hebraic and fly, or send etherial bolts when punching someone. <br /> <br /> But the Union have... Well... Union. A Node is not the private property of an agent... Its an asset for organization. You'll be assigned to one for whatever purposes your superior needs you there.. When you build a Device, that's a very important equip for the Union, it wont necessarily be YOURS (after all, the tass and the lab you used for making it are resouces of the Union, not yours).<br /> <br /> And the Union have several Scientists on Autochtonia, Mecha and others constantly building more... They'll simple get a memo saying &quot;we need 100 magnetic blasters for next month&quot;, and those blasters will be giving for the Field Agents according to the <i>need</i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:04:32-08:00","id":1036920,"title":"","content":"I think something got lost through the process. I know how primium and devices work. Primium is a passive resistance, something you could slap on things as armor. I was talking about some kind of active device, which disrupts werewolf magic, or defends technocratic constructs and agents from messing with. It could be done with, again, ridiculous amounts of primium, but how else? Which spheres would be used to make such device?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of spirit/enthropy, maybe matter and prime to fuel it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:23:05-08:00","id":1036929,"title":"","content":"That been said... It's higly unlikely that such a confrontation would happen in such a cinematic way... Althouth PC can (and on many occasions, are) be stupid, and some NPCs can too, the many secret groups on WoD usually <i>are not</i>. So, the agents would take years making preparations before such an attack.... They would do what the Union do best: gather Intel. That's REALLY were they most excel at; despite popular belief, the image of the Hit Mark or the Victor Clone full of devices putting holes on walls with punches and vaporizing steel with energy beams is quite rare. The real Technocrat is the fully normal human taxi driver, the fully human university teacher, the bureoucrat, the cop, the secretary, the criminal tug and so on. The Technocracy have a huge net of spies that keep feeding them data. That's their real power. Vampires are good manipulators, that's true, but have no Union, they literally have betrayal in their bloods, so they undermine each others efforts. So, that leaves the Union with perhaps the biggest network of contacts in the WoD. They'll use this in their favor, trying to study the local Garou, to have an assessment of their abilities, numbers, modus operandi, connections and so on.<br /> <br /> They would probably try to isolate individual Garou, even capture some, both for interrogation and for lab tests (and sentence to Mecha after that, to become a lobotomized slave and Tass batery)\u2026 <br /> <br /> Meanwhile, the Garou, or Vampire, or Traditions, or Malfean group or whatever, won't simply sit in their homes and wait. If members of the group are simply vanishing, they will investigate, and if things get too heated, they'll hide while making an assessment of the situation. If the heat is too much, they may flee - or call for assistance.<br /> <br /> Thats actually, would most likely be the outcome on most situations... The techies probably wont have that lot assaults on Nodes with full teams of Hit Marks against a legion of golems. In most of the cases, the mages will just abandonabandon the area when the heat is too much, leaving behind a few traps, maybe even sucking the Node dry before they move<br /> <br /> The only situations where you'll have Qui La Machine flying above the middle of the town, is when the players broken the Shrowd and released an army of dead just because they wanted a magical scyth from a specter... In that case, there will be one hundred Hit Marks in their house the next day and a representative from Control that wants to capture them in person","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:42:18-08:00","id":1036937,"title":"","content":"Hey,<br /> <br /> A mage could, theoretically, pull off a Freddy Krueger effect and invade the dreams of a Vampire or Garou, kill him in his dreams (which would translate over to the real world, using life 3 or whatever sphere). I assume if that mage had mind 3 or 4, he'd be able to shift and manipulate the dreams to his liking, making said Vampire or Garou powerless to fight him in the dream world.<br /> <br /> Would any of you agree?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:43:10-08:00","id":1036938,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036929#post1036929\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Vampires are good manipulators, that's true, but have no Union. they literally have betrayal in their bloods</div> </div> </div> </div>1. The Camarilla, Sabbat, Setites, True Black Hand, and Assamites do exist. <br /> 2. No, they don't.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:52:03-08:00","id":1036947,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036920#post1036920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something got lost through the process. I know how primium and devices work. Primium is a passive resistance, something you could slap on things as armor. I was talking about some kind of active device, which disrupts werewolf magic, or defends technocratic constructs and agents from messing with. It could be done with, again, ridiculous amounts of primium, but how else? Which spheres would be used to make such device?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of spirit/enthropy, maybe matter and prime to fuel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, at least one Qui La Machine would join the fight, from the other side of the gauntlet (a huge Starship with at least 3 levels beyond the &quot;ridiculous&quot; amount of Primium, and hundreds of devices and effects, and enough quintessential energy to fuel a Horizon Realm for quite some time). That thing would be strenghtning the Local Gantlet, making it harder for the Garou to use many gifts, not to mention their allied spirits. It would also try to start the sanitization process with a strong etherial pulse, effectively destroying the spiritual properties of the Caern that enpowers the Garou. Now... Garou could summon many weird spirits for defense, and that fight wouldn't be THAT easy. And, since such an attack is an abomination to Gaia, many spirits would potentially answer the call. So, the Qui La Machine would probably try to do this far away using Correspondence, before diving into the Penumbra atmosphere for the assault.<br /> <br /> Perhaps, against individual Garou, strenghtning the Gauntlet around the Garou will make it harder to use many gifts, but that's Spirit 4 to do.<br /> <br /> The good thing about that for the techies, is that while the Gauntlet increases for the Wolves, it DECREASES by the same amount to the techies. That's one thing they can exploit.<br /> <br /> The Garou would have to rally a quick counter attack, before the spiritual properties of the Caern were damaged, or the Caern irreversibly sanitized... It would be a &quot;race against the clock&quot;.<br /> <br /> All that, of course, assumes the techie had time to prepare and the Garou were caught while having margaritas under the moon<br /> <br /> Another option, perhaps, could be making the gantlet as strong as possible around <b><i>the agents</i></b>. That could be done BEFORE entering the fray, and would improve the odds too.<br /> <br /> As for Jamming Machines, I think that what you're really looking for is something to prevent that... Something that could be used routinely on other situations...<br /> <br /> So, perhaps an Entropy 3 effect to stabilize the equipment is what you're looking for, althouth, since the power is spiritual in nature, it may need Spirit 3 to touch the spirit of the machines and Prime 2 to stabilize its pattern... So, Entropy 2, Prime 2, Spirit 3, maybe that can be used as &quot;opposed effect&quot; for that Jam gift<br /> <br /> Edit: spirit 3 would be used as a kind of &quot;reanimation&quot; of the spirits, only enough to let the techies awaken the spirit, manipulate it with Prime 2, and made it sleep again... Since it's not a free, awaken spirit, wandering in the Umbra, you would need to wake it up before touching it.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, since the Gift doesn't work on fetiches, maybe it wouldn't work on awakened items too? So, just &quot;awaken&quot; all your equip with Dimensional Science 3, or turn them all with fetiches with DS 4.<br /> <br /> Having their machines working on weird ways however, would hardly be a thing the techies would enjoy much","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:53:49-08:00","id":1036948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036920#post1036920\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Which spheres would be used to make such device?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of spirit/enthropy, maybe matter and prime to fuel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Spirit (DS) alone would work as a broad catch all, but most Technocrats either don't have it or don't know how to use it the same way, so that's kind of limiting. Otherwise you could come up with a counter-effect. I would guess Matter/Entropy? Again though, my knowledge of Mage is more limited than other games. As said though, there are more straight forward ways to go about it (like getting non cyborgs to move in).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036937#post1036937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> <br /> A mage could, theoretically, pull off a Freddy Krueger effect and invade the dreams of a Vampire or Garou, kill him in his dreams (which would translate over to the real world, using life 3 or whatever sphere). I assume if that mage had mind 3 or 4, he'd be able to shift and manipulate the dreams to his liking, making said Vampire or Garou powerless to fight him in the dream world.<br /> <br /> Would any of you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>So Vampires may or may not actually dream. I don't think the books specifically say one way or the other.<br /> And Garou are dangerous in their dreams (per Werewolf books, and Wraith books). So while I would say this is a possibility, it is in no way straight forward. Garou are more than likely (depending on the book your going from and exactly how this effect would work) at full strength. Killing them there wouldn't be any easier than fighting them in the Umbra. Also, depending on if you are using the Werewolf books, each Auspice used to get a special power in dreamscapes.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-23-2017, 08:56 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:55:35-08:00","id":1036949,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036948#post1036948\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So Vampires may or may not actually dream. I don't think the books specifically say one way or the other.</div> </div> </div> </div>V20 explicitly talks about vampires dreaming. P363 Core has the most on that. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T17:59:19-08:00","id":1036950,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036949#post1036949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">V20 explicitly talks about vampires dreaming. P363 Core has the most on that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks. Then yes, the dream attack thing might work on them too. I would bet most or all of their mental Disciplines would be fully functional in a dreamscape though. If a strategy like this was a fool proof plan against them, then they'd have been dream killed out of existence.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:04:30-08:00","id":1036953,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036937#post1036937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> <br /> A mage could, theoretically, pull off a Freddy Krueger effect and invade the dreams of a Vampire or Garou, kill him in his dreams (which would translate over to the real world, using life 3 or whatever sphere). I assume if that mage had mind 3 or 4, he'd be able to shift and manipulate the dreams to his liking, making said Vampire or Garou powerless to fight him in the dream world.<br /> <br /> Would any of you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div>It would be chimerical death, as per changelling, but you could use other spheres for a more &quot;permanent&quot; solution<br /> <br /> Or, just use Mind 4 to take away his Mind and Prime 2 to turn it apart and leave the lobotomized body... But unless you have Corr 4, that will be hard to pull the necessary ritual on the side of your sleeping dangerous &quot;victim&quot;...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:14 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:17:22-08:00","id":1036958,"title":"","content":"Ah, so a Freddy Krueger effect is essentially powerless against them? Even if you were to warp their dreams and make the landscape incredibly tumultuous?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:18:37-08:00","id":1036960,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036950#post1036950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Then yes, the dream attack thing might work on them too. I would bet most or all of their mental Disciplines would be fully functional in a dreamscape though. If a strategy like this was a fool proof plan against them, then they'd have been dream killed out of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably their physical displines too, and things like thaumaturgy too, obtenebration, obfuscation, dementia would be going on hyperdrive mode, in fact many mental disciplines would go super powered... Otherwise yes, changellings would be strong as fuck.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:30:00-08:00","id":1036967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036958#post1036958\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, so a Freddy Krueger effect is essentially powerless against them? Even if you were to warp their dreams and make the landscape incredibly tumultuous?</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, this will work better against Vampires then Garou since Vampires have less (not none, but far less) defenses. <br /> <br /> I don't remember all of the Auspice powers offhand, but that sort of thing is going to be completely unexpected by the attacking Mage. Ragabash can jump to other dreams. Galliards can rewrite the dream entirely. And Ahroun can just roll Rage to damage people and things. I forgot the Theurge and Philodox powers. But this is in addition to any Gifts the Garou might have.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:34:09-08:00","id":1036970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036950#post1036950\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks. Then yes, the dream attack thing might work on them too. I would bet most or all of their mental Disciplines would be fully functional in a dreamscape though. If a strategy like this was a fool proof plan against them, then they'd have been dream killed out of existence.</div> </div> </div> </div>I disagree. How does one use Disciplines in a dream? Would the vampire even remember they had them? Dreams are slippery places, where one's memory and thoughts are jumbled. Unless the vampire was trained in Lucid Dreaming, they might not even remember they're vampires. Even if they did, how does one make eye contact for Dominate if the dream takes a non-visual form? Or if the Mage appears as an eyeless monster? Or doesn't appear at all, but instead hides, or appears as a cloud of smoke? I would grant you Auspex - <i>assuming the vampire was lucid enough to think to activate it</i> - as well as Dementation maybe, and the Path of Oneiromancy. Anything else, though? The powers may not apply.<br /> <br /> I certainly would never give the vampire access to physical Disciplines. Those are enhancements of the body, which is stuck asleep in the vampire's haven. Of no use in a dream. At best, the vampire would start sleep fighting, and tear their room apart. Fortitude, perhaps, to soak the Aggravated damage from the Mage's magickal assault. Anything else, however, is unhelpful. When on a mental battlefield, you fight with Wits and Willpower, not Dexterity and Strength.<br /> <br /> The real reasons why vampires don't all get assassinated in their sleep is because 1) you need Correspondence 3 or Mind 4 to enter the vampire's dream (that is, without needing to be physically present around the sleeping vampire, which is extremely dangerous), and 2) few Mages would either think to or bother to do it. Not every Mage is even aware that vampires can dream. Mages don't commonly know much about vampires in general. Mages also tend to avoid vampires for much the same reasons vampires avoid mages: tangling with them is often more trouble than it's worth. If the vamp finds out what the Mage did, the Mage just earned a powerful, tenacious, <i>immortal</i> adversary.<br /> <br /> Moreover, the sort of Rote devoted to sleep assassination sounds to me like esoteric knowledge, even among Mages. Let alone one created that can affect Vampires (it requires both Life and Matter, while mortals only require Life). Not that it wouldn't exist. It's just that it's more likely to be stored away in an obscure tome, sitting forgotten in some wizard's library. Waiting to be unearthed, should a Mage think to go looking for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 01-23-2017, 09:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:43:38-08:00","id":1036976,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036970#post1036970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I disagree. How does one use Disciplines in a dream? Would the vampire even remember they had them? Dreams are slippery places, where one's memory and thoughts are jumbled. Unless the vampire was trained in Lucid Dreaming, they might not even remember they're vampires. Even if they did, how does one make eye contact for Dominate if the dream takes a non-visual form? Or if the Mage appears as an eyeless monster? Or doesn't appear at all, but instead hides, or appears as a cloud of smoke? I would grant you Auspex - assuming the vampire was lucid enough to think to activate it - as well as Dementation maybe, and the Path of Oneiromancy. Anything else, though? The powers may not apply.</div> </div> </div> </div>Some powers may well not apply. I'm not arguing otherwise. This entire scenario is outside of provided rules. Your Dominate example though is a bad one. The Vampire doesn't need to look into the eyes anymore (as of V20) so there are ways around some of those examples (the best being to not actually appear there). I personally disagree that Thaum would work in general, but who knows. Again, this is all going to be house ruled. I just commented on how I would run it. There is no incorrect way to do so.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036970#post1036970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I certainly would never give the vampire access to physical Disciplines. Those are enhancements of the body, which is stuck asleep in the vampire's haven. Of no use in a dream. At best, the vampire would start sleep fighting, and tear their room apart. Fortitude, perhaps, to soak the Aggravated damage from the Mage's magickal assault. Anything else, however, is unhelpful. When on a mental battlefield, you fight with Wits and Willpower, not Dexterity and Strength.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree entirely. Fortitude would only really work, if you are translating dream damage over to their physical body.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036970#post1036970\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> The real reasons why vampires don't all get assassinated in their sleep is because 1) you need Correspondence 3 or Mind 4 to enter the vampire's dream (that is, without needing to be physically present around the sleeping vampire, which is extremely dangerous), and 2) few Mages would either think to or bother to do it. Not every Mage is even aware that vampires can dream. Mages don't commonly know much about vampires in general. Mages also tend to avoid vampires for much the same reasons vampires avoid mages: tangling with them is often more trouble than it's worth. If the vamp finds out what the Mage did, the Mage just earned a powerful, tenacious, <i>immortal</i> adversary.</div> </div> </div> </div> I agree with this entirely as well.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T18:50:42-08:00","id":1036983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036938#post1036938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. The Camarilla, Sabbat, Setites, True Black Hand, and Assamites do exist.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the Camarilla ever TRULY united, the same way that the Technocracy does, they would've conquered the world and made Mages their bitches, usefull slave-assets. The proof of my point is exactly that they haven't and they let a group a puny Mages take control of the world (when the Order of Reason began, the Order of Hermes alone could've turned them into a footnote on history. But they too had no unity - they were busy with political bickering, fighting the House Diedne thanks to the manipulations of Tremere, and after that, fighting Tremere upon realizing what he had done).<br /> <br /> A Camarilla Prince have huge power, influence, contacts, autority. But he is constantly being undermined by the other elders, who are all the time trying to prevail upon each other, and the sires and children of those enter this dance... That's not Union, it's the opposite of that. A tech agent, when he have a contact, he files a report to his supervisor about that contact with all relevant information about it, and the Supervisor will send cryptografic copies over to Control, to the Ivory Tower, and any other relevant place. Next time another MiB agent finds that person, his sunglasses will show in the HUD screen the name of the person, the agents that have had previous relations with him, the tips he gave to those agents, his know occupations and afiliations, etc. The contacts of the Prince, most likely will be a total secret to anyone but the Prince himself, a trusted ghoul or two, who probably only know that that person has some business with his site, and the person herself.<br /> <br /> While an agent can make an offcial request for equipment to his Supervisor and receive expensive magikal items that can only be made by veteran scients in a far away orbital realm that the agent himself never saw the place or met the person who made his toy, the Tremere won't even tell their Ventrue Prince what rituals they can conjure in their chantry.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036938#post1036938\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. No, they don't.</div> </div> </div> </div>Cain killed Abel<br /> <br /> The third generation killed the second.<br /> <br /> What is the jihad after all?<br /> <br /> So, leeches are so united, that they split into two major factions that hate each other... And one of those were created by rebellious children who wanted to kill their elders, and know openly preaches cannibalization of the elders. The Camarilla is soooo United, that all of it's clans have anti tribes on the sabbat, including even the Tremere. Not to mention that the Brujah hate the Ventrues, and many Camarilla neonates are anarchists (mostly brujah). Meanwhile, no one trusts the Tremere, mostly because of Ventrue propaganda to undermine their political power. Nosferatu are gossip seekers and secret keepers, and Gangrel left the boat. In the Sabbat... Well... Two civil Wars? Really? The assamites, that's a joke right? Split in 3, one side going to the Sabbat, another to the Camarilla, and other remaining &quot;pure&quot; in the &quot;old ways&quot;. The Setites... Well, the demonic serpents are the real suprise... And even so, they have an anti tribe on the Sabbat.<br /> <br /> You could have said Giovanni... Now, those truly are united. But, lets not forget that they came to be after their patriarch betrayed their true sire Capadocius and cannibalized him so... Yeah, betrail again...<br /> <br /> And the list goes on and on and on... Like Troile devouring his/her site, the Nosferatu rebelling against Absimilliard, and so on...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:00:54-08:00","id":1036989,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036976#post1036976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I personally disagree that Thaum would work in general, but who knows. </div> </div> </div> </div>I listed Oneiromancy because it's a Path devoted specifically to dreams. As such, it may prove the exception, even if all other Thaum Paths fail to work there.<br /> <br /> Alternatively, a blood sorcerer may develop a Ritual for aiding in defense against dream assault. Something like &quot;Bulwark of the Lucid Vigil&quot;, that allows a vampire without dots in the Lucid Dreaming skill to have their full wits about them. The sorcerer performs the Ritual before they go to sleep.<br /> <br /> After some thought, Dream Assassination and defenses against it sound like the sort of thing that would come up during the First Massasa War. The Order of Hermes finds out about House Tremere's treachery, and begins researching ways to fight them. Some now-forgotten magus develops a Rote for invading dreams and killing through them, and adapts it to vampiric opponents. After a choice few Tremere turn to dust during the day, seemingly in their sleep, the nascent Clan begins researching ways to defend against it. It could be part of the reason why the Tremere have Auspex as a native Discipline (or at the very least, it was prized during those nights). Perhaps even Elder or Combination powers were developed for Auspex, to provide specialized defenses, as were the Path of Oneiromancy and some select Rituals.<br /> <br /> Then the war ended, and both sides turned to other business. The Rotes and Rituals devoted to dream combat were filed away and forgotten. Oneiromancy was said to have been lost for centuries, save among the Sabbat. Could be some of Goratrix's followers knew the Path, and spread it around. I'm just speculating wildly at this point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:01:54-08:00","id":1036990,"title":"","content":"It's far easier to simply use Mind 4 to remove the Mind of your victim from their body, and Prime 2 to physically assault it and shred it into pieces, leaving a lobotomized carcass behind. And, while in Astral projection, the Mage can have the upper hand, since the might Garou or unholy Vampire won't have aggravated soaking abilities nor natural weapons (and the Mage can use pure etherial swords to strike directly their mental patterns). In that terrain, a Mage have a strong advantage","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:28:53-08:00","id":1037001,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036990#post1036990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's far easier to simply use Mind 4 to remove the Mind of your victim from their body, and Prime 2 to physically assault it and shred it into pieces, leaving a lobotomized carcass behind. And, while in Astral projection, the Mage can have the upper hand, since the might Garou or unholy Vampire won't have aggravated soaking abilities nor natural weapons (and the Mage can use pure etherial swords to strike directly their mental patterns). In that terrain, a Mage have a strong advantage</div> </div> </div> </div>Garou on the Astral Plane can and do soak Agg and most certainly have their natural weapons. They're half spirit. This isn't to say that they wouldn't be at a disadvantage, but they are far from helpless. The Astral Plane also reacts negatively to their Rage, but I don't remember the actual systems for it.<br /> <br /> For Vampires, I would just use the Auspex rules for projection, even if in this case it's unwilling. Again, the wouldn't be helpless but they'd be more disadvantaged than Garou. But they would also be more likely to know what was going on I would say.<br /> <br /> Also, as of M20 all Supernaturals with Occult would have innate countermagic against this sort of attack, in addition to their more typical defenses (though this defense seems to be largely derided among the Mage forums).<br /> <br /> Basically, there isn't (and shouldn't be) easy &quot;I win&quot; buttons against other Supernaturals. The setting losses a lot if that's the case.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-23-2017, 10:31 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:31:08-08:00","id":1037004,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036866#post1036866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Ridiculous amounts of Primium<br /> <br /> Or<br /> <br /> Send every Iterator home... Go rest a little guys...<br /> <br /> We need a Progenitor team here ASAP, we have a code-wolf situation and need specialized teams for extraction, over... Tell them to send all the Victors they have stored with the best gengenieered traits... Say what? No, no cyborgs, I told you before, it's a code WOLF situation... Yes yes, the Prime enhanced too... And the experentals, yes yes...<br /> <br /> Have you ever played StarCraft?<br /> <br /> Now, I want you to think on ZERGS<br /> <br /> If that fails, just call for an Ion Cannon burst from a satellitte in orbit (that should be the lest option if you are trying to take a Caern, because you'll want to let the Caern intact for future sanitization)</div> </div> </div> </div>Skip the Progenitor team.<br /> <br /> Neutron Pattern Disruptor array in orbit. Living things die, non-living assets (Caerns) do not. With an enlightened targeting operative, you're looking at a Perception + Energy Weapons attack at Diff 4, that ignores non-endurance non-primium soaks and deals 5 + Attack successes Aggravated damage to five targets every round. Apply perception boosting tech as liberally as you require. Oh, and it would ALSO ignore any cover they might have. Because radiation Yo.<br /> <br /> You can have multiple of these gunnery stations on a single orbital platform.<br /> <br /> They don't even see what kills them as they die. The only things that might survive are Corax. Which are unlikely to be much of a problem for more traditional operatives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:48:11-08:00","id":1037011,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037004#post1037004\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Skip the Progenitor team.<br /> <br /> Neutron Pattern Disruptor array in orbit. Living things die, non-living assets (Caerns) do not. With an enlightened targeting operative, you're looking at a Perception + Energy Weapons attack at Diff 4, that ignores non-endurance non-primium soaks and deals 5 + Attack successes Aggravated damage to five targets every round. Apply perception boosting tech as liberally as you require. Oh, and it would ALSO ignore any cover they might have. Because radiation Yo.<br /> <br /> You can have multiple of these gunnery stations on a single orbital platform.<br /> <br /> They don't even see what kills them as they die. The only things that might survive are Corax. Which are unlikely to be much of a problem for more traditional operatives.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sounds like it would hurt, but you'd likely need to throw some spirit in there too. Otherwise if there are more Garou than 5 in attendance (or if you roll badly), the werewolves might slip into the umbra to avoid getting their guts microwaved. And as far as 'seeing what kills them' there are gifts that let Garou perceive magical effects.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T19:56:25-08:00","id":1037015,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037011#post1037011\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sounds like it would hurt, but you'd likely need to throw some spirit in there too. Otherwise if there are more Garou than 5 in attendance (or if you roll badly), the werewolves might slip into the umbra to avoid getting their guts microwaved. And as far as 'seeing what kills them' there are gifts that let Garou perceive magical effects.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing to part where it's Mages that are attacking. That means the other Supernaturals have to lay down and die, unable to defend themselves.<br /> Honestly with that sort of logic there should be no enemies left alive that aren't also Mages.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:00:03-08:00","id":1037018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036983#post1036983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the Camarilla ever TRULY united, the same way that the Technocracy does, they would've conquered the world and made Mages their bitches, usefull slave-assets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. I'd say this alone shows a gross misunderstanding of the Camarilla. &quot;These so-called \u201cKindred\u201d seek to maintain a quiet harmony between vampires and humanity&quot;<br /> The Camarilla's very first Tradition is the Masquerade, seeking to remain alongside humans. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The proof of my point is exactly that they haven't and they let a group a puny Mages take control of the world </div> </div> </div> Ah, again, no. They expressly don't have conquering the world as a goal. So their failing in a non-goal doesn't make them united as a giant sect. When dominating Kindred society is their real care. It also sort of misses the point of the game. If any one faction ruled the world, kind of ruins any antagonism. Even further, victory being a measure of unity isn't a realistic measuring stick. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> the Order of Hermes alone could've turned them into a footnote on history. </div> </div> </div> Sorta like when they beat the Tremere in the Massasa War? Or the second Massasa War? Oh, wait. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But they too had no unity - they were busy with political bickering, fighting the House Diedne thanks to the manipulations of Tremere, and after that, fighting Tremere upon realizing what he had done). </div> </div> </div>Point being they didn't succeed or come close in wiping out Vampire society at any point. So it is rather pointless to mention. We could play what if in the lore all day.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> A Camarilla Prince have huge power, influence, contacts, autority. But he is constantly being undermined by the other elders, who are all the time trying to prevail upon each other, and the sires and children of those enter this dance. </div> </div> </div>Depends entirely on the Domain. Also kind of ignores everything about Justicars, Alastors, Archons, The Inner Circle, and the entire hierarchy of the society. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> That's not Union, it's the opposite of that. A tech agent, when he have a contact, he files a report to his supervisor about that contact with all relevant information about it, and the Supervisor will send cryptografic copies over to Control, to the Ivory Tower, and any other relevant place. Next time another MiB agent finds that person, his sunglasses will show in the HUD screen the name of the person, the agents that have had previous relations with him, the tips he gave to those agents, his know occupations and afiliations, etc. The contacts of the Prince, most likely will be a total secret to anyone but the Prince himself, a trusted ghoul or two, who probably only know that that person has some business with his site, and the person herself. </div> </div> </div> Again, depends entirely on the Prince. but is rather presumptuous about the cooperation of Primogen, Sheriff, Scourges, Hounds, etc. Exaggerates the disunity while overemphasizes the Union's. Kind of raises the point you yourself tried to make, if the Union are as oiled as you seem to indicate, one would think they would have already wiped out all the Traditions and there'd be nobody to play them. But that's certainly not the case. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Cain killed Abel<br /> The third generation killed the second.<br /> What is the jihad after all?<br /> So, leeches are so united, that they split into two major factions that hate each other.. </div> </div> </div> Almost like the divide between the Union and the Orders. Or Garou and the Black Spiral Dancers/Wyrm Fallen Fera. Regardless, this is a strawman. My claim was never 'leeches are all united.' Merely saying 'betrayal is literally in their blood' was a false statement. It is not LITERALLY in their blood. Besides maybe the Ravnos, but that's neither here nor there.<br /> <br /> The rest of your comments aren't really relevant because they make several false assumptions. 1. That clan unity and sect unity are the same outside Assamites and Setites. Missing that Assamites joining the Camarilla, Gangrel's leaving, and the existence or lack thereof of Tremere Antitribu are optional in V20 Or assuming relative size of antitribu in general. 2. That the Union doesn't suffer any degree of disunity in such manners. As though the Order of Reason has never had orders leave, reorganize, or be destroyed from within. But we both know that's not true. Because if we're going to go through the history of Mage groups (and the Union) we'll find that sort of thing as well. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> And the list goes on and on and on... Like Troile devouring his/her site, the Nosferatu rebelling against Absimilliard, and so on... </div> </div> </div> And again, you don't see me denying betrayal happens among vampires. But it is not LITERALLY in their blood.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:01:10-08:00","id":1037019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037001#post1037001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Garou on the Astral Plane can and do soak Agg and most certainly have their natural weapons.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's when the Garou enter the Astral Umbra <b>in his physical/spiritual </b> form. Mind 4 takes only his MIND away, not his spirit (what is the difference you may ask, I do not know, you'll have to go to a Dreamspeaker+Akashic filosophical debate)... Actually, with this, he woudnt have a body AT ALL (you need Prime 2 to make a body of light to be able to interact in a physical manner, otherwise you'd only be a Voice and a presence... But still can be attacked with primal energies)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037001#post1037001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They're half spirit. This isn't to say that they wouldn't be at a disadvantage, but they are far from helpless. The Astral Plane also reacts negatively to their Rage, but I don't remember the actual systems for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Like I said, being half spirit wouldn't protect them, since this is a purely mental attack<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037001#post1037001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">For Vampires, I would just use the Auspex rules for projection, even if in this case it's unwilling. Again, the wouldn't be helpless but they'd be more disadvantaged than Garou. But they would also be more likely to know what was going on I would say.</div> </div> </div> </div>I totally agree on that<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037001#post1037001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, as of M20 all Supernaturals with Occult would have innate countermagic against this sort of attack, in addition to their more typical defenses (though this defense seems to be largely derided among the Mage forums).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes... The problem is that those rules sucks. I do think that things like &quot;aha! I just stole your mind from the safety of my Sanctum!&quot; are pretty ridiculous and need some balancing, but the rules on M20 just imbalance things the other way around. However, I could still do a ritual to have a gazillion of successes, turning that point moot again. So, some house rules and maturity would be the ideal solution - no fast and dirty mechanics sadly<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037001#post1037001\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> there isn't (and shouldn't be) easy &quot;I win&quot; buttons against other Supernaturals. The setting losses a lot if that's the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree on that, for either way. Which is why I hate powers like high level Presence, Dominate, Gifts that can disable any and all Magic, thus turning Mages useless and Tremere or Giovanni close to that, or a Mind power that I can use on the other side of the globe to lobotomize a helpless victim. I hate &quot;rock I win, paper you lose&quot; situations","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:24:00-08:00","id":1037027,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037015#post1037015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing to part where it's Mages that are attacking. That means the other Supernaturals have to lay down and die, unable to defend themselves.<br /> Honestly with that sort of logic there should be no enemies left alive that aren't also Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem (and solution) with Mage, is that it is so open ended, that you could really do those ridiculous things. I mean, in the White Wolf metaplot itself, the Technocracy nuked the antidiluvian Ravnos, and after that, sent a super Sun Ray on him doing exactly that, using magikal satellites on orbit. So... Blame the writers...<br /> <br /> With Mage, you can easily play Space Operas with plasma cannons, force shields and tactical nukes.<br /> <br /> Some lunatics even described powers to &quot;throw away&quot; entire Horizon Realms, or even move planets on the Masters of the Art (a book that thankfully were renegaded to Oblivion)<br /> <br /> But that's the thing of the game, it's mechanics are THAT open ended to give players and STs a wide array of game plays, not to show how amanzingly powerful and higher breed mages are.<br /> <br /> That's for your team to play some titans building a new Earth from scratch; for making evil-hunters with amazing powers, or just some special people operating on the backdoors of the common world, struggling amongst many secret conspiracies and unamed terrors while having a few tricks to be able to live the name.<br /> <br /> In truth, a Mage will be as powerful as it is NEEDED for the game... In some games, simple vampires are dreadful things, ancient scourges that you REALLY don't wanna mess with. On others, they are Tass, just waiting to be gathered. When playing Space Operas, the minimum you'll have will be a full Primium exo squeleton with a gazillion of insane effects; when playing against the super conspiracy, you may not even have a Node at all.<br /> <br /> So... Like I said before, a Mage will be as weak or as powerful as the player's imagination and the ST need.<br /> <br /> So, do you wanna make demi-gods? Ok, so let the player make the ritual to make his wand do 50+ aggr... Wanna make them just powerful but not insane? Make it Max Arete+Will. Wanna take away all that power? Remove the prolonged rituals rule (now the Mages will suffer - a lot).<br /> <br /> So, there you go. Could mages just make any other lay down and die? If you wanna to play such a game, sure. Wanna make them just minor trickesters that should not provoke the weakest neonate? Fine too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:57:15-08:00","id":1037035,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037019#post1037019\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's when the Garou enter the Astral Umbra <b>in his physical/spiritual </b> form. Mind 4 takes only his MIND away, not his spirit</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know that you can separate them like that. The same way you need conjunctional Life/Spirit to affect them physically, you should probably need Mind/Spirit to do this to them mentally just my opinion though.<br /> Actually, separate question on this. I know you can project your own mind at Mind 4. To do this to someone else then, wouldn't you need Mind 5?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T20:57:58-08:00","id":1037036,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really. I'd say this alone shows a gross misunderstanding of the Camarilla. &amp;quot;These so-called \u201cKindred\u201d seek to maintain a quiet harmony between vampires and humanity&amp;quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>If only the Garou knew how kind the Camarilla is, I'm sure they would hold hands with those autruistic kindred<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Camarilla's very first Tradition is the Masquerade, seeking to remain alongside humans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, they are indeed the philantropists of WoD.<br /> The Maquerade is a self protection act, they don't really care about humans, they only care about self preservation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, again, no. They expressly don't have conquering the world as a goal. So their failing in a non-goal doesn't make them united as a giant sect. When dominating Kindred society is their real care. It also sort of misses the point of the game. If any one faction ruled the world, kind of ruins any antagonism. Even further, victory being a measure of unity isn't a realistic measuring stick.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, they just seek power to relieve the boredom of their lives.<br /> The fact no one faction ever had a total victory, doesn't mean that ot wouldn't been possible. Being &quot;un-fun&quot; doesn't make it impossible either.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sorta like when they beat the Tremere in the Massasa War? Or the second Massasa War? Oh, wait.</div> </div> </div> </div>Read again. I said the Order of Hermes could've wiped out the <b>Order of Reason</b> (not the Tremere) at the very beggining of it, but didn't do it because they couldn't be allowed to bother stop their political bickering.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Point being they didn't succeed or come close in wiping out Vampire society at any point. So it is rather pointless to mention. We could play what if in the lore all day.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Tremere is the most nonsense ever in the WoD. But whatever, it's cannon, and they actually are fun. So be it. <br /> <br /> But read again what I said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Depends entirely on the Domain. Also kind of ignores everything about Justicars, Alastors, Archons, The Inner Circle, and the entire hierarchy of the society. <br /> Again, depends entirely on the Prince. but is rather presumptuous about the cooperation of Primogen, Sheriff, Scourges, Hounds, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just strawman. When add all that to the mix, it gets even worse, with even more political bickering and hidden agendas. It doesn't mean individuals don't cooperate AT ALL, but that is very limited and undermined by internal competition.<br /> <br /> While we are at it, why did the Tremere survived?<br /> <br /> Unity. And the mighty Tzimisce were divided as hell. Which is why the Tremere kicked them over and over.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Exaggerates the disunity while overemphasizes the Union's. Kind of raises the point you yourself tried to make, if the Union are as oiled as you seem to indicate, one would think they would have already wiped out all the Traditions and there'd be nobody to play them. But that's certainly not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well... In 3ed that's kind of what happened... They wiped out the Traditions for good... But on the metaplot, that caused the Avatar Storm, something that had nothing to do with their organiztion and methods, but ratter were something no one could predict (like tornado destroying both armies, after one of the sides had strike a decisive victory on the field)<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Almost like the divide between the Union and the Orders. Or Garou and the Black Spiral Dancers/Wyrm Fallen Fera. Regardless, this is a strawman. My claim was never 'leeches are all united.' Merely saying 'betrayal is literally in their blood' was a false statement. It is not LITERALLY in their blood. Besides maybe the Ravnos, but that's neither here nor there.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, it is a strawman. Yours. You still haven't adressed the fact that an agent will receive a powerful artifact from a guy he never met on the Moon and get Intel from sources he never saw, while a Vampire will never introduce his assets to his closer social circle, or that a Tremere will never even show one of his books to others.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The rest of your comments aren't really relevant because they make several false assumptions. 1. That clan unity and sect unity are the same outside Assamites and Setites. Missing that Assamites joining the Camarilla, Gangrel's leaving, and the existence or lack thereof of Tremere Antitribu are optional in V20 Or assuming relative size of antitribu in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>More strawman.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. That the Union doesn't suffer any degree of disunity in such manners. As though the Order of Reason has never had orders leave, reorganize, or be destroyed from within. But we both know that's not true. Because if we're going to go through the history of Mage groups (and the Union) we'll find that sort of thing as well.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Masons, the Gabrielites, those two started dissent amongst the Order of Reason. Result: persecuted and extinct. After that, the Termodinamic and Diferential Engineers (Etherite and Virtual Adepts) fled to avoid the same fate. Dissention is not tolerated within the Union; those who do not adhere are ejected. That's why those groups were cast aside. But that cleaning process keep the Union... A Union. The Etherite or VA would've broken the Time Table, they would've brought anarch. After each one of those guys left, the Union got even more united. Note that the union didn't lose power in any of those situations.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037018#post1037018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> And again, you don't see me denying betrayal happens among vampires. But it is not LITERALLY in their blood.</div> </div> </div> </div>Do you have any idea of what the jihad is? And why ALL the kindred play it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T21:05:05-08:00","id":1037037,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037035#post1037035\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know that you can separate them like that. The same way you need conjunctional Life/Spirit to affect them physically, you should probably need Mind/Spirit to do this to them mentally just my opinion though.<br /> Actually, separate question on this. I know you can project your own mind at Mind 4. To do this to someone else then, wouldn't you need Mind 5?</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't remember exactly, but I guess not. It wouldn't make sense thou, since Mind 4 is direct mental manipulation, like dealing with memories and compeling a mind, while 5 would be full mental control, which is the ability to create a new mind or breaking ones silver cord (leaving the body behind for good)<br /> <br /> About the Garou Mind/Spirit, you're probably right... Since there is no rules anywhere thou, it's once again up to the ST... But I would agree with you on that one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T21:43:06-08:00","id":1037045,"title":"","content":"Everything gets to resist mental magick effects with Willpower. In addition, Garou are one of the few entities that can return the favor by traveling the Dream Zone (and they are entering your dreams, so you may be in trouble).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-24-2017, 12:56 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-23T22:00:55-08:00","id":1037049,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037036#post1037036\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If only the Garou knew how kind the Camarilla is, I'm sure they would hold hands with those autruistic kindred</div> </div> </div> </div>Don't try to misstate what I said again. I'm not claiming they are altruistic. Also, the Garou do have misconceptions about most Kindred regardless. So that's not saying much.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, they are indeed the philantropists of WoD.<br /> The Maquerade is a self protection act, they don't really care about humans, they only care about self preservation. </div> </div> </div>Again, I'm not saying they care about humans. All my statements were about how they weren't some group that seeks world or human conquest as you incorrectly stated. So you can say, 'well, if they had unite, they would be ruling the world' because it explicitly isn't something they strive for. And the typical Kindred is going to just want to ignore a dangerous mage.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Sure, they just seek power to relieve the boredom of their lives.<br /> The fact no one faction ever had a total victory, doesn't mean that ot wouldn't been possible. Being &quot;un-fun&quot; doesn't make it impossible either. </div> </div> </div> The fact remains that no one faction in WoD has total control over the world. So bringing it up is a moot point. It means nothing. It didn't happen within the setting, so on that basis, it isn't possible. Hypotheticals are something entirely different than talking about the setting. The Union, The Orders, The Garou Nation, Camarilla, Sabbat, Society of Leopold, nobody has total domination. It is an unrealistic end point because the setting was written purposefully with contesting factions with no one as the current victor.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Read again. I said the Order of Hermes could've wiped out the <b>Order of Reason</b> (not the Tremere) at the very beggining of it, but didn't do it because they couldn't be allowed to bother stop their political bickering. </div> </div> </div>You didn't make that clear when you stated it. Even after rereading, it looks a lot more like you were saying the Order of Hermes could have wiped out the Camarilla when the Order of Reason started.<br /> <br /> That said, I'll take you on your supposed intent. In which case, it doesn't matter. Whether or not the Order of Hermes could have wiped out the Order of Reason doesn't have much bearing on the current discussion. And again, is a needless hypothetical.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Just strawman. When add all that to the mix, it gets even worse, with even more political bickering and hidden agendas. It doesn't mean individuals don't cooperate AT ALL, but that is very limited and undermined by internal competition. </div> </div> </div> No, you misunderstand. A strawman would have been to say 'The Camarilla has perfect unity.' But your statement literally said that Princes are so paranoid that they keep secrets from everyone but one or two people And everyone is out to get one another. That itself is inherently a false presentation of the Camarilla. It ignores context of each situation and the workings of their higher ups involved. It just isn't accurate. I'm not out here to show that Kindred society is without flaws. But the point remains that numerous (Camarilla, Sabbat, True Black Hand, Inconnu, Anarch Free State) are all functioning organizations of vampires.<br /> <br /> The goal of the Camarilla is to uphold the Traditions. And generally they've done that sufficiently. But you depict an unrealistic picture of them with statements like, 'The contacts of the Prince, most likely will be a total secret to anyone but the Prince himself, a trusted ghoul or two, who probably only know that that person has some business with his site, and the person herself.' Besides being incorrect, if internal competition was as crippling as you seem to think, the Traditions wouldn't be upheld. Yet, lo and behold, they remain law in Camarilla domains.<br /> <br /> If we're being technical, I do agree that the Sabbat and True Black Hand have significantly more structure than the Camarilla when it comes to hierarchy, if that's anything.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> While we are at it, why did the Tremere survived?<br /> Unity. And the mighty Tzimisce were divided as hell. Which is why the Tremere kicked them over and over. </div> </div> </div> Tremere survived from unity, AND joining the Camarilla/having Thaumaturgy. A lack of any of those three components would've spelled their end. Not really relevant, though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Well... In 3ed that's kind of what happened... They wiped out the Traditions for good... But on the metaplot, that caused the Avatar Storm, something that had nothing to do with their organiztion and methods, but ratter were something no one could predict (like tornado destroying both armies, after one of the sides had strike a decisive victory on the field. </div> </div> </div> Rogue Council was a thing and they certainly didn't wipe out all Tradition mages. And I'm pretty sure Ascension features an ending with Technocrat civil war or Nephandi winning as possibly outcomes as well, so...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yes, it is a strawman. Yours. You still haven't adressed the fact that an agent will receive a powerful artifact from a guy he never met on the Moon and get Intel from sources he never saw, while a Vampire will never introduce his assets to his closer social circle, or that a Tremere will never even show one of his books to others. </div> </div> </div> How is it my strawman? That's what you said.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036983#post1036983\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, leeches are so united, .</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not my argument, and it seems like you are just parroting the word strawman now. My argument was merely that they have structures comparable to the Union's unity and betrayal is not literally in their blood.<br /> <br /> As far as addressing the moon base, the entire thing is a false comparison. If you are in Camarilla territory upholding a Blood Hunt, covering up a Masquerade breach, or serving as a Justicar, you can damn well expect people to help or get smacked down. They don't need moon summoned artifacts because that's not really productive to the Camarilla's goals, which are namely the protection of the Traditions. Not to mention the lack of logistics for it. But they do work together, and solidly, when it comes to facing the keeping the traditions and fighting Sabbat. The Tremere don't just ignore the Sect's enemies. If you try and openly be Sabbat, break the Masquerade, or feed in a domain without permission in Camarilla territory, see what happens. But painting Kindred as they entirely disfunctional beings misses why they even have titles in the first place. They are good at policing itself to keep them hidden. The proof is in the pudding, the Masquerade is upheld. Defy that and you might very well be declared a non-person and killed.<br /> <br /> And Sabbat packs do assist one another, they do teach each other disciplines, and they do follow their Sect hierarchy. They support the Black Hand. Have you ever read the Code of Milan? Do you know how the Vaulderie works? But same thing, go ahead and say no to the inquisitor asking for a sit-down to talk about infernalism. Tell your Bishop you don't want to help in the Crusade. See what happens. Because one of their very codes is that you put sect over personal concerns.<br /> <br /> And even more-so for the True Black Hand who I think are the best example of Cainites remaining loyal to one another. A group who has maintained their secrecy and goal for some time. Those sects function towards their goal as coherent groups, much in the same manner as the Union. Being Kindred doesn't simply mean you will necessarily turn on others in your group. And many within these groups can count on the assistance of others if needed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> More strawman. </div> </div> </div>Not really. You mention the antitribu and past conflicts as examples of sect disunity.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Camarilla is soooo United, that all of it's clans have anti tribes on the sabbat, </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> In the Sabbat... Well... Two civil Wars? </div> </div> </div>Again, this comes off as parroting because there isn't a strawman, I'm addressing a specific point here that you are claiming antitribu are evidence of Camarilla disunity. This is literally you saying the Camarilla isn't united with Antitribu as evidence. That's false because it only shows clan disunity, not sect disunity. The two are not inherently one and the same. Further, it sets up an impossible standard. There are no heavy numbers of how many Antitribu exist in comparison to their core clans. So as long as <i>some</i> exist, supposedly they are evidence of rampant disunity. Which isn't really verifiable. Again, touching back that V20 specifically leaves aspects of the Gangrel, Tremere Antitribu, and Camarilla Assamites as optional.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The Masons, the Gabrielites, those two started dissent amongst the Order of Reason. Result: persecuted and extinct. After that, the Termodinamic and Diferential Engineers (Etherite and Virtual Adepts) fled to avoid the same fate. Dissention is not tolerated within the Union; those who do not adhere are ejected. That's why those groups were cast aside. But that cleaning process keep the Union... A Union. The Etherite or VA would've broken the Time Table, they would've brought anarch. After each one of those guys left, the Union got even more united. Note that the union didn't lose power in any of those situations. </div> </div> </div> And this is just an absurd double standard. Apparently the Union can have infighting and defection and that's for the best. But when the Camarilla or Sabbat have it, that's a showing of disunity. Fact is that both organizations have history of that sorta thing. No organization is without these flaws, clearly we can see they exist in the Union as well as Kindred society in varying degrees. All you are seemingly doing is trying to white-wash Union flaws that can come up just like with anyone else. The Sabbat Civil Wars led to the Code of Milan, I'd call that a unifying aspect as well. And the True Black Hand have had even less infighting than that between them. I can very much make a case that the Sabbat Civil Wars, as well as the Hand Dispute of the TMR, have led to better Sects overall. But the point isn't to show them better than the Union, merely comparable in unity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">Do you have any idea of what the jihad is? And why ALL the kindred play it?</span></span> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">1. Jyhad, not Jihad.<br /> 2. Do you know what the word literally means? Because <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">tha<span style=\"font-family:inherit\">t remains <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">half my issue with your <span style=\"font-family:inherit\">original statement. </span></span></span></span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:inherit\"><span style=\"font-family:inherit\">3. They don't. </span></span>Point of fact, all Kindred do not necessarily participate in the Jyhad. And those that do are interested in countless goals that do not relate inherently with being a Kindred.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12552,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","user":"Monalfie","date":". 01-24-2017, 09:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T02:55:55-08:00","id":1037104,"title":"","content":"Each of the Conventions possesses their own goals for the Ascension, and they are quite willing to do anything (and I mean anything) to make sure that the ideals of the other four Conventions do not shape the final form of the Ascension (look at the relationship between the Syndicate and Pentex). In addition, the East Asian, Southeast Asian, and South Asian Technocrats belong to the Five Metal Dragons, each of which have their own goals separate from their 'parent' Convention and each of which have a Mage population equal to their parent Conventions. The only reason why the Union exists seems to be that the Conventions just loathe the Mages outside the Union more than they dislike Mages within the Union.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T07:15:07-08:00","id":1037182,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The only reason why the Union exists seems to be that the Conventions just loathe the Mages outside the Union more than they dislike Mages within the Union. </div> </div> </div>lol. Incidentally, this it's why the Traditions exist too!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think something got lost through the process. I know how primium and devices work. Primium is a passive resistance, something you could slap on things as armor. I was talking about some kind of active device, which disrupts werewolf magic, or defends technocratic constructs and agents from messing with. It could be done with, again, ridiculous amounts of primium, but how else? Which spheres would be used to make such device?<br /> <br /> I'm thinking of spirit/enthropy, maybe matter and prime to fuel it.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as the Anti Gift Generator goes. It may not be easy to do. It depends a lot on how the ST rules magick in general and Gifts in particular.<br /> With Spirit 4 you can disrupt the conection between the spiritual that the Garou have, adding up to +3 to the difficulty of Gifts. Making them more difficult, and making Primium more effective (as it will have to counter less successes). Adding Prime at 4-5 could create a more effective dampening field altering the supernatural energies that enact the Gift.<br /> <br /> This kind of effect won't affect gifts that don't require a roll, however. One of the many problems of crossover it's that Mage assumes everything magical that wasn't already casted requires a roll. This isn't true for other games. This adds to the problem of assuming that you will have to counter a single Trait (Arete), while most games use Attribute + Skill.<br /> In contrast, Werewolf assume that you ain't going to need to counter every power, thus they don't have many &quot;countermagick style&quot; rules. These are added by Mage (in M20), and if they are a bit reviled (by me among others) it's because of how they're worded, rather than by the general spirit of making other splats less vulnerable to the many magely &quot;you die, no save&quot; buttons .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:13:15-08:00","id":1037223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037182#post1037182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">These are added by Mage (in M20), and if they are a bit reviled (by me among others)<u> it's because of how they're worded</u>, rather than by the general spirit of making other splats less vulnerable to the many magely &quot;you die, no save&quot; buttons .</div> </div> </div> </div>Indeed. I have problems with static supernatural gifts counterspelling True Magick in a <i>pure</i> Mage game, simply because of the theme of how True Magick works by breaking reality (And thus no static power can be prepared for it, as the very same power is part of the Matrix that gets broken). In turn, True Magick also can't actually counterspell linear powers, only go effect-vs-effect to disrupt them, IMO. After all, True Magick can't counterspell normal reality events.<br /> <br /> However, in a <i>True Crossover (TM)</i> I absolutely have no issue with True Magick being counterspellable by linear powers ( and vice versa ) simply for the sake of balance and fairness between splats. That's a-okay.<br /> <br /> The only thing I <b>do</b> have an issue with is how most of those rules directly pit an usually very tiny Arete pool versus a potentially 8-dice attribute+ability pool that even a starting out-of-chargen non-Mage character can have. It's senseless. It makes a starting linear splat easily counterspell an Archmage.<br /> <br /> Yet there is such a simple solution to that: The best rule I've found so far way actually Mage...seeecond edition? I don't quite remember, but basically it said that Arete-vs-linear-power counterspelling simply takes the arete roll result <b>x2</b>. As I see Mage characters going up to an Arete of 5 as a limit for &quot;normal&quot; characters, that roughly equals the attribute+ability pool max of around 10 that other normal-level linear splats can have, and is IMO the best solution. It's simple, it's fair.<br /> <br /> Elders/Methuselas/Arete 6+ Mages are their own league, but the rule makes them match up as well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":6606,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","user":"Ambrosia","date":". 01-24-2017, 01:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T08:25:52-08:00","id":1037231,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036990#post1036990\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's far easier to simply use Mind 4 to remove the Mind of your victim from their body, and Prime 2 to physically assault it and shred it into pieces, leaving a lobotomized carcass behind. And, while in Astral projection, the Mage can have the upper hand, since the might Garou or unholy Vampire won't have aggravated soaking abilities nor natural weapons (and the Mage can use pure etherial swords to strike directly their mental patterns). In that terrain, a Mage have a strong advantage</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> How do you assault someone with prime 2? Doesn't it only enchant things to deal agg? I'm under the impression that prime 3, not prime 2, can be used to utilize quinessential energies against someone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12664-kingjohn","name":"KingJohn","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:01:34-08:00","id":1037296,"title":"","content":"In M20 you need Prime 3 to do direct damage with Prime. In previous editions it was Prime 2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:17:18-08:00","id":1037306,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037296#post1037296\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In M20 you need Prime 3 to do direct damage with Prime. In previous editions it was Prime 2.</div> </div> </div> </div>Good to know. I always did used that effect as Prime 3 as a house rule, since it doesn't make sense for it to be Prime 2 and because it's too powerful for a level 2 Sphere. I'm glady to know they made that change","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T11:21:56-08:00","id":1037309,"title":"","content":"However, you can use Prime 2 and a point of Quintessence to make that Mind 4 attack aggravated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can still *enhance* normally non-aggravated spell damage with Prime 2 to aggravated levels.<br /> <br /> You just need Prime 3 if you want the Prime sphere to do aggravated Prime-Bolts on its own.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:03:25-08:00","id":1037340,"title":"","content":"Prime 2 does let you &quot;Rub The Bones&quot;, disrupting the target's pattern and dealing Bashing damage. This Effect I think has been around since 2nd Ed, and HDYDT reiterated it for M20.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:06:21-08:00","id":1037343,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037104#post1037104\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Each of the Conventions possesses their own goals for the Ascension, and they are quite willing to do anything (and I mean anything) to make sure that the ideals of the other four Conventions do not shape the final form of the Ascension (look at the relationship between the Syndicate and Pentex). In addition, the East Asian, Southeast Asian, and South Asian Technocrats belong to the Five Metal Dragons, each of which have their own goals separate from their 'parent' Convention and each of which have a Mage population equal to their parent Conventions. The only reason why the Union exists seems to be that the Conventions just loathe the Mages outside the Union more than they dislike Mages within the Union.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yet, the Union will still remain the ONLY group in the WoD in which the clan/tribe (White Wolf love to make those small little &quot;families&quot; of supernaturals... They even tryed to do that with wraiths using the Guilds, but in that one they failed) will be CONSTANTLY producing valuable resources (Qui La Machine starships, enhanced cyborgs, plasma weapons, glasses with HUD screens connected to the Web, and many many others) for ANOTHER supernatural &quot;family&quot; within the same group/sect.<br /> <br /> I mean, a Son of Gaia could convince an Uktena to make him a fetish, the Ventrue prince can ask the local Tremere regent to place some wards on his lair, and a Satyr can ask a Troll for assistance, or a Celestial Chorus can give a blesses sword to a worthy Verbena.<br /> <br /> But all that is done most of the times on indivual scales, not as a whole. The Technocracy however, is very different.<br /> <br /> The agent on the frontlines will be using a highly sophisticated glass Device, which he didn't made.<br /> <br /> His car filled with Primium, were also made by some masters on the sky that he never met.<br /> <br /> His bulletproof suit too.<br /> <br /> Most likely, the vast majority of agents don't have any knowledge on Prime... Heck, most aren't even awaken<br /> <br /> Still, an agent can hope to make a request for special equipment... And receive it.<br /> <br /> That kind of cooperation is unique in the WoD... Most traditional mages at earlier stages, for instante, won't even have a Node to work on, or a good Sanctum/Lab to develop. An agent however, can hope to have a huge infrastructure and backup for him to manage his work.<br /> <br /> One of the things that must be understand is how the idea of the Technocracy evolved since the 1ed in the 90's. At that time, they REALLY were a misterious shadowy organization; no &quot;Guide to the Big Brother&quot;. They were the enemies, the emontionless machine-like men who's sole purpose were to hunt down the &quot;freedom fighters&quot; Mages. As such, they truly were EVERYWHERE.<br /> <br /> Since that, many things changed. First of all, they were changed into &quot;not THAT bad&quot;. And became playable characters. So, all that &quot;human experimentation&quot;... Well, that's because of the Computer in Authoctonia... Oh, the Sindics problems is due to the Pentex infiltration... And so on.<br /> <br /> So, after that reshaping, the Union changed a lot... And ceased to be the &quot;Big Brother&quot; to become just another critter in the WoD... Oh, the Technocracy is bad? Well, Pentex is worse... You know what? Those Void Engeneers guys aren't that bad after all... Well, we can even ally with them once in a while. And on many metaplots, you can see nonsensical things like &quot;techies+tradi&quot; alliances... That would be akin to allying with Hitler to fight Stalin (althouth, I do have to admit that allying with Stalin to fight Hitler were just as bad). Now, you can find, on many occasions, players who don't really wanna send firebolts on techie asses all the time, but rather would prefer to establish some common ground with them (and if you play with techies, you can find the reverse situation too). That was completely ridiculous at the original sources of the game... They had NO reedemable qualities what so ever at the beggining. They were a charicature of the modern western world, mirrored with the worse of it, to be a cinical critical view of our society, a vision very 90's (were scientists are souless elitists that have no concerns whatsoever about the common people, Engeneers are part of the machine that enslave all, and astronauts are selfish bastards that spend money which could be used to feed the poor, and so on). Hell, look the first editions of the conventions books... The Progenitor for example, wanted to make a drug to destroy people's souls to avoid awakenings (it would make people a little autistic.. But who cares right?).<br /> <br /> Another thing: that idea were NEVER meant to be includes on crossover metaplots. The Union were never meant to vaporize god-like vampires using spacial orbitting Ion Cannons. They were made as enemies for MAGES. They weren't supposed to be running after your Garou char in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> So, it needed a lot of rework to make them appealing for people, and to be able to work in a crossover world","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:10:39-08:00","id":1037347,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ambrosia</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037309#post1037309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">However, you can use Prime 2 and a point of Quintessence to make that Mind 4 attack aggravated <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> You can still *enhance* normally non-aggravated spell damage with Prime 2 to aggravated levels.<br /> <br /> You just need Prime 3 if you want the Prime sphere to do aggravated Prime-Bolts on its own.</div> </div> </div> </div>The difference is that, with (now) Prime 3, you can throw a super HADOUKEN or super kamehameha if you keep concentrating your cosmus for a few rounds...<br /> <br /> Or, you can make a light saber with a gazillion successes that does 10^10000000000 damage and could cut black holes on half","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:39:27-08:00","id":1037366,"title":"","content":"Not really, every roll past the first for a specific effect increases the difficulty by one, at least in Revised (each failed roll on a ritual effect). If you have Arete 3 and Prime 3 and wanted to make a Hadouken, you would have to make a difficulty 7 roll, with a minimum number of successes equal to one (for targeting another Pattern) plus one for every two health levels of damage plus one for aggravated damage. Since you are not directly targeting the Pattern of the target with Prime, your target gets a chance to dodge.<br /> <br /> So, let us say you wanted to destroy one of the Kindred. You would need to get a minimum of six successes (one for targeting another Pattern and five successes for eight health levels of aggravated damage). We will assume that the Mage is spending one point of Willpower and one point of Quintessence per roll, as Willpower and Quintessence are difficult to recover, in addition to the one point of Quintessence required to charge the aggravated damage effect. The effect then will take three turns to cast (using average values), with difficulty 6 for the first roll, difficulty 7 for the second roll, and difficulty 8 for the third roll (+1 difficulty for every two other magical effects ongoing). <br /> <br /> Now, the utility for a Mage is that the range of the effect is LoS (when they are not using Correspondence), so a Mage on the roof of a skyscraper can do massive amounts of damage. If the Mage is an assassin, all they need is LoS to their target and three turns to cast the effect. Now, any supernatural creature with Awareness will have a chance to detect that they are being targeted, so they might be able to dodge, but any mundane (or any mundane object) will be unable to dodge because they will not detect the effect. So a beginning Mage character with Arete 3, Prime 3, Avatar 5, and Willpower 10 would be one of the most frightening assassins in the cWoD because they could easily kill people mortals without leaving any evidence of the kill (though they would still suck in close combat), but they would start attracting attention if they made too many impossible kills in a given area during a given interval.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T12:54:26-08:00","id":1037376,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>KingJohn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1036937#post1036937\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey,<br /> <br /> A mage could, theoretically, pull off a Freddy Krueger effect and invade the dreams of a Vampire or Garou, kill him in his dreams (which would translate over to the real world, using life 3 or whatever sphere). I assume if that mage had mind 3 or 4, he'd be able to shift and manipulate the dreams to his liking, making said Vampire or Garou powerless to fight him in the dream world.<br /> <br /> Would any of you agree?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Good luck using Mind on Night-Folk<br /> <br /> how do you do that page 117<br /> <br /> <br /> A mage who\u2019s using Mind to attack another mage has<br /> an automatic difficulty of that target\u2019s Willpower + 3,<br /> thanks to the mental shielding techniques that mages<br /> learn as part of their training.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 The Storyteller may assume that the same rule holds true<br /> for Night-Folk, certain of whom \u2013 like elder creatures,<br /> or vampires with the Dominate Discipline \u2013 may have<br /> a difficulty of Willpower + 5 instead.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 A roll to influence several mages or Night-Folk at once<br /> is difficulty 8 (Willpower 5 + 3) if the caster is being<br /> clever and sneaky about his influence, and difficulty 10<br /> (Willpower 5 + 5) if he\u2019s being blatant about it.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 If one target in that group has a Willpower that\u2019s higher<br /> than 5, then the difficulty is that character\u2019s Willpower<br /> + 3 or + 5. And if that takes the difficulty over 10, then<br /> the Optional Rule of Thresholds takes over. (See Mage<br /> 20, Chapter Eight, p. 387.) Essentially, that dominant<br /> character exerts his influence over the \u201cpack,\u201d making<br /> it harder for the mage to influence them all. Yes, this<br /> all makes it pretty damned hard to influence a pack of<br /> vampires with the Mind Sphere, especially if their leader<br /> is especially Will-full, understands Dominate, or both.<br /> <br /> <br /> \u2022 If the caster is trying to use magickal Mind-force to compel<br /> Night-Folk to do things they do not want to do (as in being<br /> an \u201cUnwilling Target\u201d to Puppetry, as described below),<br /> then the difficulty gets the usual +3 modifier in addition<br /> to the other difficulty modifiers \u2013 that is, +6, +8, or highest<br /> Willpower + 6 or + 8. Yes, this supersedes the usual limits<br /> on difficulty modifiers, and yes it makes it very hard to<br /> force Night-Folk to perform acts they are not willing to<br /> perform. Sorry, but Count Dracula is not your bitch.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Plus you have to get past their innate counter-magick","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:02:04-08:00","id":1037381,"title":"","content":"My, that is some fearsome difficulty penalties.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:09:49-08:00","id":1037388,"title":"","content":"By the way, when people talk about how the Union is so united and solid and all hugs together in a joyfull alliance, are we still talking of the Union who purged the Cabal of Pure Tought, or the one where the Ksirafai reinvented themselves as House Jannissaries, or the one which once had among its members the Virtual Adepts and the Sons of the Ether, or again the one that in Revised Edition is on the verge of a civil war between the NWO and the Syndicate? The same Union where the Void Engineers have a foot outside the door because they do not give a damn about the Pogrom and are all kisses and hugs with the Euthanatos? Or again the one where the Progenitors are hindering and sabotaging the higher ups of the other convetions to avoid the civil war?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just saying...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:25:04-08:00","id":1037397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037381#post1037381\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My, that is some fearsome difficulty penalties.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah and that's just the tip of the iceberg, Mage use success based system, so aside from the difficulty of the task you need to achieve enough base success to activate the effect.<br /> <br /> Possessing some one requires 2 success per point of willpower of the victim, if he has a willpower equal to 6 or higher, if his willpower is lesser than 6 you need 10 success.<br /> <br /> This is for possession; changing memories of a victim would be 3 success for a little change and 5 for a greater rewriting.<br /> <br /> So...how many success would require a psychic assault that must kill the victim?<br /> <br /> In any case a mental attack can be repelled with a willpower roll, so you have to stack enough success at an uncanny base difficult and get past the willpower rolls of the victim.<br /> <br /> <br /> It's faster to nuke the town where the Night-folk lives, really.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 04:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T13:57:20-08:00","id":1037408,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037388#post1037388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">By the way, when people talk about how the Union is so united and solid and all hugs together in a joyfull alliance, are we still talking of the Union who purged the Cabal of Pure Tought, or the one where the Ksirafai reinvented themselves as House Jannissaries, or the one which once had among its members the Virtual Adepts and the Sons of the Ether, or again the one that in Revised Edition is on the verge of a civil war between the NWO and the Syndicate? The same Union where the Void Engineers have a foot outside the door because they do not give a damn about the Pogrom and are all kisses and hugs with the Euthanatos? Or again the one where the Progenitors are hindering and sabotaging the higher ups of the other convetions to avoid the civil war?<br /> <br /> <br /> Just saying...</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that it is the same Union <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />. The key thing about the Union is that it is as united as any other group of people who suffer from megalomania, narcissism, and borderline personality disorder (which means that its members will stab each other in the back whenever they consider it within their best interest, regardless of the cost to their larger group). Honestly, the most stable group in the Union are the Void Engineers, and that is not exactly high praise considering how many of them are secretly Nephandi who dress up as aliens and jump into their spacecraft so they can covertly rape the mundanes...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:05:38-08:00","id":1037412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037366#post1037366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, every roll past the first for a specific effect increases the difficulty by one, at least in Revised (each failed roll on a ritual effect). If you have Arete 3 and Prime 3 and wanted to make a Hadouken, you would have to make a difficulty 7 roll, with a minimum number of successes equal to one (for targeting another Pattern) plus one for every two health levels of damage plus one for aggravated damage. Since you are not directly targeting the Pattern of the target with Prime, your target gets a chance to dodge.<br /> <br /> So, let us say you wanted to destroy one of the Kindred. You would need to get a minimum of six successes (one for targeting another Pattern and five successes for eight health levels of aggravated damage). We will assume that the Mage is spending one point of Willpower and one point of Quintessence per roll, as Willpower and Quintessence are difficult to recover, in addition to the one point of Quintessence required to charge the aggravated damage effect. The effect then will take three turns to cast (using average values), with difficulty 6 for the first roll, difficulty 7 for the second roll, and difficulty 8 for the third roll (+1 difficulty for every two other magical effects ongoing). <br /> <br /> Now, the utility for a Mage is that the range of the effect is LoS (when they are not using Correspondence), so a Mage on the roof of a skyscraper can do massive amounts of damage. If the Mage is an assassin, all they need is LoS to their target and three turns to cast the effect. Now, any supernatural creature with Awareness will have a chance to detect that they are being targeted, so they might be able to dodge, but any mundane (or any mundane object) will be unable to dodge because they will not detect the effect. So a beginning Mage character with Arete 3, Prime 3, Avatar 5, and Willpower 10 would be one of the most frightening assassins in the cWoD because they could easily kill people mortals without leaving any evidence of the kill (though they would still suck in close combat), but they would start attracting attention if they made too many impossible kills in a given area during a given interval.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thats not correct. The dif only increases increase by 1 on rituals if you fail any one roll; a begginer char can, thus, keep it up safely for 5 turns by spending will points each turn before casting. Now, about the dif, some considerations<br /> <br /> -each quintessence lowers dif by 1<br /> -if your foci is unique, it also lowers your dif by 1<br /> -if it is something you have dedicated a lot of study, also lowers by 1<br /> -if the effect has a compatible ressonance with the Mage, also lowers by 1<br /> <br /> So, if Im an Etherite that use my lightsaber (I have PhD in stable laser optics on the Victorian University in Concordia), and can only use it with crystals from Saturn's Rings and my ressonamce is mostly Pattern (Laser), that would be a Vulgar dif 4 effect to me.<br /> <br /> But that is useless talk, since I can bet my target wont wait for we to overcharge my saber...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T14:34:58-08:00","id":1037424,"title":"","content":"Yes, rituals only suffer a difficulty increase with failed rolls, but rituals usually take hours while spells usually take turns (Revised, p. 150). The paradox that Mages will receive from botching a ritual roll after the Mage already has a couple dozens successes will probably kill the Mage straight out or send the Mage into a Quiet so deep that the Mage might have trouble existing outside of the Deep Umbra. Since the Mage in question will have botched a roll to overcharge a lightsaber, the Mage is probably a fan of Star Wars and his Quiet will probably make him believe that he is a Jedi acting on behalf of the Old Republic (if he thinks that the Traditions are the Old Republic) or acting against the Empire (if he thinks that the Union is the Empire).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T16:35:46-08:00","id":1037471,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037015#post1037015\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You're missing to part where it's Mages that are attacking. That means the other Supernaturals have to lay down and die, unable to defend themselves.<br /> Honestly with that sort of logic there should be no enemies left alive that aren't also Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>You're missing the part where that is <i>one weapons system. </i>It requires Life 3 and ten successes to build and then can do that as many times a day as you feel like as long as you have the PE to fuel it. How hard do you think it is for the Union, the single largest gathering of mages on Earth to produce enough of these to carpet bomb a Sept into nothingness within a few turns?<br /> <br /> Add onto that, ACTUAL technological weapons. Open up with the Neutron pattern disruptor to take out key defenders, follow up with carpet bombing under the guise of 'terrorism'. Napalm does up to 10 dice of damage a turn, for ten turns. A 120 Millimeter cannon does 20 dice of damage from a RIDICULOUS distance. Bombs? A block of C-4 does 20 dice of damage per block losing one die for every yard away from the epicenter of the blast it travels. Imagine a crate of that, dropped into your sept at night while everyone is sleeping. Antimatter? Ehehehehaahahahaha.<br /> <br /> The union's offensive capabilities are quite frankly <i>ridiculous.</i> There is a reason why they use the <i>US MILITARY</i> as their cover story when they go out in force. Which is why Mage is largely not about walking up to the local Construct and giving them what-for. It's about sneaking around and hitting them where they aren't looking.<br /> <br /> The Union, quite rightly, considers other splats nonthreatening because quite frankly, they <i>are</i> non threatening in most cases. Circumstance can make them dangerous. But in an up and up war? They would be exterminated in a heartbeat. The problem is the Union doesn't have the manpower to both devote to that, and the traditions and since the traditions are the ones who actually have a shot at knocking the union off their pedestal, guess who get's the bullseye?<br /> <br /> A Typical Sept is somewhere around 15 Garou and their Kinfolk. They get bigger of course. But that's the average. The only source I could find on Garou Septs was that they were 'numerous' with over 300 Septs in the USA, including Alaska and Hawaii.<br /> <br /> Over 300, to me, says that there's more than three hundred, but less than 350. So. Even generously giving the Garou 400 Septs in the USA. That's still 6,000 werewolves. Vs WELL OVER A MILLION soldiers and the industrial complex that backs them up. Along side reality smashing superscience.<br /> <br /> The Salvation War series covered how this goes. A little bit of healing will not help you if you bring medieval or pre-medieval warfare to bear against a more advanced military.<br /> <br /> The ONLY REASON this hasn't happened is because the Union considers the Garou a nuisance at worst.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:05:38-08:00","id":1037490,"title":"","content":"Strangely enough though, the Garou are actually a credible threat because they can attack the Technocrats six ways to Sunday. The Garou do not consider the Technocrats as an immediate threat though, as they are more concerned with the Wyrm than the Weaver. If they ever found out that the Technocrats were responsible for Pentex (which is one of the big secrets in cWoD), they would probably change their mind.<br /> <br /> You have cyborgs and tanks? No problem, Garou use Jam Technology to make it so even your knives cannot cut.<br /> <br /> You have orbital weapons? No problem, Garou can personally go up there and wreck your technology by just stepping off through the Aetherial Realm and the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> You want to carpet bomb a Caern? No problem, Garou can summon a Nameless and compel it to take the name of one of your installations, removing it from existence and going off like a nuclear weapon.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats may think they rule the world, but the rest of the splats really do not care. If the Garou Nation ever felt that the Technocrats were an existential threat, the Technocrats would be in trouble. And we are not even discussing the damage that the elder Kindred of the Camarilla could do, which could be much more devestating to the Technocracy. How many members of the Technocracy could survive Auspex 8 (Psychic Assault) from a 5th generation Kindred with Manipulation 8 and Intimidation 8?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T17:36:35-08:00","id":1037507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037366#post1037366\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not really, every roll past the first for a specific effect increases the difficulty by one, at least in Revised (each failed roll on a ritual effect). If you have Arete 3 and Prime 3 and wanted to make a Hadouken, you would have to make a difficulty 7 roll, with a minimum number of successes equal to one (for targeting another Pattern) plus one for every two health levels of damage plus one for aggravated damage. Since you are not directly targeting the Pattern of the target with Prime, your target gets a chance to dodge.</div> </div> </div> </div>That seems really involved. I'll just stick to Focus maneuvers, I guess.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:21:34-08:00","id":1037538,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037490#post1037490\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Strangely enough though, the Garou are actually a credible threat because they can attack the Technocrats six ways to Sunday. The Garou do not consider the Technocrats as an immediate threat though, as they are more concerned with the Wyrm than the Weaver. If they ever found out that the Technocrats were responsible for Pentex (which is one of the big secrets in cWoD), they would probably change their mind.<br /> <br /> You have cyborgs and tanks? No problem, Garou use Jam Technology to make it so even your knives cannot cut.<br /> <br /> You have orbital weapons? No problem, Garou can personally go up there and wreck your technology by just stepping off through the Aetherial Realm and the Deep Umbra.<br /> <br /> You want to carpet bomb a Caern? No problem, Garou can summon a Nameless and compel it to take the name of one of your installations, removing it from existence and going off like a nuclear weapon.<br /> <br /> The Technocrats may think they rule the world, but the rest of the splats really do not care. If the Garou Nation ever felt that the Technocrats were an existential threat, the Technocrats would be in trouble. And we are not even discussing the damage that the elder Kindred of the Camarilla could do, which could be much more devestating to the Technocracy. How many members of the Technocracy could survive Auspex 8 (Psychic Assault) from a 5th generation Kindred with Manipulation 8 and Intimidation 8?</div> </div> </div> </div>Jam Technology works within 50 feet. They're dead if they get within roughly 2000 yards.<br /> <br /> They step sideways and get shot by the weapons systems that can phase into alternate realities.<br /> <br /> Spirit Wards. As far as spirits are concerned, Technocratic strongholds never existed to start with. Part and parcel with the standard Technocratic Construct status.<br /> <br /> How many 5th generation Kindred are there? Not that many. That's how many. Not to mention that Auspex 8 is both nonlethal, and easily countered with a mental ward. I hope they enjoy their botches. Assuming they can even get close enough to use it. Because again. Dead at 2000 yards.<br /> <br /> The point is this. Werewolf is on an entirely different scale and story type than mage. It is wholly unequipped for a full scale crossover with the mage setting. Werewolves are scary. Werewolves are threatening. Werewolves are not in any way an existential threat.<br /> <br /> Vampire is actually, a lot better equipped to deal with Mage than Garou are. Simply because of a combination of being secretive by default and being intermingled with the civilian populace, making brute force tactics difficult.<br /> <br /> Garou on the other hand live in hippie camps in the woods like 'noble savages' Where they are a giant glowing target for bombing<br /> <br /> And while the Garou and Vampires are forced to send their best and brightest, their most powerful mystics to the front lines to pull their tricks. The Union, (And quite frankly the traditions as well though it's not as emphasized in their lore because most are mystics rather than technomancers.) can just grab joe schmoe off the street who's good with a gun. Load him down with technomagickal gizmos and have a potent fighter.<br /> <br /> This is why they would lose. Because mage, as a setting, can afford to lose a few people. It won't hurt them in the long run. But every 5th generation Kindred that gets fried? There is no replacing them. Every Garou is important to your cause and every one you lose is an important genetic asset lost. You will run out of troops long before the Mages do. Because the mages can make ANYONE a super soldier. They can make ANYONE able to hurl fireballs the size of a volkswagon. They can make anyone able to roll 4 dice on any skill they happen to need at the moment.<br /> <br /> Mages aren't powerful because they can uber-buff themselves or vaporize people with a funny look, though they can. They're powerful because their abilities uniquely allow them to industrialize supernatural mojo. A powerful mage doesn't need to personally walk into a Garou caern and engage the alpha in hand to hand combat. He can round up a dozen followers. Hand them a few plasma cannons and a hover-ship and tell them to get to it. And if they fail? So what! He can do it again next week. And the week after that. and be no worse off than he was before.<br /> <br /> Garou can only boost their numbers via babies. Which is hard to get when your tiny population is busy being decimated against an equally deadly foe that outnumbers you 166 to 1.<br /> <br /> Vampires can only boost their numbers via the embrace, which while allowing for greater numbers of vampires, also creates progressively weaker vampires as you go down, meaning they're very very vulnerable to decapitation attacks. You wipe out the upper echelons of vampires? It's <i>over.</i> There is no coming back from that. Admittedly Vampires are, for aforementoned reasons much more of a problem to take on than Garou.<br /> <br /> <br /> The fact that they're weaker, in a fair head on fight, does not mean they're insignificant or even weak. It's a difference in scale. Werewolf isn't about the same things as Mage. Mage is about Humans can do anything if they put their mind to it. Werewolf is about super-powered furred captain planets literally fighting an evil spirit god that causes pollution, hatred, and people who talk in the theater in personal honor duels for the soul of the planet.<br /> <br /> And the simple fact of the matter is that the setting itself has it's reasons for the Technocracy simply not being ABLE to wage a war of Genocide on either Vampires or Garou. Much like the Traditions aren't able. And in some cases aren't even willing.<br /> <br /> Those reasons aren't &quot;The garou are too powerful to take on.&quot; Those reasons are &quot;The Garou are too troublesome to take on.&quot; They're just hard enough to kill that it's not in the budget to do so.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:38:19-08:00","id":1037547,"title":"","content":"yeah yeah, uber death ray cannon stomps everything, how boring.<br /> <br /> Since we have reached pure fictional hypotesis just for the fun of it Technocracy is dead, because malkavian methuselah have destroyed all their compounds with psychic nuke bombs trown at miles of distance using Auspex and Dementation, after few seconds everyone in the structure start frenzy and the construct becomes Rapture from bioshock.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the 4th gen Methuselahs of the Lasombra Clan have just pulled the abyss out of their pants and now all the bases of the Technocracy are floating into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> And all the stations in the orbit falls down, because a lazy 4th gen Ravnos has just decided that gravity will not work anymore near the station, or that the oxygen in the above mentioned station is going to transform in cyanide, and he has done this at miles of distance because auspex, animalism or possession or just a bit of thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe the director of the construct has just pushed the self-destruction button, because a Ventrue methusealh somewhere in Hong Kong has used Domination 3 to reforge his memory and turn him in a manchurian candidate.<br /> <br /> Or maybe a Nosferatu methuselah is killing everybody without being seen because his obfuscate levels are too high to be pierced.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Tremere Inner Council just pulled a level 9 ritual that makes worldwide the effect of the ritual machine blitz, and so every construct in the world stops working, and if you are in the space good luck without life-support systems.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Japheth or Lazarus have just opened a gate for army of wraiths into the construct, safely from the shadowlands,who knows.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Ur-Shulgi just killed everybody because he has infinite powers<br /> <br /> <br /> And everything the Technocracy will do has already been forseen, because many methuselahs have INT 9, so everything these mages can think has already been tought by some elder leech, or maybe it's just Ausepx 8 that let you see the future, who knows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe the Antedeluvians have just destroyed them all, who knows, Haqim use Quietus 10, all the Technocrats in the world start screaming because their blood is boiling, no dice to roll, no counter magick,it's the rule, if the Ante want's it,it happens, it just work because Haqim will. Or maybe every construct on the Earth is swallowed by Ennoia, because, you know, she's the planet now, or maybe Malkav just made all the Technocrats a bunch of Marauders,again, who knows.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Zhyzhak has just summoned the Green Dragon, or maybe the Werewolves have summoned another Incarna to destroy the Technocracy,and they die because no one can win against an Incarna<br /> <br /> Can we stop this childish act?<br /> <br /> <br /> It is stated all over again and again that the Technocrats simply cannot do these kind of things, that they do not have resources to destroy the other splats, it's in the books, well written, there are lot of examples of Technocrats who bite the dust, it is heavily stated that the Union simply lack the firepower to do what you are suggesting, and it is written also in the Technocray Convention Books and guides. So, what are we talking about?<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 09:45 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:46:32-08:00","id":1037556,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037547#post1037547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">y<br /> And everything the Technocracy will do has already been forseen, because many methuselahs have INT 9, so everything these mages can think has already been tought by some elder leech, or maybe it's just Ausepx 8 that let you see the future, who knows.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Antedeluvians have just destroyed them all, who knows, Haqim use Quietus 10, all the Technocrats in the world start screaming because their blood is boiling, no dice to roll, no counter magick,it's the rule, if the Ante want's it,it happens, it just work because Haqim will. Or maybe every construct on the Earth is swallowed by Ennoia, because, you know, she's the planet now, or maybe Malkav just made all the Technocrats a bunch of Marauders,again, who knows.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> See, you <i>say</i> that, but the scoreboard reflects a different reality:<br /> <div align=\"center\"><b>Antediluvians killed by a Technocracy: 1<br /> <br /> Technocracies killed by an Antediluvian: 0</b></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:51:18-08:00","id":1037560,"title":"","content":"Yeah, a frenzied Antediluvian who had fought for three days and three nights against three of the most powerful bodhisattva in the world, facing an army of wraiths in the meanwhile. He wasn't even focusing on the Technocracy.<br /> <br /> Oh, by the way, you should read again Night of the Prophecy, there was plenty of dead Technocrats on the field.<br /> <br /> And killing him just caused the loss of all the amalgams and constructs not on Earth for the subsequent Avatar-storm. Cheap, wasn't it?<br /> <br /> Even more: you sure he is dead? Ravana in Ten Thousand hells seemed quite in good shape if you ask me.<br /> <br /> There is a reason if Iteration X has forseen the extintion of the human race in a matter of decades.<br /> Ascension, page 192<br /> <br /> <br /> If the Technocracy is so strong than you must explain why their statistic says that they are going to lose in a matter of decades.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 10:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T18:53:18-08:00","id":1037562,"title":"","content":"Is it really childish to point out that Mage and Werewolf operate on very fundamentally different setting conceits? Differences that are not immediately obvious due to the fact the way the games are typically played are not dissimilar and the setting information that paints the picture is somewhat obscure?<br /> <br /> in both cases, you have a team of 3-5 people, each with their own special powers who run around having adventures. Because that's what you <i>do</i> when you tabletop game. So you go &quot;Oh hey, there are these guys with powers that seem to counter mages. Cool.&quot;<br /> <br /> I like the Union. I will freely admit to that, I am a TOTAL Union fanboy.<br /> <br /> But the reason the Union is strong isn't munchkin tricks. It's because the union operates on a modernized industrial scale. They don't make a relic uberweapon and hand it down to the champion of the convention.<br /> <br /> No. They build 2000 slightly less good ones and pass them out to every soldier on the front lines.<br /> <br /> You don't <i>see</i> this outside of the fluff. Because that's not the way the game is played. The game is played with small teams of 3-5 people. With fleshed out characters who all know each other and generally have some plot they follow.<br /> <br /> They have some unique rules that are cool and help to represent this facet but it's not really the same as looking it straight in the face.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:04:32-08:00","id":1037565,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037471#post1037471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The ONLY REASON this hasn't happened is because the Union considers the Garou a nuisance at worst.</div> </div> </div> </div>So like I said:<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">That means the other Supernaturals have to lay down and die, unable to defend themselves.<br /> Honestly with that sort of logic there should be no enemies left alive that aren't also Mages.</div> </div> </div> </div>You made the same argument a while back (and sort of in this thread now that I've caught up again) dealing with Vampires (up to and including the Ante's is I remember right). In your mind, seemingly all of the WoD lives and dies on the whims of the Technocracy. If that makes sense to you, so be it. I'm not going to bother arguing. Mages are awesome. Everyone else sucks. End of story.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:25:25-08:00","id":1037577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037565#post1037565\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So like I said:<br /> <br /> You made the same argument a while back (and sort of in this thread now that I've caught up again) dealing with Vampires (up to and including the Ante's is I remember right). In your mind, seemingly all of the WoD lives and dies on the whims of the Technocracy. If that makes sense to you, so be it. I'm not going to bother arguing. Mages are awesome. Everyone else sucks. End of story.</div> </div> </div> </div>See. That's where we disagree.<br /> <br /> Just because the technocracy is <i>really good</i> at killing things, does not mean other things aren't awesome. Though I personally dislike the werewolf setting.<br /> <br /> Vampires are awesome. And in fact, out of all the other splats, I'd give Vampires the highest chance if it came to an all out war, to the point where I do not know for certain who would win, I'm leaning technocracy, but I'm quite obviously biased in that matter. : P Though I've never had the books so most of my knowledge of it is second hand. I like the setting.<br /> <br /> But, the combination of the masquerade and their relative unobtrusiveness overall combines to make the Vampires almost tolerable to the union. To the point where, even if all other factions were wiped out, I don't know if they would even bother trying to wipe out vampires rather than just integrating them with the consensus somehow.<br /> <br /> Werewolf? I..... don't like werewolf. I find it's setting obnoxious and nonsensical. I find it's characters annoying and unrelatable. I see no real appeal in playing an ALPHA MALE RAWR WEREWOLF who fights for mother nature and fucks women to make babies for mother nature and she should be HAPPY about having a mutant infant rip it's way out of her and etc etc etc. I find Kinfolk to be super depressing and honestly do not understand why so many people want to play one. So no, I can't say in total honesty that I think werewolf is awesome. In fact I'd be lying.<br /> <br /> And to be blunt, Garou act like total morons. Personally I find that to be one MORE part of the setting I hate. Because the hero's are complete unlikable assholes. Even the Union, with it's whole 'corrupt monolith' theme at least generally has good guys amongst the bad. With a genuinely good goal that's off kilter a bit and needs fixing. With werewolf there's just nothing but a depressing slide to the apocalypse with thoroughly unlikable people.<br /> <br /> Changeling on the other hand? Very awesome! I love changeling. Not quite as much as mage, but still. Again this is one that I haven't played.<br /> <br /> Wraith, I have a non-opinion on. As I know less than nothing about it. As in, what I know about it is probably wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:28:00-08:00","id":1037578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037560#post1037560\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, a frenzied Antediluvian who had fought for three days and three nights against three of the most powerful bodhisattva in the world, facing an army of wraiths in the meanwhile. He wasn't even focusing on the Technocracy.</div> </div> </div> </div>The trophy in the Hall of Fame only cares about who got the kill shot in, son.<br /> <br /> <b>[Ravnos] -- February 1, 2000, by ORBITAL SPACE MIRRORS</b>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:32:20-08:00","id":1037582,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037578#post1037578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The trophy in the Hall of Fame only cares about who got the kill shot in, son.<br /> <br /> <b>[Ravnos] -- February 1, 2000, by ORBITAL SPACE MIRRORS</b></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Every Technocrat outside the Earth -- Febraury 1, 2000, by the shoting at the wrong thing with Orbital Space Mirrors.<br /> <br /> MECHA,CONTROL,AUCHTONIA, Beloved homes, masters, and inspiring idols, forever in our toughts.</b><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:34:36-08:00","id":1037584,"title":"","content":"In cWoD, every splat has their own problems (Traditions versus Technocracy, Camarilla versus Sabbat, Seelie versus Unseelie, etc). While one faction could probably launch a war against another splat, they would leave themselves open to annihilation by their opposite faction for questionable gains. Yes, the Technocracy could possibly wage war against the Garou, but they would likely weaken themselves to such a degree that every other Mage faction would eat them alive. The same applies to the rest of the splats, so you end up with a five-sided Cold War (Fera vs Mage vs Vampire (Kindred and KJ) vs Wraith vs Changeling). While there are individual and local conflicts, each faction avoids all-out war with the other splats for fear of what their opposite number would do. That is why the appearance of Demons and Hunters upset things, they disturb the balance.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:35:38-08:00","id":1037586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037582#post1037582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Every Technocrat outside the Earth -- Febraury 1, 2000, By the shoting at the wrong thing with Orbital Space Mirrors.<br /> <br /> MECHA,CONTROL,AUCHTONIA, Beloved homes, masters, and inspiring idols, forever in our toughts.</b><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>We can replace those. an Antidiluvian dead, is dead forever. : P<br /> <br /> That is actually the vampires one real weak point. If you knock off the top levels of their tower, they will <i>never again</i> rise that high. They can only go down.<br /> <br /> Also for once, I have nothing really to disagree with there, Aya Tari. Agreed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:38:02-08:00","id":1037588,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037586#post1037586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> We can replace those. an Antidiluvian dead, is dead forever. : P</div> </div> </div> </div>No you can't,you should read more the Revised Edition.<br /> <br /> <br /> Umbra is lost, after the Avatar storm there will be no space construction in the spirit world.<br /> <br /> Void Engineers even need to rely on Cerberus and Ravana's Navel to get by.<br /> So no, no space stations, Avatar Storm is a bitch, as of Revised there are no Construct in the umbra,and no Technocrats in space that it is not a Void Engineer.<br /> <br /> Oh, except for Threat Null, obviously.<br /> <br /> And Control? Well, Control is gone.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> an Antidiluvian dead, is dead forever. : P </div> </div> </div><br /> Yeah, just like Tzimisce,Saulot,Lasombra and Cappadocius, death was really a problem for the...oh wait!<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 10:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com