ian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:41:58-08:00","id":1037593,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037588#post1037588\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, just like Tzimisce,Saulot,Lasombra and Cappadocius, death was really a problem for the...oh wait!</div> </div> </div> </div>I see your Tzimisce, Saulot, Lasombra, and Cappadocius, and raise you Ventrue, Troile, Set, and Ravnos. Seems like the Antediluvians die just fine as long as you don't try to diablerize them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:43:49-08:00","id":1037594,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BenjCano</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037593#post1037593\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I see your Tzimisce, Saulot, Lasombra, and Cappadocius, and raise you Ventrue, Troile, Set, and Ravnos. Seems like the Antediluvians die just fine as long as you don't try to diablerize them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Set is alive and well, he is just sleeping in Egypt because the Silent Striders cursed him. same goes for Troile in torpor well under Carthage, together with Moloch.<br /> Ventrue also is quite alive, legends says that he died at the time of the second city, saddly Alexander, his greek infant, has been embraced in 700 bc, so...<br /> <br /> As for Ravanna, I repeat, it seemed to me that he was doing quite well in Thousands Hell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander</a><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 10:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:49:23-08:00","id":1037599,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037594#post1037594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Set is alive and well, he is just sleeping in Egypt because the Silent Striders cursed him. same goes for Troile in torpor well under Carthage, together with Moloch.<br /> Ventrue also is quite alive, legends says that he died at the time of the second city, saddly Alexander, his greek infant, has been embraced in 700 bc, so...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander</a></div> </div> </div> </div>Pretty sure Set is dead as they get... even in the Gehenna scenario when his children try to revive him, they are instead slain instantly to be 'reunited' with their god.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:50:17-08:00","id":1037601,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037599#post1037599\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pretty sure Set is dead as they get... even in the Gehenna scenario when his children try to revive him, they are instead slain instantly to be 'reunited' with their god.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> And in another Ghenna Scenario he is alive and well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:52:16-08:00","id":1037603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037594#post1037594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Set is alive and well, he is just sleeping in Egypt because the Silent Striders cursed him. same goes for Troile in torpor well under Carthage, together with Moloch.<br /> Ventrue also is quite alive, legends says that he died at the time of the second city, saddly Alexander, his greek infant, has been embraced in 700 bc, so...<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander</a></div> </div> </div> </div>It's like some people didn't even read <i>Gehenna</i>. Troile and Moloch went into Torpor at the fall of Carthage in lieu of being murdered by the Roman legions. Implying, y'know, that the Roman legions <i>could have murdered them. </i>Then they got sealed in by salt and fire and that's all she wrote, boys.<br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gyazo.com/dd8567a93849d262f699b058dbd1ed55.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <img src=\"https://i.gyazo.com/9a957ed1b625adfbb291e301674dcad6.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <img src=\"https://i.gyazo.com/d00ea646091db1c652e8fa21f06fed91.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I seem to have acquired a site for running play by post games. This is unexpected and frightening and come watch either the glorious play or the magnificent train wreck:<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php\" target=\"_blank\">The Malkavian Madness Network</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1515-benjcano","name":"BenjCano","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1515_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1276"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T19:52:42-08:00","id":1037604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037547#post1037547\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">yeah yeah, uber death ray cannon stomps everything, how boring.<br /> <br /> Since we have reached pure fictional hypotesis just for the fun of it Technocracy is dead, because malkavian methuselah have destroyed all their compounds with psychic nuke bombs trown at miles of distance using Auspex and Dementation, after few seconds everyone in the structure start frenzy and the construct becomes Rapture from bioshock.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the 4th gen Methuselahs of the Lasombra Clan have just pulled the abyss out of their pants and now all the bases of the Technocracy are floating into the Abyss.<br /> <br /> And all the stations in the orbit falls down, because a lazy 4th gen Ravnos has just decided that gravity will not work anymore near the station, or that the oxygen in the above mentioned station is going to transform in cyanide, and he has done this at miles of distance because auspex, animalism or possession or just a bit of thaumaturgy.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe the director of the construct has just pushed the self-destruction button, because a Ventrue methusealh somewhere in Hong Kong has used Domination 3 to reforge his memory and turn him in a manchurian candidate.<br /> <br /> Or maybe a Nosferatu methuselah is killing everybody without being seen because his obfuscate levels are too high to be pierced.<br /> <br /> Or maybe the Tremere Inner Council just pulled a level 9 ritual that makes worldwide the effect of the ritual machine blitz, and so every construct in the world stops working, and if you are in the space good luck without life-support systems.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Japheth or Lazarus have just opened a gate for army of wraiths into the construct, safely from the shadowlands,who knows.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Ur-Shulgi just killed everybody because he has infinite powers<br /> <br /> <br /> And everything the Technocracy will do has already been forseen, because many methuselahs have INT 9, so everything these mages can think has already been tought by some elder leech, or maybe it's just Ausepx 8 that let you see the future, who knows.<br /> <br /> <br /> Or maybe the Antedeluvians have just destroyed them all, who knows, Haqim use Quietus 10, all the Technocrats in the world start screaming because their blood is boiling, no dice to roll, no counter magick,it's the rule, if the Ante want's it,it happens, it just work because Haqim will. Or maybe every construct on the Earth is swallowed by Ennoia, because, you know, she's the planet now, or maybe Malkav just made all the Technocrats a bunch of Marauders,again, who knows.<br /> <br /> Or maybe Zhyzhak has just summoned the Green Dragon, or maybe the Werewolves have summoned another Incarna to destroy the Technocracy,and they die because no one can win against an Incarna<br /> <br /> Can we stop this childish act?<br /> <br /> <br /> It is stated all over again and again that the Technocrats simply cannot do these kind of things, that they do not have resources to destroy the other splats, it's in the books, well written, there are lot of examples of Technocrats who bite the dust, it is heavily stated that the Union simply lack the firepower to do what you are suggesting, and it is written also in the Technocray Convention Books and guides. So, what are we talking about?</div> </div> </div> </div>What we are talking about, is that the MAIN concern of the Union is the Traditions first, Nephandi second, and Marauders third... And the rest after all those. The Union COULD wipe out one class of critters from the WoD... But that would be so freaking resource-time consuming, that would make them in a delicate vulnerable position against their real enemies, against the ones that are REALLY a threat to them: the Traditions. That's why the Union doesn't go an a insane crusade against those.<br /> <br /> Besides, there are too many crittters out there, just cleaning one would be meaninless, since the others would just fill the Void left... And it would SEVERELY weaken the Union.<br /> <br /> So, it's not that they can't, it's that it's not desirable to them","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:06:30-08:00","id":1037611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037582#post1037582\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Every Technocrat outside the Earth -- Febraury 1, 2000, by the shoting at the wrong thing with Orbital Space Mirrors.<br /> <br /> MECHA,CONTROL,AUCHTONIA, Beloved homes, masters, and inspiring idols, forever in our toughts.</b></div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't caused by the death of Ravnos, but by the major assaults of Traditional strongholds, mainly Doissetep and Concordia, Horizon got lost because the Avatars of MANY masters and archmages were shattered and scattered on the Umbra, creating the Avatar Storm. It had nothing to do with Ravnos.<br /> <br /> One more deed of the Technocracy: waking the Neverborn Goroon with a nuclear explosion in the Labirinth, causing the vanish of Charon, just to weaken some Nefandi.<br /> <br /> Other deeds: destruction of Doissetep and Concordia, the biggest traditionalists bastions<br /> <br /> EDIT: They also caused the sixth great maelstrom in the Underworld... Frankly, the Union became the big crossover mataplot hook for WoD on all that &quot;end of the world&quot; trash history","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-24-2017, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:16:30-08:00","id":1037618,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Undead rabbit</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037594#post1037594\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> <br /> Set is alive and well, he is just sleeping in Egypt because the Silent Striders cursed him. same goes for Troile in torpor well under Carthage, together with Moloch.<br /> Ventrue also is quite alive, legends says that he died at the time of the second city, saddly Alexander, his greek infant, has been embraced in 700 bc, so...<br /> <br /> As for Ravanna, I repeat, it seemed to me that he was doing quite well in Thousands Hell.<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander\" target=\"_blank\">http://whitewolf.wikia.com/wiki/Alexander</a><br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Troile isn't the original 3rd was he? Capadoccius IS DEAD. He turned into a wraith (don't tell me you consider a wraith as &quot;living&quot;), but were eventually destroyed by the Giovani.<br /> <br /> Saulot will end up being &quot;ejected&quot; from his infected borrowed body, tzimisce courtesy. RIP Saulot.<br /> <br /> As for Ventrue... One of his children had a lot of his blood (I forgot the name), and used it to make some 4th generations over the ages. It wasn't Ventrue embracing.<br /> <br /> But... You know... Were is the projenitor of the TRUE BRUJAH?<br /> <br /> EDIT: oh, I forgot another one... Malkav were killed by Haqim. His lunacy may still linger in his children, but that's it.<br /> <br /> So, those guys are gone for good.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12880,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","user":"Karlgust","date":". 01-24-2017, 11:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:20:25-08:00","id":1037619,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037611#post1037611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> That wasn't caused by the death of Ravnos, but by the major assaults of Traditional strongholds, mainly Doissetep and Concordia, Horizon got lost because the Avatars of MANY masters and archmages were shattered and scattered on the Umbra, creating the Avatar Storm. It had nothing to do with Ravnos.<br /> <br /> One more deed of the Technocracy: waking the Neverborn Goroon with a nuclear explosion in the Labirinth, causing the vanish of Charon, just to weaken some Nefandi.<br /> <br /> Other deeds: destruction of Doissetep and Concordia, the biggest traditionalists bastions</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.<br /> <br /> Storytelle Companion, page 15<br /> <br /> <br /> THE NUKES<br /> <b>In 1999 the Technocracy used neutron missiles and<br /> orbiting mirrors to reduce the Ravnos Antediluvian vampire<br /> (the oldest of its bloodline) to dust. That much maybe either<br /> rumor or common knowledge among some Tradition mages<br /> at this point. What is not well known is that the Technocrats<br /> also detonated a spirit nuke in the Labyrinth at the same<br /> time, and a relic nuke from Stygia destroyed Enoch. So much<br /> spirit energy released in such violent fashion has had terrible<br /> consequences. Wraiths are assailed by the Sixth Maelstrom<br /> (the fury of which is unprecedented), and the Gauntlet takes<br /> on such a fiery new character that magic becomes inordinately<br /> difficult.</b><br /> <br /> <br /> THE AVATAR~STeRTTl<br /> <b>An unexpected effect of the tremendous outpouring of<br /> spirit power,</b> the Avatar-storm is born when humans and<br /> mages alike have their semi-corporeal spirit Avatars shredded<br /> by the power of the Maelstrom and spirit winds. Caught<br /> up in this sudden spirit gale, even the most potent mages are<br /> left with little time to escape. Many powerful mages flee<br /> beyond Earth, seeking shelter in Horizon Realms. A few try<br /> to immure themselves in their Sanctums.<br /> Others are not so fortunate. Surprised by the howling<br /> destruction, some mages suffer Gilgul. Others experience<br /> the devastation of having their Avatars flayed, shredded and<br /> turned into spirit-debris as the pieces are caught up and flung<br /> wildly about by the Maelstrom winds. Thus, a flying wall of<br /> razor-sharp Avatar shards creates an almost impenetrable<br /> barrier, reinforcing the Gauntlet and making magic quite<br /> difficult to enact in the modern age.<br /> <br /> <br /> Even more the Avatar Storm as started where Ravana has been hit, Eutanathos revised book, page 35, and in the node that was near the blast site has become the greatest shallowing in the world, and the only safe port from where you can go to the umbra,like the eye of a tornado.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 11:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:27:14-08:00","id":1037624,"title":"","content":"Enoch were destroyed by the wraiths at the request of Anubis.<br /> <br /> It seems that the Avatar Storm was caused by the sixth maelstrom, caused by the TWO nukes on the Underworld (they did go a bit hardcore on that)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:28:00-08:00","id":1037628,"title":"","content":"Besides, that was something they couldn't predict.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-24T20:34:06-08:00","id":1037630,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037618#post1037618\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Troile isn't the original 3rd was he? Capadoccius IS DEAD. He turned into a wraith (don't tell me you consider a wraith as &quot;living&quot;), but were eventually destroyed by the Giovani.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why not? Japhet is a wraith and it's not a problema for him being the Capuchin,freeing Unre and in general being one of the most powerful spirit of the shadowlands,and so on,so why being a wraith should be a problem for his master?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Saulot will end up being &quot;ejected&quot; from his infected borrowed body, tzimisce courtesy. RIP Saulot. </div> </div> </div>You should read again the extracts from Becket Jhyad Diary, Saulot is alive and well, and in two places at the same time.<br /> <br /> His dark side is inside the worm in Wien, and his light side is in Hundedora.<br /> <br /> <br /> From The Fall of the House<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tsang:</b> I am Tsang Kwong, once the One Who Knows. I watch and Master Zao-Lat sees all.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Beckett:</b> Saulot is dead.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tsang:</b> Zao-Lat lives. Your white worm is merely a chrysalis. He is reborn, through blood of Tzimisce and Tremere both. His Hun in the body of a mortal youth, his P'o within the worm. It is as he planned.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Beckett:</b> Tremere has been ousted from his own body \u2014</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tsang:</b> \u2014 and occupies that of his favored childe: Goratrix. The two have a sympathetic bond. As mortals they were lovers.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Beckett:</b> I need to know the plans of Saulot and Tremere.</span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b>Tsang: </b>They circle and align and await the appropriate time.</span></span> </div> </div> </div><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> As for Ventrue... One of his children had a lot of his blood (I forgot the name), and used it to make some 4th generations over the ages. It wasn't Ventrue embracing. </div> </div> </div>Source?<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> But... You know... Were is the projenitor of the TRUE BRUJAH? </div> </div> </div>Several millennia in the future from now, if I remember correctly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> EDIT: oh, I forgot another one... Malkav were killed by Haqim. His lunacy may still linger in his children, but that's it. </div> </div> </div>Source? Because Malkav is alive and well in several books: Crimson Fountain, Clan Novel Saga, Ghenna book, and so on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12142,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","user":"Undead rabbit","date":". 01-24-2017, 11:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12142-undead-rabbit","name":"Undead rabbit","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"888"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T06:47:43-08:00","id":1037807,"title":"","content":"It's worth to note that M20 introduces new metaplot that includes the cesation of the Avatar Storm among other things. This it's supposed to be optional, but it's also the current story of Mage, and all new books are supposedly going to assume this.<br /> <br /> Also, Karlgust it's not entirely wrong. The Avatar Storm was caused by a conjunction of factors, including the nuking of the Underworld, the True Death of the Ravnos Antediluvian, and the fall of Doissetep, I think this it's stated in the Revised Storytellers Handbook, but I don't have the books right now.<br /> <br /> Also, in late Revised (VE Convention Book), it's stated that the Storm would have ended if the Void Engineers weren't sustaining it with bizarre Wonders. This would contradict the new canon of M20, unless the VE decided to stop doing this for some reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:55 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T07:19:47-08:00","id":1037823,"title":"","content":"Also. What a twist! Now we're fighting Antediluvians. Mages have to be really powerful if one needs to pull off Storyteller Fiats to defeat them.<br /> <br /> I think that part, if not all, of Enginseer arguments to &quot;defeat other supernaturals&quot; are bassed on underestimating the resources that other splats have. Also, everyone underestimates the resources of the Garou Nation. They may not be as influential in th human world as the Technocracy or the Camarilla, but they compensate this having a very strong influence within the Spirit Worlds. And the Technocracy hasn't many allies there. But then, from a Mage perspective, this kind of bias isn't rare.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T07:43:08-08:00","id":1037835,"title":"","content":"I agree that Mages often underestimate the resources of the Garou Nation. It is relatively easy for Garou to learn how to summon spirits and, if pressed, the Garou Nations could potentially send millions of spirits against its enemies. Of course, they would not do so unless they suffered an existential threat because every spirit they send against their enemies is a spirit that is not doing its job.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T07:57:45-08:00","id":1037840,"title":"","content":"Probably my favorite aspect of V20 is the assertion that the nuking of Enoch is optional as well. That said, the entire discussion of Antedeluvian status is pretty pedantic. The point of 'the Union <i>could</i> wipe out all vampires or werewolves itself is entirely indeterminable. The amount of variables are staggering. I love a good white room scenario as much as the next guy. But you'll never possibly be able to account for everything to make any definitive statement. Especially when each faction's win condition would be entirely different.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T08:38:26-08:00","id":1037856,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>AyaTari</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It is relatively easy for Garou to learn how to summon spirits and, if pressed, the Garou Nations could potentially send millions of spirits against its enemies. Of course, they would not do so unless they suffered an existential threat because every spirit they send against their enemies is a spirit that is not doing its job.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sending a literal army of spirits may be beyond the ancient pacts that gives wolves their authority. I think there was a moment, in the Amazon, where werewolves started mass producing fetishes, and they had big problems with the spirits because of this. But I'm not certain. No Umbral lord should like their minions to get mass slaughtered, however.<br /> <br /> But Influence it's not just summoning and making the spirits work for you. Influence among spirits can works just like influence in the human world. It's easier to access the intel and a few resources of US Army than to send them to fight an all out war.<br /> <br /> Werewolves could convince Aetherial Spirits to discover where the Technocracy has it's satelites and space ships, then attack them in foce from the Aetherial Realm (which technomancers cannot affect nor access).<br /> They can joint these attacks to those of the spirit lords that have been angered by the Technocracy (Moon it's going to fall very quickly), obtianing, if not armies, at least a few platoons of spiritual troops. Incidentaly, some spirit lords have pacts with traditionalist mages, so the wolves may get some unlikely allies among the Traditions.<br /> They can hide in the places of the umbra that are hard to scan (there are places where Correspondence and Time either doesn't work, or work poorly), protected by alied spirit that know the place.<br /> They can make pacts with the Paradox spirits. Werewolves have largely ignored these spirits, thinking they're minnions of the Weaver that punish mages (who are largely inconsecuantial for the Apocalipse), but in a War with mages, these beings might turn the tide, as they have Charms and properties specialy designed to fuck with Mages (for instance, they can only be affected by Spirit 5, and even then at a great difficulty)<br /> Making deals with Treath Null may seem outlndish and dangerous (as they believe to be the Technocracy), but if intermediares of the Weaver are used, it may work (as weaver spirits have always been friendly to Autochtonia).<br /> <br /> All in all, the Technocracy can defend against these strategies, and may have the advantage in the mudball due to their influences with the most powerful earthly splat, the humans, which seems to be superior to the influence that werewolves have. But such a war would be catastrophical for both, and a great advantage for Treath Null and the Wirm. The first would see VE attention drift, the latter would have a golden chance of infiltrating the Technocracy even more, and to use it as a mean to finish the Garou interference in their affairs. The Traditions may gain some bases too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:49 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:06:07-08:00","id":1037866,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037856#post1037856\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sending a literal army of spirits may be beyond the ancient pacts that gives wolves their authority. I think there was a moment, in the Amazon, where werewolves started mass producing fetishes, and they had big problems with the spirits because of this. But I'm not certain. No Umbral lord should like their minions to get mass slaughtered, however.</div> </div> </div> </div>It isn't just a matter of authority, but you are generally right. Spirits don't typically do the fighting for werewolves- rather, the opposite holds true. There are some very warlike spirits, but Garou are meant to be the warriors of Gaia on either side of the Gauntlet. Saying there are 'millions' of spirits that would fight on the behalf of the Garou is not realistic.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:36:32-08:00","id":1037876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037866#post1037866\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It isn't just a matter of authority, but you are generally right. Spirits don't typically do the fighting for werewolves- rather, the opposite holds true. There are some very warlike spirits, but Garou are meant to be the warriors of Gaia on either side of the Gauntlet. Saying there are 'millions' of spirits that would fight on the behalf of the Garou is not realistic.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thankfully, spirits are generally willing to give you a Gift to do said fighting better than before. It's like the Dominus system from Aria/Dawn of Sorrow, but you don't even have to kill anything... directly, anyway. Earning that Glory Renown gets messy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T09:47:11-08:00","id":1037881,"title":"","content":"The same spirit summoning power that's just as volatile as true magic? And has a chance of unleashing an angry Celestine on the summoner? Good luck with that.<br /> <br /> Not to mention that the union pursued an open, upfront, and ridiculously successful war on the Umbra itself for decades. Carving out frankly massive swathes of formatted space. As of revised they retained a huge chunk of the solar system, and this is after the DA destroyed 90% of formatted space.<br /> <br /> If spirits could stop them, I think they would have already.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:37:28-08:00","id":1037904,"title":"","content":"Excellent points, <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar23_3.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"23\" data-vbnamecard=\"23\">Saur Ops Specialist</a>; also from a meta-game point of view, the game would be silly if werewolves primarily fought via summoning spirits and unleashing them like animistic pokemon.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037881#post1037881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same spirit summoning power that's just as volatile as true magic? And has a chance of unleashing an angry Celestine on the summoner?</div> </div> </div> </div>Except it isn't. I have been playing WtA for years and spirit summoning has never resulted in catastrophe. The chart just isn't that difficult to play around. Theurges are good at what they do, there are ways of mitigating difficulty, and if they still roll badly they can expend willpower to prevent botches. I think the Theurge in my group has had precisely one storm jaggling show up that was less than pleasant.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037881#post1037881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that the union pursued an open, upfront, and ridiculously successful war on the Umbra itself for decades. Carving out frankly massive swathes of formatted space. As of revised they retained a huge chunk of the solar system, and this is after the DA destroyed 90% of formatted space.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe in <i>your </i>game. Obviously if we are talking about WtA or crossovers in general, that may not be the case at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:42:04-08:00","id":1037907,"title":"","content":"Erego just as volatile as true magic.<br /> <br /> Though even if you don't botch anything below three successes nets you a hostile spirit.<br /> <br /> And that is simple brute fact of the mage setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T10:46:28-08:00","id":1037912,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037907#post1037907\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Erego just as volatile as true magic.<br /> <br /> Though even if you don't botch anything below three successes nets you a hostile spirit.<br /> <br /> And that is simple brute fact of the mage setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nothing is as volatile as Special K.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:25:19-08:00","id":1037929,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that the union pursued an open, upfront, and ridiculously successful war on the Umbra itself for decades. Carving out frankly massive swathes of formatted space. As of revised they retained a huge chunk of the solar system, and this is after the DA destroyed 90% of formatted space.</div> </div> </div> </div>What war?. They didn't just used the &quot;format space rote&quot; against the wishes of the spirits and the Traditions, if that's what you're referring to. They merely convinced the masses that space was empty, then sended normal people and proves there to &quot;carve&quot; it. That's the way space it's normaly formated. That's the way they're reformatting it right now. It's natural and subtle, and there's not much anyone could have done to stop it without controlling the Consensus (and that was the real war, not in or against the Umbra, but to change the minds of the masses).<br /> <br /> And it's utterly contradicted by werewolf Umbra (where &quot;conventional space&quot; it's infinite, and always was), so not realy an argument in crossover. It's a Pure Mage stuff<br /> <br /> They never faced a war against spirits until Treat Null (and they aren't precissely winning). They did won war against the Nephandi (and back then they were alied with the Traditions), and fought against the Traditions in another circumstance (against the Etherites mostly. The battle was raging when the Storm hit). They never faced a war against werewolves, nor in the Middle Umbra.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2017, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T11:49:52-08:00","id":1037944,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037881#post1037881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention that the union pursued an open, upfront, and ridiculously successful war on the Umbra itself for decades. Carving out frankly massive swathes of formatted space. As of revised they retained a huge chunk of the solar system, and this is after the DA destroyed 90% of formatted space.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037904#post1037904\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe in <i>your </i>game. Obviously if we are talking about WtA or crossovers in general, that may not be the case at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>The power and influence of the Weaver could suggest that Technocracy is very powerful from the WtA perspective as well.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:21:08-08:00","id":1037974,"title":"","content":"If you want to know, there's a section about the Technocracy in the Book of the Weaver. They are not given a lot of importance. They are unwittingly working for the goals of the Weaver, and thus they're treated as &quot;mostly ok&quot; by this being, but in the end, they're dinamic forces of change like all mages. Their part on the big plan has an expiration. Also, technology and science aren't controled nor given to the masses by them. These are gifts given by the spirits to all humans (well, it's a Werewolf book, what else could you expect?).<br /> <br /> Also, there's a very big chasm between being &quot;very powerful&quot;, and being a force that can't be opposed by anything that hasn't Arete.<br /> would say that, in crossover, the Technocracy should be very powerful. Any other conteplation would be damaging to the place they have in Mage. Making them overwhelmingly important by buying all that they say about themselves, seems too much.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-25-2017, 03:24 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:37:38-08:00","id":1037984,"title":"","content":"*Prompt for discussion of game-related philosophy or play style*<br /> *crickets*<br /> <br /> *My favorite thing can beat up your favorite thing*<br /> *Every comment*","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1503-faradn","name":"Faradn","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1503_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"792"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:38:01-08:00","id":1037986,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037974#post1037974\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you want to know, there's a section about the Technocracy in the Book of the Weaver. They are not given a lot of importance. They are unwittingly working for the goals of the Weaver, and thus they're treated as &amp;quot;mostly ok&amp;quot; by this being, but in the end, they're dinamic forces of change like all mages. Their part on the big plan has an expiration. Also, technology and science aren't controled nor given to the masses by them. These are gifts given by the spirits to all humans (well, it's a Werewolf book, what else could you expect?).<br /> <br /> Also, there's a very big chasm between being &amp;quot;very powerful&amp;quot;, and being a force that can't be opposed by anything that hasn't Arete.<br /> would say that, in crossover, the Technocracy should be very powerful. Any other conteplation would be damaging to the place they have in Mage. Making them overwhelmingly important by buying all that they say about themselves, seems too much.</div> </div> </div> </div>Can't be opposed by Garou =/= can't be opposed by anything without Arete.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:49:02-08:00","id":1037990,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037984#post1037984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Prompt for discussion of game-related philosophy or play style*<br /> *crickets*<br /> <br /> *My favorite thing can beat up your favorite thing*<br /> *Every comment*</div> </div> </div> </div>Gotta love the forums. The Splat vs Splat discussions always seem go that route, and it is usually treated incredibly one sided. Either &quot;my side&quot; wins overwhelmingly or loses overwhelmingly. Either way, this doesn't seem to be supported in setting since everyone still has their place in the world.<br /> <br /> In case I missed it, what was the last &quot;Prompt for discussion of game-related philosophy or play style&quot;? I'm all for redirecting the topic of discussion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T12:51:49-08:00","id":1037993,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aleph</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037823#post1037823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also. What a twist! Now we're fighting Antediluvians. Mages have to be really powerful if one needs to pull off Storyteller Fiats to defeat them.<br /> <br /> I think that part, if not all, of Enginseer arguments to &amp;quot;defeat other supernaturals&amp;quot; are bassed on underestimating the resources that other splats have. Also, everyone underestimates the resources of the Garou Nation. They may not be as influential in th human world as the Technocracy or the Camarilla, but they compensate this having a very strong influence within the Spirit Worlds. And the Technocracy hasn't many allies there. But then, from a Mage perspective, this kind of bias isn't rare.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not our fault. Like I said in another topic, it doesn't make much sense that the Union could have more than half a dozen Qui La Machine, which while being something damn insane (those things DO have the firepower to fight Cthulhu-like Lovecraftian aliens of the Deep Umbra), should also be insanely hard to build (I would consider that each one of those should have the efforts of almost all the Masters and a good percentage - maybe at least 25% - of the remaining enlightened personel of the Union, not to mention a lot of mundane effort - resources and manpower - to build, and ludicruous amounts of both Tass and quintessence - maybe all of the energy of Mecha 1 and 2 - and all that for at least a few years... The Etherites perhaps could have ONE single Ethership, and they would have to pull all their resources for a full decade for that)<br /> <br /> But in the plot, both the Union and the Etherites have hundreds to thousands of those... It's absolutely unreal. But it's part of the scenario that the writters created.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:05:18-08:00","id":1037998,"title":"","content":"But in the setting, lets not forget that it is the VE that keep the things-men-were-not-meant-to-know away from Earth, not the paladins of Gaia, who are too busy with the demons inside","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:15:41-08:00","id":1038005,"title":"","content":"And in this unrealistic scenario, that Union in fact DID waged a full scale war against... Well, pretty much everything they didn't liked in the Umbra.<br /> <br /> Have they done it alone? Well, probably some hundreds of thousands of pattern spiders follow their starships on each battle... Maybe their cruisers are just the tip of the spear for the Weaver forces than make the real cleaning after they pass, without revealing that to his ignorant paws... Whatever you wanna.<br /> <br /> But that's how it has been putted in the scenario, like it or not, no matter how unrealistic that may be","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T13:38:58-08:00","id":1038019,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Faradn</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1037984#post1037984\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Prompt for discussion of game-related philosophy or play style*<br /> *crickets*<br /> <br /> *My favorite thing can beat up your favorite thing*<br /> *Every comment*</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to hug you for that comment, Faradn. It's perfect.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T14:58:16-08:00","id":1038053,"title":"","content":"Wow, this thread escalated quickly into the usual pissing contest between splats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Anyway, thanks for the ideas about the gift disruptor device. I was thinking along the same lines and quite possibly I'll will use it in a future chronicle somehow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T15:31:40-08:00","id":1038073,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>PM\u00e1rk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038053#post1038053\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow, this thread escalated quickly into the usual pissing contest between splats. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>Doesn't count for much, but it took quite a few pages for it to devolve.<br /> <br /> On the Gift counter thing, by the books Spirit alone is supposed to be able to do it. I'd imagine the VEs already have devices that would work. Countering Gifts would work on the same principles as countering Spirit Charms.<br /> More complicated methods will exist for countering specific Gifts by coming up with tailored counter effects.<br /> <br /> Someone earlier did bring up the problem with Mage crossover being that Mage assumes rolls need to be made for effects, and so some Gifts can't be countered using the Mage system. It really just depends on how you go about it. Either way, the books don't cover it well when it comes to rolls and automatic Gifts.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T16:20:01-08:00","id":1038099,"title":"","content":"Well, I think that the majority of Gifts that do not allow a roll effectively give their recepients another innate ability, so those Gifts would be as immune to countermagic as innate abilities like lethal or aggravated soak or spending Rage for additional actions or spending blood to boost Attributes. The same argument could be made concerning the Physical Disciplines of the Kindred and Risen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:08:16-08:00","id":1038112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038073#post1038073\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't count for much, but it took quite a few pages for it to devolve.<br /> <br /> On the Gift counter thing, by the books Spirit alone is supposed to be able to do it. I'd imagine the VEs already have devices that would work. Countering Gifts would work on the same principles as countering Spirit Charms.<br /> More complicated methods will exist for countering specific Gifts by coming up with tailored counter effects.<br /> <br /> Someone earlier did bring up the problem with Mage crossover being that Mage assumes rolls need to be made for effects, and so some Gifts can't be countered using the Mage system. It really just depends on how you go about it. Either way, the books don't cover it well when it comes to rolls and automatic Gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>If the mage has one dot of prime, any successes would be more successes than the Garou got, which means they win, and can even turn the effect back on the Garou if they feel like it.<br /> <br /> And honestly, the original post's question was a somewhat loaded one in that it presumed mages walk around helpless 90% of the time.<br /> <br /> Prey presumes a certain action set. Running, Hiding, avoid and evade and only fighting when backed into a corner.<br /> <br /> Mages are not this. Mages are absolutely <i>brutal </i>ambush predators.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:20:50-08:00","id":1038119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038112#post1038112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the mage has one dot of prime, any successes would be more successes than the Garou got, which means they win, and can even turn the effect back on the Garou if they feel like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, at that point, you'd probably need to establish what kind of successes a mage needs to produce a similar effect. Anything else is as bad a crossover rule as a vampire with Dominate 6 automatically bypassing all defenses because the Mind Sphere doesn't go up to 6.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:24:56-08:00","id":1038121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038112#post1038112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If the mage has one dot of prime, any successes would be more successes than the Garou got, which means they win, and can even turn the effect back on the Garou if they feel like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>A lot of your other assertions were extremely biased towards will-workers and this seems no different. I see nothing in Prime 1 that allows for what you are describing. Prime 1 (like most single-dot spheres) is quite limited. If you are allowing a mage to disrupt or control werewolf gifts with Prime 1 you are likely doing something wrong.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T17:26:49-08:00","id":1038122,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038119#post1038119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No, at that point, you'd probably need to establish what kind of successes a mage needs to produce a similar effect. Anything else is as bad a crossover rule as a vampire with Dominate 6 automatically bypassing all defenses because the Mind Sphere doesn't go up to 6.</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, their crossover rules basically say &quot;Pick an appropriate sphere and roleplay it.&quot;<br /> <br /> In any case, the point wasn't so much that they can turn the effect back on the garou because most Garou powers are buffs, so much as it allows them to counter things that don't have rolls.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:02:03-08:00","id":1038136,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Laughing Stranger</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038121#post1038121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A lot of your other assertions were extremely biased towards will-workers and this seems no different. I see nothing in Prime 1 that allows for what you are describing. Prime 1 (like most single-dot spheres) is quite limited. If you are allowing a mage to disrupt or control werewolf gifts with Prime 1 you are likely doing something wrong.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm sorry, I missed this entirely.<br /> <br /> It's in the rules for countermagic. Prime one allows for prime-senses, the effects of which are.... A.) You can countermagic things that are not targeting you. and B.) if you get more successes than the opponent you can 'flip' the spell turning it back on them. With every success beyond those needed to cancel theres counting as a success towards the effect.<br /> <br /> So say someone throws a fireball at you. They roll two successes, you roll three. You negate their fireball and throw a 3 damage fireball back at them. (1 success + forces bonus damage.)<br /> <br /> The point is not that you can 'flip' the spell, though that's what the wording is there for. But that it confirms that countermagic can also counter abilities if you get more successes than the opponent rather than just removing successes.<br /> <br /> Seeing as the rules for cross-splat countering are essentially stillborn and they can only do one magical action per turn, (Barring talismans.) and countermagic takes that up.....<br /> <br /> Though mages with the Kinfolk merit, IIRC can make always coincidental spells if they use sphere magic to recreate Garou gifts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:03:19-08:00","id":1038138,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038112#post1038112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If the mage has one dot of prime, any successes would be more successes than the Garou got, which means they win, and can even turn the effect back on the Garou if they feel like it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just no. That isn't how things work. And Prime doesn't really cover Spirit powers, so it isn't the catch-all that the Spirit Sphere is (as written). I could just as much argue that not having to roll equals infinite successes, which would be just as incorrect.<br /> <br /> Prime 1 is not going to help (at all) for countering Spirit of the Fray, for example. You would either need Spirit (kind of useless here since there is no activation roll to counter, nor any time to do so) or Time, which would be a much better fit. But at that point, you would actually have to inflict an opposing Effect to counter the Gift. And if you can do that, you are better off slowing the Gaoru down enough to cancel actions, and not just their initiative roll.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038136#post1038136\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though mages with the Kinfolk merit, IIRC can make always coincidental spells if they use sphere magic to recreate Garou gifts.</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like another terrible crossover rule. A kinfolk Mage shouldn't be able to coincidentally summon a bygone beast for example, just because a Gift can do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:05 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:06:21-08:00","id":1038140,"title":"","content":"Hey, I just got here. What did I miss?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:07:49-08:00","id":1038141,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saikou</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038140#post1038140\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, I just got here. What did I miss?</div> </div> </div> </div>We moved slightly away (for the moment) from arguing Splat vs Splat worldwide wars.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> so...a positive step, I think.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:15:23-08:00","id":1038144,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038138#post1038138\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Just no. That isn't how things work. And Prime doesn't really cover Spirit powers, so it isn't the catch-all that the Spirit Sphere is (as written). I could just as much argue that not having to roll equals infinite successes, which would be just as incorrect.<br /> <br /> Prime 1 is not going to help (at all) for countering Spirit of the Fray, for example. You would either need Spirit (kind of useless here since there is no activation roll to counter, nor any time to do so) or Time, which would be a much better fit. But at that point, you would actually have to inflict an opposing Effect to counter the Gift. And if you can do that, you are better off slowing the Gaoru down enough to cancel actions, and not just their initiative roll.<br /> <br /> That sounds like another terrible crossover rule. A kinfolk Mage shouldn't be able to coincidentally summon a bygone beast for example, just because a Gift can do it.</div> </div> </div> </div>It has to EXACTLY replicate the gift. It can't be slightly based off the gift. IIRC.<br /> <br /> &quot;If your character is a<br /> sorcerer, you might be able to learn a few spirit Gifts, and an Awakened<br /> mage can use these inherent magical powers as well without<br /> threat of Paradox.&quot; ~ Shapechanger Kin, 4-pt Merit.<br /> <br /> Also, perhaps I was unclear. You'd need the ability to <i>normally </i>countermagic something under that header first. Meaning a dot in that sphere. Countermagic is very low hanging fruit, but also difficult to pull off and very suboptimal.<br /> <br /> The one dot of prime simply upgrades you from merely removing successes (Which is irrelevant to some of the Garou's gifts.) to stopping anything that gets less successes than you.<br /> <br /> Though honestly most of the 'splat hook' merits are kind of broken. Because they allow for double dipping in two splats power-sets. Ghoul Mages are insane. Especially since you can grab unbondable and then basically just curbstomp random vampires for their vitae and become some sort of weird vampire vampire.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11744,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","user":"Enginseer-42","date":". 01-25-2017, 09:19 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:19:49-08:00","id":1038145,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038141#post1038141\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We moved slightly away (for the moment) from arguing Splat vs Splat worldwide wars.<img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> so...a positive step, I think.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think now we're on terrible crossover rules, and how kin mages using Garou Gift effects isn't really passable by either game's standards. I know that on the Werewolf side, humans using Gifts is a no-no, and I think on the Mage side there's some argument to be made about not intersecting with linear effects.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:24:11-08:00","id":1038149,"title":"","content":"Right... I'll just be leaving then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/959615-chronicle-report-keepers-of-the-wyck\" target=\"_blank\">Keepers of the Wyck: A Chronicle I'm running</a> FINALE: Chapter 39: Green Fairy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12193-saikou","name":"Saikou","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12193_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1406"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:24:17-08:00","id":1038150,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's kind of weird since it specifies you don't have Gnosis, the connection to the spirit world, but you can still use spirit tricks....","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:33:02-08:00","id":1038155,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038144#post1038144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> It has to EXACTLY replicate the gift. It can't be slightly based off the gift. IIRC.<br /> <br /> &quot;If your character is a<br /> sorcerer, you might be able to learn a few spirit Gifts, and an Awakened<br /> mage can use these inherent magical powers as well without<br /> threat of Paradox.&quot; ~ Shapechanger Kin, 4-pt Merit.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay. So this doesn't mean what you are taking it to mean, at least by my reading. What this says is that (per normal Kinfolk rules), the Kin Mage can learn a Gift or 2 and those innate powers do not come with Paradox, because they aren't Magick.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038144#post1038144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Also, perhaps I was unclear. You'd need the ability to <i>normally </i>countermagic something under that header first. Meaning a dot in that sphere. Countermagic is very low hanging fruit, but also difficult to pull off and very suboptimal.<br /> <br /> The one dot of prime simply upgrades you from merely removing successes (Which is irrelevant to some of the Garou's gifts.) to stopping anything that gets less successes than you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is there a difference? If you use countermagic and get more successes than your opponent, doesn't that stop their power from working (since that should leave them with zero successes)? This isn't meant to be me being difficult. Your explanation (without Prime) is how I understood countermagic to work in general.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038144#post1038144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though honestly most of the 'splat hook' merits are kind of broken. Because they allow for double dipping in two splats power-sets. Ghoul Mages are insane. Especially since you can grab unbondable and then basically just curbstomp random vampires for their vitae and become some sort of weird vampire vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div> But at that point, your ST is letting you make a min-maxed character (with the unbondable Merit), so that is as much on them as on you. I agree said Merits overcomplicate things, but in general the game assumes everyone is in it for the role playing factor. Besides, that Mage's existence sounds like it could be both terrible (constantly needing to hunt Vampires, which is more than a bit dangerous) and interesting (from a story perspective).<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:34:53-08:00","id":1038156,"title":"","content":"I think the point of the Kinfolk Mages is that they can use Spheres to create coincidental effects that would normally be vulgar because they mimic Fera Gifts if they have the appropriate Shamanic Paradigm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:40:17-08:00","id":1038158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038156#post1038156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think the point of the Kinfolk Mages is that they can use Spheres to create coincidental effects that would normally be vulgar because they mimic Fera Gifts if they have the appropriate Shamanic Paradigm.</div> </div> </div> </div>At least what was quoted doesn't say anything of the sort. Is there some other place that supports that interpretation more? All I see from the quote is that kinfolk Mages can learn a few Gifts (same as any Kinfolk has the potential to) that don't get them paradox when used.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:45:51-08:00","id":1038163,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> &quot;If your character is a sorcerer, you might be able to learn a few spirit GIFTS, and an Awakened<br /> mage can use THESE inherent magical powers as well without threat of Paradox.&quot; </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine. This is clearly talking about using gifts, and I am not sure how the sentence structure could be construed otherwise. The gifts are the 'inherent magical powers' referenced, not a backhanded way of saying that you could make your sphere rotes look like Fera gifts so as to avoid paradox.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3695-the-laughing-stranger","name":"The Laughing Stranger","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3695_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1010"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T18:53:12-08:00","id":1038169,"title":"","content":"Unsung Heroes (p. 68) clearly states the capabilities of Kinfolk Mages in relation to replicating the effects of Gifts under Mirrors of the Soul.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:13:04-08:00","id":1038184,"title":"","content":"That section also bars anyone with Gnosis or Gifts from awakening, which would seem to run contrary to what the Merit states, which is that said Kinfolk mage can learn Gifts.<br /> <br /> Both sets of rules are written from the other games perspective and so it isn't surprising that they contradict each other. Each game has a different goal for incorporating the crossover.<br /> <br /> Also, as with any of the older books: take what's in them with a grain of salt. There is probably a reason that wasn't reprinted in the new Kinfolk book.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-25-2017, 10:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:22:53-08:00","id":1038190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038155#post1038155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference? If you use countermagic and get more successes than your opponent, doesn't that stop their power from working (since that should leave them with zero successes)? This isn't meant to be me being difficult. Your explanation (without Prime) is how I understood countermagic to work in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, normally. But Garou have powers that work without requiring rolls. Thus having no successes to negate. So negating successes, the normal means of victory, doesn't work. Because normally if you negate them down to zero successes, then the effect doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> But in this case, there's no roll being made, so no successes to negate, so their lack of successes being negated doesn't actually, mechanically speaking, do anything to stop the effect.<br /> <br /> Then you add prime 1, and it's clause that if you get MORE successes than they do. This also counts as a victory and allows you to turn the spell back on them. The turning is essentially besides the point.<br /> <br /> Basically it's a way to make the rules SORTA work, if not very well. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also it's a reading that supports my mage supremacy, MWAHAHAHAHA... I mean... Uhhh... &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">To be entirely fair, such a.... literal reading of the rules seems to be counter to white wolfs general style of game development. But eh.</span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:31:51-08:00","id":1038195,"title":"","content":"You have made a logical fallacy though. No successes is not the same as zero successes, so Prime 1 would have no effect because no successes might as well be infinite successes. It would be like saying that 'Apple' is less than '1', when 'Apple' has nothing to do with '1'.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","user":"Aya Tari","date":". 01-25-2017, 10:34 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:33:44-08:00","id":1038197,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038099#post1038099\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, I think that the majority of Gifts that do not allow a roll effectively give their recepients another innate ability, so those Gifts would be as immune to countermagic as innate abilities like lethal or aggravated soak or spending Rage for additional actions or spending blood to boost Attributes. The same argument could be made concerning the Physical Disciplines of the Kindred and Risen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, Primium can &quot;cancel&quot; those said &quot;innate abilities&quot;, so I would say that countermagic would too.<br /> <br /> Primium: besides giving innate countermagic dices, weapons made of Primium can also remove the innate defenses of supernaturals. Every success on the counter effect of Primium, removes one dice of the resistance against aggravated damage from the supernatural being, like the vampiric Fortitude or the werewolves Vigor resistance. <br /> <br /> Besides of that, Primium always does aggr damage.<br /> <br /> That's the effect of Primium as said on the SoE revised.<br /> <br /> So, that implies that countermagik can be used against innate abilities of the critters of the WoD, even against natural resistance versus aggravated","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:35:25-08:00","id":1038200,"title":"","content":"No, they mean the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> The Definition of Zero is &quot;No amount or Number.&quot; The definition of None is &quot;No amount, Not any, not at all.&quot;<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:48:01-08:00","id":1038208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038155#post1038155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay. So this doesn't mean what you are taking it to mean, at least by my reading. What this says is that (per normal Kinfolk rules), the Kin Mage can learn a Gift or 2 and those innate powers do not come with Paradox, because they aren't Magick.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, the merit allows the Mage exactly that, to learn some level 1 gifts, and he can use them without paradox because they aren't magik. That's EXACTLY what the merit does.<br /> <br /> What I think that Engiseer-42 was saying, is that you could replicate Garou gifts using spheres to make them coincidental (that could be troublesome, since for some gifts you would need Life 4 to mimic the form of Crinos and Mind 2 to mimic the Delirium in order to use it, for example). That however, could be debatable, but at least in a small town of kinfolk... Yeah, I agree, it would be coincidental.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038155#post1038155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is there a difference? If you use countermagic and get more successes than your opponent, doesn't that stop their power from working (since that should leave them with zero successes)? This isn't meant to be me being difficult. Your explanation (without Prime) is how I understood countermagic to work in general.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your oponent have 1 success and you have 5 successes on the counter, you can turn 4 success against him, if aplicable<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>idpersona</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038155#post1038155\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But at that point, your ST is letting you make a min-maxed character (with the unbondable Merit), so that is as much on them as on you. I agree said Merits overcomplicate things, but in general the game assumes everyone is in it for the role playing factor. Besides, that Mage's existence sounds like it could be both terrible (constantly needing to hunt Vampires, which is more than a bit dangerous) and interesting (from a story perspective).</div> </div> </div> </div>Make it a Ghoul, Kinfolk AND with Fae Blood.<br /> <br /> You'll be able to learn a few level 1 Gifts, up to level 3 Cantrips if memory serves, up to level 5 disciplines... <br /> <br /> Oh yes, you'll also have Spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the most ridiculous character concept (the half Garou half Fae that steals vampiric blood to be a bettwr Mage... WTF...)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:53:41-08:00","id":1038211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038200#post1038200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, they mean the exact same thing.<br /> <br /> The Definition of Zero is &quot;No amount or Number.&quot; The definition of None is &quot;No amount, Not any, not at all.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>No. None is a subjective concept (the Mage has none of the qualities of a Nephandi) while zero is an objective concept (the Mage has zero points of Quintessence).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T19:58:38-08:00","id":1038215,"title":"","content":"Not really. None and Zero mean the exact same thing. A lack of a thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:10:33-08:00","id":1038226,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038190#post1038190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Yes, normally. But Garou have powers that work without requiring rolls. Thus having no successes to negate. So negating successes, the normal means of victory, doesn't work. Because normally if you negate them down to zero successes, then the effect doesn't happen.<br /> <br /> But in this case, there's no roll being made, so no successes to negate, so their lack of successes being negated doesn't actually, mechanically speaking, do anything to stop the effect.<br /> <br /> Then you add prime 1, and it's clause that if you get MORE successes than they do. This also counts as a victory and allows you to turn the spell back on them. The turning is essentially besides the point.<br /> <br /> Basically it's a way to make the rules SORTA work, if not very well. <span style=\"font-size:8px\">Also it's a reading that supports my mage supremacy, MWAHAHAHAHA... I mean... Uhhh... &lt;.&lt;<br /> <br /> <span style=\"font-size:12px\">To be entirely fair, such a.... literal reading of the rules seems to be counter to white wolfs general style of game development. But eh.</span></span></div> </div> </div> </div>At least the conversation has steered towards the amusing. It is worth noting though, that all of the Gifts I can think of that don't have rolls aren't powers you use on someone else. They either affect the Garou personally, or directly effect how the Garou interacts with their environment. So turning the Gift back on the user wouldn't seem to <i>be able to</i> have an effect.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038197#post1038197\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Well, Primium can &quot;cancel&quot; those said &quot;innate abilities&quot;, so I would say that countermagic would too.<br /> <br /> Primium: besides giving innate countermagic dices, weapons made of Primium can also remove the innate defenses of supernaturals. Every success on the counter effect of Primium, removes one dice of the resistance against aggravated damage from the supernatural being, like the vampiric Fortitude or the werewolves Vigor resistance.<br /> <br /> Besides of that, Primium always does aggr damage.<br /> <br /> That's the effect of Primium as said on the SoE revised.<br /> <br /> So, that implies that countermagik can be used against innate abilities of the critters of the WoD, even against natural resistance versus aggravated</div> </div> </div> </div>I have never seen such wording. I would guess this is a translation thing, but Garou don't have &quot;Vigor resistance&quot;. Even with that interpretation, Primium isn't cancelling innate abilities so much as being extra deadly. The presence of Primium (to my knowledge) has zero effect on a Vampire's ability to spend blood to heal (besides being Agg damage) or a Garou's ability to shapeshift.<br /> <br /> Edit: found it in my book. The wording is different in the English version. Following the rules for Priumium being rolled as countermagic: &quot;If the Primium has been made into a weapon, this effect is rolled to weaken the strength of any supernatural defense, allowing Primium blades blades and bullets to punch through defensive Forces Effects and weaken enhanced soak capabilities.&quot;<br /> <br /> I suppose you can read &quot;enhanced soak capabilities&quot; as Fortitude and Garou's innate soak, but I think that would be going a bit far. To me, it seems to read as the Primium counters magical (as in active spell) enhancements, which would make sense since it's countermagic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":805,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","user":"idpersona","date":". 01-25-2017, 11:15 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-25T20:26:27-08:00","id":1038242,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038208#post1038208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> No, the merit allows the Mage exactly that, to learn some level 1 gifts, and he can use them without paradox because they aren't magik. That's EXACTLY what the merit does.<br /> <br /> What I think that Engiseer-42 was saying, is that you could replicate Garou gifts using spheres to make them coincidental (that could be troublesome, since for some gifts you would need Life 4 to mimic the form of Crinos and Mind 2 to mimic the Delirium in order to use it, for example). That however, could be debatable, but at least in a small town of kinfolk... Yeah, I agree, it would be coincidental.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree with the first part of the statement (that a Kin Mage can learn and use some Kinfolk or Rank 1 Paradox free Gifts) completely, though it is certainly more complicated than that.<br /> <br /> How it was stated initially though (or at least how I read it) was that being a Kin Mage let you replicate any Gift and have it be coincidental. That's what I was confused by. And having seen the wording, I disagree with that reading of it.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038208#post1038208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> If your oponent have 1 success and you have 5 successes on the counter, you can turn 4 success against him, if aplicable</div> </div> </div> </div>I was asking about counterspelling without using Prime. The Prime enhanced version of counterspelling seems to be required to &quot;turn&quot; spells or effects. In any case, I think statement of mine that you specifically were replying to here has been cleared up. It's just another case of the rules breaking down during crossover (when someone's power isn't rolled). I think I'm on the same page as <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> on this point now. Though he/she is having a side disagreement with <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar11683_2.jpeg');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11683\" data-vbnamecard=\"11683\">Aya Tari</a> on the meaning of nothing and/or zero.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038208#post1038208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Make it a Ghoul, Kinfolk AND with Fae Blood.<br /> <br /> You'll be able to learn a few level 1 Gifts, up to level 3 Cantrips if memory serves, up to level 5 disciplines...<br /> <br /> Oh yes, you'll also have Spheres.<br /> <br /> <br /> And the most ridiculous character concept (the half Garou half Fae that steals vampiric blood to be a bettwr Mage... WTF...)</div> </div> </div> </div>The Discipline level max is wholly dependent on the strength (Gen) blood you can get your hands on. In any case, this wild character idea is sounding entirely too close to what Haight became. And no good can come of that. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T05:34:14-08:00","id":1038359,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038144#post1038144\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ghoul Mages are insane. Especially since you can grab unbondable and then basically just curbstomp random vampires for their vitae and become some sort of weird vampire vampire.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is the benefit? The rules for Vampire (as far as I recall) make it so you stop being able to gain <i>more</i> access to mage stuff. And learning disciplines aren't necessarily better than what you could learn with magic for the high cost. So you just become an ungrowing immortal who also needs the blood of dangerous vampires. Though arguably the best route, if you really wanted to, would be to stake a Vampire and make him into a blood filter. There are ghouls out there who do this (the whole unbondable+feeding off vampires). But keeping one in storage just seems better business than needing to hunt them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038169#post1038169\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Unsung Heroes (p. 68) clearly states the capabilities of Kinfolk Mages in relation to replicating the effects of Gifts under Mirrors of the Soul.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is says is that SPECIFICALLY AROUND WEREWOLVES you can make certain spells coincidental if it looks like a gift effect. This isn't a comment on the other merit. Just that if we're talking about the rules in Unsung Heroes, only specifically trying to mimic gifts with spheres around them can make possibly make it fine. And that's if you act as though you are using a gift too.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12552-monalfie","name":"Monalfie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12552_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1261"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T06:00:28-08:00","id":1038369,"title":"","content":"On the same page it says that the connection to Gaia, either through Gifts or Gnosis, precludes Awakenening. It is just like with Changeling Kinfolk, you cannot overlap (and the level one Gifts you would have access to are really not worth the XP for a Mage).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:54:52-08:00","id":1038508,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038359#post1038359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is the benefit? The rules for Vampire (as far as I recall) make it so you stop being able to gain <i>more</i> access to mage stuff. And learning disciplines aren't necessarily better than what you could learn with magic for the high cost. So you just become an ungrowing immortal who also needs the blood of dangerous vampires. Though arguably the best route, if you really wanted to, would be to stake a Vampire and make him into a blood filter. There are ghouls out there who do this (the whole unbondable+feeding off vampires). But keeping one in storage just seems better business than needing to hunt them.</div> </div> </div> </div>Mages can't gain more Arete while as ghouls, and in fact can lose it, slowly but surely, until suffering gilgul and losing their magik. Besides, the Avatar can get addicted to the cursed blood, and keep that adiction on new reencarnations.<br /> <br /> So... It's really a TERRIBLE idea<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monalfie</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038359#post1038359\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What is says is that SPECIFICALLY AROUND WEREWOLVES you can make certain spells coincidental if it looks like a gift effect. This isn't a comment on the other merit. Just that if we're talking about the rules in Unsung Heroes, only specifically trying to mimic gifts with spheres around them can make possibly make it fine. And that's if you act as though you are using a gift too.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Easier to just having a Sanctum thou, than trying to befriend the furry ones so that they let you mimic them.<br /> <br /> By that idea, you could also mimic Tremere (or Tzimisce Koldun, or Giovani) inside their chapels to avoid paradox too...<br /> <br /> But all that is just silly","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T11:57:03-08:00","id":1038509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038369#post1038369\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the same page it says that the connection to Gaia, either through Gifts or Gnosis, precludes Awakenening. It is just like with Changeling Kinfolk, you cannot overlap (and the level one Gifts you would have access to are really not worth the XP for a Mage).</div> </div> </div> </div>Yep, just a little bit of bad coherence between all the published materials, a thing far too common on WoD","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T12:31:08-08:00","id":1038519,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038508#post1038508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Mages can't gain more Arete while as ghouls, and in fact can lose it, slowly but surely, until suffering gilgul and losing their magik. Besides, the Avatar can get addicted to the cursed blood, and keep that adiction on new reencarnations.<br /> <br /> So... It's really a TERRIBLE idea</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if you have Blood Treachery or not.<br /> <br /> Blood Treachery did a lot to make Ghoul Mages a terrible idea.<br /> <br /> Some new group that just branched over into mage from their vampire game and only has the core book? Given blood treachery is a tad obscure. To the point I'm not even sure the name I'm using is right...<br /> <br /> The default Merit merely says that completing seekings is harder. Not impossible, and no mention of Arete loss is there. The primary downsides are Resonance based. Your resonance will change to static and entropic to match the vampires you're feeding off of. Which is at worst a conditional modifier to your spells.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-26T21:30:28-08:00","id":1038755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038519#post1038519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> The default Merit merely says that completing seekings is harder. Not impossible, and no mention of Arete loss is there. The primary downsides are Resonance based. Your resonance will change to static and entropic to match the vampires you're feeding off of. Which is at worst a conditional modifier to your spells.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, those downsides, and the fact that you're a blood-junkie. If Storytellers make use of that aspect of being a Ghoul, effects on their Arete and/or Avatar shouldn't be necessary. Doubly so, if the Mage risks the blood bond.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:25:51-08:00","id":1040678,"title":"","content":"I ran a game for a Euthanatos who ran across a Black Spiral Dancer, his solution was to use Matter 3, to change the hair around the Dancer's head into Nitroglycerine. Mages CONTROL reality, they do so at their own peril as Reality doesn't like it when they do, but if they are willing to face the consequences, they can accomplish anything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12903-gangrel_reaper","name":"Gangrel_Reaper","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12903_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T08:31:12-08:00","id":1040682,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1038755#post1038755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, those downsides, and the fact that you're a blood-junkie. If Storytellers make use of that aspect of being a Ghoul, effects on their Arete and/or Avatar shouldn't be necessary. Doubly so, if the Mage risks the blood bond.</div> </div> </div> </div>Involvement with Cainites alone is problematic. Unless you take Vitae from a Caitiff, a Clan can become aware of you. There is also the chance of info about you (traded in to cover some Boons, perhaps) ending up in the hands of the Nosferatu; or the Malkavian Madness Network might notice you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3254-muad-dib","name":"Muad'Dib","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3254_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2059"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T11:16:14-08:00","id":1040777,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Muad'Dib</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Involvement with Cainites alone is problematic. Unless you take Vitae from a Caitiff, a Clan can become aware of you. There is also the chance of info about you (traded in to cover some Boons, perhaps) ending up in the hands of the Nosferatu; or the Malkavian Madness Network might notice you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quite true. Same could be said for involvement with Mages. Mages are very rare, each one it's hard to replace. They join in Chantries and Constructs for protection and power in numbers. If a vampire sucks a random mage in the street, unless the Mage it's a lonely Orphan, there will be an investigation (mages are very good at this), and, perhaps, a very angry Master. And you don't want that over your shoulder if you're the typical vampire, I would say.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Gangrel_Reaper</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I ran a game for a Euthanatos who ran across a Black Spiral Dancer, his solution was to use Matter 3, to change the hair around the Dancer's head into Nitroglycerine. Mages CONTROL reality, they do so at their own peril as Reality doesn't like it when they do, but if they are willing to face the consequences, they can accomplish anything.</div> </div> </div> </div>The problem with these examples it's that they're dependant on certain interpretations of the rules. We don't know exactly how this happened, in terms of Dice/Rules, so it doesn't count as a general example. The same approach would/could have failed with a different ruling (like, say, enabling counterspelling, since it was a transmutation. Or saying that you need also Life 3 + Spirit 3 because werewolves are half spirit)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1683,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","user":"Aleph","date":". 01-30-2017, 02:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1683-aleph","name":"Aleph","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3056"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T15:02:04-08:00","id":1040925,"title":"","content":"Hair is also under Life while it is still attached to a character, so you would need a minimum of Life 3/Matter 3 for that sort of thing. And 100 grams of nitro would hardly do anything to a BSD.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T16:13:19-08:00","id":1040966,"title":"","content":"Not sure where you got the 100 grams thing... But yeah. 100 grams isn't even enough for the standard explosive rules to apply. You need at least a pound of explosives. Heck just doing the math, dividing the damage to be proportional, it doesn't even come out to one die of damage.<br /> <br /> Also, personally I'd rule explosives to constitute a complex material. And as such would need matter 4. Explosives are composed of complicated intermixed chemicals, not one solid mass of material.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:19:49-08:00","id":1040985,"title":"","content":"Good point on the complex materials. I rechecked Revised, and altering the pattern of a complex life form is Life 4, so you would need Life 4/Matter 4/Spirit 3 to transform Garou hair to nitro (it would also be vulgar). I think that it would just as easy to transform their hair to silver (and much more effective).<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:39:00-08:00","id":1040992,"title":"","content":"Seems like it would be easier to simply use Matter 4/Prime 2 + 1 point of Quint to create a few pounds of nitro out of nothing around them. 3*(Pounds of Nitro) dice of damage and yards of blast radius.<br /> <br /> Though what sort of successes would be needed is up for debate/dependent on the chronicle.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:50:53-08:00","id":1040998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1040925#post1040925\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hair is also under Life while it is still attached to a character, so you would need a minimum of Life 3/Matter 3 for that sort of thing. And 100 grams of nitro would hardly do anything to a BSD.</div> </div> </div> </div>If your Paradigm is a mystical one, sure, hair is life while still attached.<br /> <br /> If you Paradigm is scientific however, hair and nails are matter, even if attached to a living being","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T17:53:28-08:00","id":1041000,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1040992#post1040992\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Seems like it would be easier to simply use Matter 4/Prime 2 + 1 point of Quint to create a few pounds of nitro out of nothing around them. 3*(Pounds of Nitro) dice of damage and yards of blast radius.<br /> <br /> Though what sort of successes would be needed is up for debate/dependent on the chronicle.</div> </div> </div> </div>Just make the same rules for success/damage. Each success on the effect makes enough explosive to deal 2 aggr damage per success. Plus 1, because it will be an explosion (forces). And don't forget you'll need a spark to ignite","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-30T18:08:49-08:00","id":1041011,"title":"","content":"Nitroglycerin just needs to be jostled slightly. It's RIDICULOUSLY explosive.<br /> <br /> And it has it's own rules. For every die of damage that explosives deal at the epicenter, the blast spreads outwards by one yard. Losing a die of damage for every yard. So. One pound of Nitro.<br /> <br /> Three Dice of damage at the epicenter. One yard out? Two dice. Two yards out? One dice. And after that, the blast dissipates.<br /> <br /> So, making each success enough for 2/3rds of a pound of nitro would, notably be a tad ridiculous.<br /> <br /> Though you can USE explosions as foci for forces effects. I was talking more about transmuting ACTUAL explosives.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T09:36:08-08:00","id":1041309,"title":"","content":"To create or transform explosive substances, you ought to apply Forces as well. It would be a bit strange if you need Forces to transform your pattern into a firebreathing something but not to transform the stone's pattern into a firespawning explosive.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T13:22:24-08:00","id":1041441,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041309#post1041309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To create or transform explosive substances, you ought to apply Forces as well. It would be a bit strange if you need Forces to transform your pattern into a firebreathing something but not to transform the stone's pattern into a firespawning explosive.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think you need Forces. Does dynamite only work with Mages with forces?<br /> <br /> Nitroglycerin is a mundane substance (it is part of the Consensus). It needs only matter to create.<br /> <br /> If things were like that, you would need Life to create any organic substance (like urine) which is not the case.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:10:58-08:00","id":1041473,"title":"","content":"Life is needed for living substances (fruit, nuts, yeast, etc). Urine is rarely living.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11683-aya-tari","name":"Aya Tari","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11683_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5986"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T14:41:13-08:00","id":1041487,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041473#post1041473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life is needed for living substances (fruit, nuts, yeast, etc). Urine is rarely living.</div> </div> </div> </div>And if it is, then you know you've got bigger problems <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://drive.google.com/uc?export=view&amp;id=0B9RzepSqCby3Mi1KUmJ5aWUwRVk\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/805-idpersona","name":"idpersona","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar805_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2117"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T17:20:59-08:00","id":1041577,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041309#post1041309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To create or transform explosive substances, you ought to apply Forces as well. It would be a bit strange if you need Forces to transform your pattern into a firebreathing something but not to transform the stone's pattern into a firespawning explosive.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but in that case you're creating fire from nothing. In this case, you're rendering the pattern unstable enough to detonate itself. Though radioactive materials come under Matter 5 explicitly IIRC. As matter which give off forces.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-01-31T19:14:42-08:00","id":1041634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041473#post1041473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life is needed for living substances (fruit, nuts, yeast, etc). Urine is rarely living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Among those, yeast is an actual organism (well, colony of them), so it'd be a no-brainer for requiring it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T07:59:05-08:00","id":1041831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karlgust</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041441#post1041441\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't think you need Forces. Does dynamite only work with Mages with forces?<br /> <br /> Nitroglycerin is a mundane substance (it is part of the Consensus). It needs only matter to create.<br /> <br /> If things were like that, you would need Life to create any organic substance (like urine) which is not the case.</div> </div> </div> </div>Following this logic (granted taken to the extreme) why should you need Forces to create fire? Since Fire is a mundane substance (part of the Consensus) it needs only Matter to create.<br /> <br /> When you start to mix PBD and RBD you get a mess. Either you need all the spheres for the Process (PBD rules that you need all spheres that are touched in your effect e.g. Mastery of several Spheres to conjure a taxi out of thin air). RBD rules that you need only the spheres for the Result (Correspondence 3 is enough for the taxi, since the result is you on another location).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> following your logic you could circumvent the need for Forces if you give yourself the ability to exhale highly flammable substances (Organic of course so that you need only Life 3)This gets ridiculous really fast if you think about it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:17:42-08:00","id":1041838,"title":"","content":"I don't see anything wrong with circumventing Spheres with the clever application of other Spheres. That's the kind of thinking that should be rewarded, and it's not like Matter or Life give you the same kind of control as Forces does.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Mage: The Ice-ension: An Epic Game of Reality on the Rink","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/758-ramnesis","name":"Ramnesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar758_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2220"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T08:30:46-08:00","id":1041841,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041831#post1041831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following this logic (granted taken to the extreme) why should you need Forces to create fire? Since Fire is a mundane substance (part of the Consensus) it needs only Matter to create.<br /> <br /> When you start to mix PBD and RBD you get a mess. Either you need all the spheres for the Process (PBD rules that you need all spheres that are touched in your effect e.g. Mastery of several Spheres to conjure a taxi out of thin air). RBD rules that you need only the spheres for the Result (Correspondence 3 is enough for the taxi, since the result is you on another location).<br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42\" style=\"background-image:url('data:image/svg+xml;base64,');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"11744\" data-vbnamecard=\"11744\">Enginseer-42</a> following your logic you could circumvent the need for Forces if you give yourself the ability to exhale highly flammable substances (Organic of course so that you need only Life 3)This gets ridiculous really fast if you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Until someone shoots you with a dragonsbreath round and you explode because you have sacs of highly flammable substances in your body.<br /> <br /> There are advantages and disadvantages to such things. The advantage to it is that you don't require forces to perform a 'forces' effect. The disadvantages are, aside from the lack of the default forces + 1 to damage, that your technique has to largely follow the rule of science. How much flammable liquid can you fit in a human body without looking like a boomer from left 4 dead? What happens when you're caught in a fire yourself? Unless you make yourself fire-proof it's going to cause you harm just as much as the target as you spray crude oil out of your throat and then ignite it. Added onto it, you have to deal with the fact that your creation will work largely based upon how the present consensus says it would work. If you're spewing highly flammable liquids out of your tear-ducts and then igniting them, that's going to have less leeway than a mage who just casts fireball.<br /> <br /> Same with conjuring up C-4. C-4 will do what C-4 does and unless you have forces you cannot ALTER that.<br /> <br /> Also, Fire isn't a substance. It's how we perceive the energy, or forces, given off by exothermic reactions","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:30:16-08:00","id":1042153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Nonsense</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041831#post1041831\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Following this logic (granted taken to the extreme) why should you need Forces to create fire? Since Fire is a mundane substance (part of the Consensus) it needs only Matter to create.<br /> <br /> When you start to mix PBD and RBD you get a mess. Either you need all the spheres for the Process (PBD rules that you need all spheres that are touched in your effect e.g. Mastery of several Spheres to conjure a taxi out of thin air). RBD rules that you need only the spheres for the Result (Correspondence 3 is enough for the taxi, since the result is you on another location).<br /> <br /> <span class=\"b-bbcode-user js-bbcode-user\">Guest</span> following your logic you could circumvent the need for Forces if you give yourself the ability to exhale highly flammable substances (Organic of course so that you need only Life 3)This gets ridiculous really fast if you think about it.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;Fire&quot; is not matter. Fire is plasma, it's energy in the pattern of light and heat. There are many flammable substances that ignite with oxigen, but they aren't <i>energy</i>. And those substances need an initial imput of energy to ignite (in the case of nitroglycerin, it needs a very tiny initial &quot;push&quot; because it is too reactive, so it can ignite with a little movement. Other substances need more - wood will need a lot of heat before get on fire). In the case o nitroglycerin, there is no manipulation of Forces (energy) AT ALL.<br /> <br /> But fire is ENERGY. You can use matter to suck the O2 away and end it, or use also matter to make MORE O2, thus &quot;controlling&quot; the fire, but you can't turn it into light or make a Ball of fire float around with Forces","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T18:37:20-08:00","id":1042154,"title":"","content":"Besides, whats wrong with that? Is it about game balance?<br /> <br /> Well, it's not unbalanced. Because you could just turn the air around your target in l acid. You can turn the floor bellow him turn into mud, and than turn it back into a solid state. With life, you can just give the bad eye to someone and make 'em take damage.<br /> <br /> Its not unbalanced, and RAW, it is alright","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-01T19:58:28-08:00","id":1042190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Aya Tari</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1041473#post1041473\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Life is needed for living substances (fruit, nuts, yeast, etc). Urine is rarely living.</div> </div> </div> </div>Depending upon version and sourcebook, this is not strictly the case and largely depends upon paradigm, and the nature of the Pattern. The primary hard-and-fast rule is the Pattern in question has to be irrevocably inert; Life magic <i>can</i> and <i>does</i> (depending upon paradigm) govern &quot;dead&quot; organisms, or constituent parts of that organism, that retain enough viability to sustain or propagate <i>other</i> Life patterns.<br /> <br /> That biology as a properly-defined modern natural science is a newcomer compared to physics and chemistry,massively complicates matters. Yes, the <i>Consensus</i> holds the existence of microorganisms, biotic processes, evolution, and the like, but individual Paradigms <i>don't</i> and mages tend to be all over the place when it comes to Life, compared to Forces or Matter as the other two Pattern spheres.<br /> <br /> For example, you can use Life magic to preserve, say, a pound of fresh meat. The animal that pound of meat came from is most likely dead, so that particular Life pattern is gone. It doesn't matter precisely <i>what</i> Effect the mage uses to preserve the meat, what matters is they <i>can</i>. So, strictly speaking, as a constituent part of an organism that retains enough viability to sustain or propagate Life patterns, you could technically use Life magic to make (fresh) urine. Humans can survive (in the short term) drinking urine for wont of potable water, and fresh urine due to its urea content is excellent plant fertilizer. Cold, stale piss would obviously be a Matter pattern, however (which bears out, considering urea naturally decays into ammonia).<br /> <br /> Don't ask me why in God's name a mage would want to use Life magic to make pee-pee. Maybe an Ecstatic with a golden shower fetish would want to do it, I dunno. Or maybe a Tradition mage a bit lacking in the wits and intelligence department, caught in a survival situation and didn't catch onto the notion the same Life magic they're using to Bear Grylls that motherfucker could be just as easily used to purify ambient water.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":431,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","user":"Theodrim","date":". 02-01-2017, 11:08 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/431-theodrim","name":"Theodrim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar431_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1841"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:29:57-08:00","id":1042504,"title":"","content":"Maybe the Mage prefer to turn his poo into pee-pee... It's cleaner...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12880-karlgust","name":"Karlgust","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"614"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-02T10:37:21-08:00","id":1042506,"title":"","content":"No Matter, no Forces and a fire that needs to be put out.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"815"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-04T20:50:09-08:00","id":1043843,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Theodrim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1042190#post1042190\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, strictly speaking, as a constituent part of an organism that retains enough viability to sustain or propagate Life patterns, you could technically use Life magic to make (fresh) urine.</div> </div> </div> </div>Life 2, in fact. Making the body do something it already tends to is pretty easy. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6072-quantumboost","name":"Quantumboost","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6072_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"590"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-05T00:19:41-08:00","id":1043880,"title":"","content":"Life 3/Prime 2 for vulgar quantities and pressure.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>So, this Zen Master walks up to a hot dog stand and says: &quot;Make me one with everything!&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12022-nonsense","name":"Nonsense","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12022_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join