=\"_blank\"> </a> </div> <div class=\"url ellipsis\"> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7DCz1SgByDM\" target=\"_blank\"> https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=7DCz1SgByDM </a> </div> <div class=\"meta\"> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Rare footage of a Hermetic invisibility ritual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T14:22:28-07:00","id":1229229,"title":"","content":"Something I forgot to mention about Freak Legion's &quot;creative&quot; genitalia Power. The damage being unsoakable is just thrown out there, with no caveat.<br /> <br /> RAW, in the WoD, the vaginas and penises of Fomori can, in some cases, inflict damage which will even harm Methesulahs with Fortitude 9. After all, they can't soak the damage. I doubt there are many tables where &quot;okay we just need to find a bane-infested human who can, well, dickslap this ancient vampire to death&quot; will fly, for mechanical and ethical reasons (if not because of poor taste), but the mere fact that it's possible on paper is something I find hilarious.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-21T16:33:32-07:00","id":1229256,"title":"","content":"I thought it was only unsoakable if you had put yourself in a.... delicate position with them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11744-enginseer-42","name":"Enginseer-42","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"774"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-06-22T11:50:24-07:00","id":1229416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Enginseer-42</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1035738-mages-are-nothing-but-prey-to-other-supernaturals?p=1229256#post1229256\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I thought it was only unsoakable if you had put yourself in a.... delicate position with them?</div> </div> </div> </div>The text does heavily imply that, yes. 90s Werewolf games were wild by the looks of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11620-twig","name":"twig","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11620_5.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4568"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-04-27T12:13:09-07:00","id":1308362,"title":"","content":"I haven't followed this whole thread but a mage's strongest moves are A) learn the lay of the land, and B) get potential threats to fight each other.<br /> <br /> Example: a Sabbat pack wants to take over a nightclub diatrict were satyr allies of the mage cabal (Hermetics and intellectually inclined C of X) have a freehold. The NWO is snooping in the area too. And the local Bonegnawers, allies of the Satyrs, are being bullied by Shadow Lords that want the Bonegnawer caern.<br /> <br /> Answer: use conjunctive effects of Time and Entropy to have the Sabbat, the NWO, and the Shadow Lords constantly run into each other. Direct the rituals against the Sabbat because they are the least able to detect and counter the effect. And presto! At least two of your problems go away. Bonus, the third problem is softened up for later.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":857,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","user":"Astromancer","date":". 04-27-2019, 08:00 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/857-astromancer","name":"Astromancer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar857_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2195"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T07:40:19-07:00","id":1312290,"title":"","content":"Mages and sorcerers/linear mages are both still mortal and frail unless they use magic. They are in someway &quot;prey&quot;, but they are no mewling kittens. If they are given time to prepare, they can be very formidable and deadly opponents. And a mage with high Arete would be capable of doing things even on the spot depending on their spheres and the number of dots they have in each.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24121-starcomet","name":"Starcomet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24121_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"96"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T08:01:02-07:00","id":1312292,"title":"","content":"Calling mages &quot;mortal without their magic&quot; doesn't mean much from this practical standpoint either. Other night folk have an advantage in this sense, but mostly it stems from having ready and easy access to advantages inherent to their form.<br /> <br /> A mage can be set up such that, in a similar fashion, he simply won't be defenseless in an ambush. It might take active effort in having these powers up, but most mages prone to do so already integrate these into their lifestyles.<br /> Most mages that can truly be caught unprepared are those that wouldn't prepare anyway. Probably a more common occurrence than with other night folk since their lives are closer to humanity's, and humanity has never been this peaceful.<br /> <br /> So yes, a bellicose mage is little more than a mortal without his magick. <i>Don't count on that</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse/visitormessage/1408635-visitor-message-from-synapse#post1408635\" target=\"_blank\">Check my Exalted homebrew</a>!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/32-synapse","name":"Synapse","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar32_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1507"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-05-15T09:07:37-07:00","id":1312306,"title":"","content":"I guess that it isn't dead the thread that can forever lie<br /> <br /> ...<br /> <br /> Ask Ravnos if he thinks mages are nothing but prey now...Really, this whole opinion surged from a particular reading that:<br /> <br /> a)It's a very personal take on how the rules are &quot;lived&quot; by the IOC characters...ST discretion, making mages to be unprepared more often than not. And that would depend on how dangerous it's mage society at the moment (that is, if the Technocracy heeds the pogrom fans or not)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Synapse</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Most mages that can truly be caught unprepared are those that wouldn't prepare anyway. Probably a more common occurrence than with other night folk since their lives are closer to humanity's, and humanity has never been this peaceful.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody lives closer to humanity than Hunters, and they're the most prepared of all. Mages being peaceful or not it's more a function of what mages <i>do </i>than anything else.<br /> <br /> If the ST want's mage society to do charity and procelitize, and the Technocracy it's almost never hostile - as it happens during the general apathy of Revised - then yeah they won't be prepared for the 1 in 100.000 vampire being hungry unless the mage lives in a war zone...but if ST says mage society it's fraugth with power struggles and Technocracy will kick your door sonner rather han latter (or that the Traditions are going to blow up the lab sooner rather than latter) - like it was the case on 2e - then most are going to be, at least, ready to protect themselves against other mages and their constructs/supernaturaly equiped minions/etc. M20 it's metaplot agnostic enough as to refuse to clearly define the current state of the Ascencion War, so this it's mostly ST conceit.<br /> <br /> b)Doesn't take in count what other supernaturals think about mages or about prey at all:<br /> <br /> All cores talk about how mages can be very dangerous, none suggests to <i>prey </i>on them. This is, supposedly, the stereotipical view on mages that supernaturals have.","signature":"","edited"